    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CLAS's decarbonization strategy, as articulated in the refreshed 2023 CLI 2030 Sustainability Master Plan (SMP), is built on a science-based approach validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) and aligned with a 1.5°C climate scenario. The strategy centers on reducing Scope 1 and 2 emissions through a structured Carbon Mitigation Hierarchy that prioritizes avoidance, reduction, replacement, and compensation. Key focus areas include low-carbon transition with specific targets to reduce absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 46% by 2030 from a 2019 baseline, reduce carbon emissions intensity by 72%, and achieve 45% of electricity consumption from renewable sources. The company also aims to have 50% of its portfolio achieve minimum green ratings by 2025 and 100% by 2030, demonstrating a comprehensive approach to decarbonizing its real estate portfolio.\n\nTo implement this strategy, CLAS employs a multi-faceted approach across its operations. The company is implementing energy efficiency measures through low consumption design and high energy efficiency standards, while deploying smart building analytics and on-site renewable energy solutions. CLAS has established a comprehensive green lease program targeting 100% implementation across its properties by 2030, working with tenants to encourage adoption of green practices. The company conducts climate scenario analysis to assess potential impacts on its portfolio and actively monitors transition risks through its Environment, Health and Safety Management System (EHSMS). Additionally, CLAS is pursuing green building certification for its properties and engaging suppliers on climate-related requirements to address Scope 3 emissions.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a robust governance framework with oversight from the Board and executive leadership. CLAS aligns its climate-related disclosures with TCFD recommendations and ensures transparency through regular reporting. The company validates its carbon emissions targets through SBTi and has maintained external assurance for its Scope 1 and 2 emissions since FY 2010. CLAS also monitors country-specific regulatory developments globally, adapting its strategy to respond to evolving climate policies in key markets including Singapore, Australia, the UK, and Europe. Through these integrated efforts, the company is working toward its 2050 net zero commitment while addressing both physical and transition climate risks.",
      "notes": "Comprehensive multi-page strategy section found across sustainability report. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) and includes plans for Scope 3. Contains specific targets, implementation approaches, and supporting governance mechanisms. Strategy is science-based with SBTi validation and aligns with 1.5°C scenario. Includes detailed carbon mitigation hierarchy showing prioritization of decarbonization approaches.",
      "status": null
    },
