    "strategy": {
      "summary": "AIA's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based approach validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), with the company becoming the first pan-Asian life and health insurer to achieve this validation for both operations and investments. The cornerstone of their strategy is the comprehensive Climate Transition Plan (CTP) published in November 2023, which outlines a clear roadmap to achieving net-zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050. This plan integrates climate considerations into governance, risk management, and operations across the organization, with specific near-term targets including a -46.2% reduction of Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2030, and sector-specific targets for power generation (-49.3% per MWh) and real estate (-58.5% per sqm) portfolios. The strategy is grounded in the company's commitment to validate all near-term emissions reduction targets through SBTi, establishing accountability and science-aligned methodologies for their decarbonization journey.\n\nTo implement this strategy, AIA has launched several concrete initiatives. The company completed validation of its operational emissions reduction targets by SBTi, marking the culmination of two years of cross-functional work across the Group Office and business units. They have begun developing decarbonization roadmaps across all 17 in-scope business units, with operational teams preparing local implementation plans. AIA Indonesia pioneered the 'One Policy One Tree' initiative, planting 30,000 trees across five provinces to absorb approximately 2,000 tonnes of CO₂e. The company also achieved significant digital transformation milestones with 94% of digital submissions for buy, service, and claims transactions, reducing paper usage, and 91% electronic submissions for claims. Additionally, 100% of new buildings and redevelopments are required to be green certified, while 24,108 employees completed the ESG 101 e-learning program to build internal climate capabilities.\n\nAIA's decarbonization strategy is supported by strategic partnerships and external engagement. The company participated actively at COP28, hosting panel discussions on climate resilience and announcing their Climate Transition Plan alongside SBTi CEO Luiz Amaral. They serve as a launch partner in Cathay Pacific's Sustainable Aviation Fuel program and are members of the Joint Committee on Climate Change (JC3) in Malaysia. AIA contributed to the SBTi Financial Net-Zero Expert Advisory Group and engaged with regulators through initiatives like the Green Finance Industry Taskforce in Singapore. The company has also established a Climate Action Task Force to guide implementation, while integrating climate considerations into governance through regular engagement with agents, investors, and customers across the Asia-Pacific region.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across images 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8. Strategy details comprehensive near-term targets validated by SBTi with specific implementation timelines. The Climate Transition Plan serves as the central strategic document with detailed sector-specific targets. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) and investment portfolio decarbonization (Scope 3). Implementation details include concrete programs like One Policy One Tree initiative and ESG 101 training program.",
      "status": null
    },
