      "summary": "CEREIT's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on a structured approach to achieve net-zero operational carbon emissions by 2040, with specific focus on energy efficiency, emissions reduction, and data-driven decision making. The company developed the initial steps of its Net Zero Strategy in 2023, establishing targets for Scope 1 and 2 operational carbon emissions intensity reduction for its core portfolio. This strategy is supported by a comprehensive ESG CAPEX program with a €8.2 million budget (€6.6 million completed by year-end), implementing tangible measures including LED lighting installations, BMS upgrades, smart building technology, waste sorting units, and water leak detection devices across the portfolio. The company also expanded its green lease program, with 30% of lease agreements incorporating environmental clauses requiring tenant-customers to share utility consumption data and collaborate on sustainability initiatives, representing a 6.5 percentage point increase from 2022.\n\nTo support these initiatives, CEREIT implemented a robust data collection and monitoring framework, connecting 100% of its assets to the Deepki platform for comprehensive utility bill, GHG emissions, energy usage, water consumption, and waste management data. The company conducted energy audits for 88% of its portfolio, with results directly feeding into annual capex planning aligned with its Net Zero Strategy. CEREIT also developed climate scenarios aligned with a 1.5°C warming scenario and utilized the Carbon Risk Real Estate Monitor (CRREM) tool to assess transition risks across its European assets. The company further enhanced its climate risk management by integrating climate risks into its enterprise risk management framework and establishing internal audit procedures specifically for climate-related information and processes.",
