    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Del Monte Pacific's decarbonization strategy is built on a science-based approach with a clear net zero target by 2050, supported by concrete actions across their operations and value chain. The company has registered with the Science Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) to align their emissions reduction goals with net zero standards, demonstrating a commitment to measurable, science-aligned targets. They've expanded their GHG emissions reporting to include Scope 3 emissions from toll packers, top suppliers, transportation, and logistics service providers, reflecting a comprehensive approach to emissions accounting. The company has already achieved a 6% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions from FY21 to FY22 and is targeting a 3% annual reduction in cannery emissions, which they've successfully met for the current year with emissions reduced to 122,286 MTCO2eq.\n\nTo implement this strategy, Del Monte Pacific is executing multiple specific initiatives across their operations. They are installing solar power systems at their cannery (with completion targeted for December 2023) and plantation (by end of FY24), directly reducing reliance on fossil fuels. In transportation, they're shifting 35% of third-party delivery transportation to double-decker trucks by FY24, installing GPS devices on 100% of third-party delivery transportation to optimize routes, and transitioning transport units to electric vehicles (EV) or plug-in hybrid electric vehicles (PHEV). They're also improving truckload efficiency to 7.5 miles per gallon and reducing empty miles driven in the supply chain by 20%, while increasing cover cropping by 5% per year to enhance carbon sequestration in agricultural operations.\n\nThe company is taking a holistic value chain approach, working with suppliers, third-party manufacturers, and customers to develop a glide path to net zero emissions. Their climate-related report outlines how they're adapting to climate change impacts on operations, such as water stress and extreme weather events, and adjusting mitigation strategies accordingly. Governance frameworks support these efforts, with alignment to standards from the Singapore Exchange Securities Trading Limited (SGX-ST) and the Philippine Stock Exchange. Del Monte Pacific is also conducting GHG inventory gap analysis and training key employees on climate change to ensure organizational capacity for ongoing decarbonization progress.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with specific decarbonization initiatives across operations and value chain. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) and supply chain emissions (Scope 3). Concrete implementation details provided including specific timelines, percentages, and technologies. Value chain engagement is a key component of their approach.",
      "status": null
    },
