      "summary": "Flex's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a multi-faceted approach targeting both operational emissions and value chain impacts. The company has committed to reducing absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 50% by 2030 from a 2019 baseline and reaching net zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2040. Their operational strategy focuses on three key pillars: reducing energy consumption needs, leveraging system efficiency as a mitigation tactic, and increasing the percentage of renewable energy resources in their energy portfolio. In 2022, they achieved a 27% decrease in Scope 1 and 2 emissions from their baseline and had 98.51 MW of renewable energy, representing a 145% year-over-year increase, with specific projects like the 580-kilowatt solar installation at their Pamplona, Spain site demonstrating tangible implementation.\n\nThe company is actively engaging its supply chain to drive decarbonization, with a goal to have 50% of preferred suppliers set GHG emissions targets by 2025 and 100% by 2030. As of 2022, they had achieved 69% progress toward their 2025 supplier target goal, with 35% of preferred suppliers having GHG reduction targets. Flex's Supplier Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Program, which won the Sustainability Initiative of the Year from the Business Intelligence Group in 2022, supports this effort through supplier assessments, one-on-one meetings, and training on setting science-based targets. Additionally, they are working with customers to ensure 70% have science-based targets by 2025, with 64% of specified customers achieving this in 2022.\n\nTo support these initiatives, Flex is implementing specific operational measures including zero-waste certification (9% of sites certified in 2022 toward a 50% target by 2025), water reduction efforts (6% reduction in water-scarce areas in 2022 toward a 5% target by 2025), and expanding renewable energy integration across their facilities. The company is also leveraging frameworks like TCFD and CDP to share knowledge and best practices, while maintaining strong governance standards that have earned them recognition as industry leaders in sustainability performance.",
