      "summary": "Gallant Venture Ltd.'s decarbonization approach is integrated within its climate risk management framework, following TCFD recommendations to identify and address climate-related risks and opportunities. The company has completed a formal qualitative scenario analysis to evaluate climate impacts across short, medium, and long-term horizons, with specific attention to scenarios aligned with a 2°C or lower warming pathway. This analysis has been pivotal in guiding their strategic decision-making process, helping develop business response plans that enhance resilience to climate change impacts and prepare for potential exposures from the changing business and environmental landscape.\n\nA concrete decarbonization initiative highlighted in the report is the implementation of solar photovoltaic systems across their industrial parks. The company has installed a 7.4 MWp solar PV system on the factory rooftop of Batamindo Industrial Park, which is expected to generate approximately 8.8 million kWh annually. This system, scheduled for completion in 3Q 2024, represents the first phase of a broader program to deploy solar PV systems across multiple operating locations over the coming years. These installations are specifically designed to provide green energy to tenants of their industrial parks as part of their transition to renewable energy sources.\n\nThe company has established a dedicated governance structure to oversee sustainability performance, with the Board, Sustainability Reporting Committee (chaired by the Chief Financial Officer), and management team all involved in climate-related risk assessment and management. Management actively champions sustainability initiatives and develops risk management processes for sustainability-related projects, ensuring that climate considerations are integrated into business operations and strategic planning. The Chief Financial Officer chairs the Sustainability Reporting Committee, which oversees the Group's sustainability performance by evaluating material ESG topics and providing progress updates to the Board.",
