      "summary": "GSS Energy Limited’s decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a structured climate change transition plan targeting a 10% reduction in absolute Scope 2 GHG emissions by FY2035, with FY2022 as the baseline. The strategy is driven by three strategic levers: reduce, produce, and neutralise, which collectively address emissions across operations, energy generation, and residual impacts. The 'Reduce' lever focuses on cutting emissions within operations and the supply chain through systematic machinery maintenance, high-efficiency lighting, behavioral changes (e.g., staff training on energy-saving practices), and transitioning to low- or zero-carbon energy sources. The 'Produce' lever emphasizes on-site renewable energy generation, exemplified by the installation of solar panels on the rooftop of its China subsidiary CGP’s factory in June 2022, which aims to lower future GHG emissions. The 'Neutralise' lever plans to offset unavoidable residual emissions using renewable energy certificates (REC) and carbon credits once relevant markets mature. Additionally, the company expanded into the EV sector, launching the UNO-X electric motorcycle in November 2023 via a partnership with Iso, which consumes only 17% of the energy used by internal combustion engine (ICE) motorcycles, aligning with global transportation decarbonization trends.",
