    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Kerry Properties Limited's decarbonization strategy for 2023 is structured around a comprehensive Carbon Neutrality Roadmap with science-based targets aligned with their Sustainability Vision 2030 and net-zero by 2050. The company has established specific, measurable targets across three timeframes: short-term (2025) targets include 25% reduction in GHG intensity and 20% reduction in energy intensity, with free carbon audits for 50% of their properties; medium-term (2030) targets focus on achieving all near-term science-based targets with free carbon audits for 75% of properties; and long-term (2050) target is achieving carbon neutrality across operations and supply chain. These targets were validated through the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), with the company having already submitted targets for validation in 2023.\n\nThe company is implementing this strategy through concrete initiatives including becoming the first in Asia to obtain LEED Zero Carbon & Waste certifications for their Jing An Kerry Centre in Shanghai, designing and building energy-efficient properties with green certifications, and retrofitting existing buildings for energy savings. They are increasing renewable energy procurement and developing green partnerships with tenants, including free carbon audit programs and green leasing options. Technology integration is central to their approach, with the adoption of Building Information Modelling during construction and Internet of Things in operational properties to optimize energy management and building systems. The company also conducts climate risk and vulnerability assessments (CRVA) and has rolled out Climate Checklists for Mitigation Measures across all sites.\n\nTo support implementation, Kerry Properties has established a comprehensive governance structure with the Sustainability Steering Committee overseeing strategy execution. The company actively engages stakeholders through employee awareness programs like Climate Fresk Workshops and the 4-Colour Biz-Green Outfit Social Challenge, while collaborating with value chain partners on decarbonization initiatives. Notably, their 2023 progress already exceeds their 2025 targets, with 32.7% GHG intensity reduction and 24.7% energy saving achieved against baseline year 2017. The company also emphasizes value chain emissions reduction through engagement with tenants, construction materials suppliers, and other stakeholders across the property development lifecycle.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with detailed roadmap and specific initiatives. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) and value chain emissions (Scope 3). Contains specific targets with measurable progress data. Includes concrete implementation mechanisms and governance structure. Shows 2023 progress already exceeding 2025 targets.",
      "status": null
    },
