      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy is structured around integrating climate risk management into its operational framework, guided by the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) recommendations. It focuses on governance, risk assessment, and transparency to address climate-related risks and opportunities while minimizing environmental impact. The Board oversees the formulation of climate strategy and disclosure of climate-related risks and opportunities, ensuring alignment with sustainability goals, while Management implements mitigation and adaptation measures to embed these principles into daily operations. This approach acknowledges the Group’s minimal direct environmental footprint but emphasizes proactive risk management to support long-term business continuity.\n\nSpecific initiatives include group-wide energy conservation practices, recycling initiatives, and flexible working arrangements, which form part of risk treatment plans developed under the Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) framework. These actions aim to reduce energy consumption and associated emissions, particularly within Scope 2 (indirect) emissions from electricity use in rented offices. The company also actively monitors evolving regulatory trends in the low-carbon transition to anticipate compliance requirements, mitigate transition risks, and adapt operations proactively. Additionally, the Group is committed to enhancing climate-related disclosures in line with TCFD, aiming to provide comprehensive evaluations of climate change’s financial impacts in future sustainability reports to build stakeholder trust and inform strategic decision-making.",
