    "strategy": {
      "summary": "OUE REIT's decarbonization strategy for 2023 is structured around its 'Stewarding the Environment' pillar, with a comprehensive approach targeting both operational efficiency and systemic change. The company has established specific, measurable targets including reducing commercial segment energy intensity by 25% and Scope 2 GHG emissions intensity by 25% by FY 2030. To achieve these goals, OUE REIT is implementing a multi-faceted approach that includes energy-efficient infrastructure upgrades across its portfolio. Specific initiatives include progressive replacement of T5 lighting with LED lighting at properties like OUE Bayfront and Lippo Plaza, installation of automated metering systems, and optimization of HVAC operations through smart energy solutions. The company has also upgraded building management systems at key properties, such as implementing the L-QUBE, DEOS System at Crowne Plaza Changi Airport, which provides integrated building automation and energy management capabilities. Additionally, OUE REIT is expanding renewable energy generation through solar panel installations at One Raffles Place Tower 2, with plans for further expansion in FY 2024. A critical component of their strategy is tenant engagement, with green leases accounting for approximately 50.3% of Singapore's commercial segment net lettable area as of December 2023. The company has developed a Green Guide for Tenants outlining energy and water management recommendations and conducts regular discussions with tenants to set annual reduction targets. Supporting these operational initiatives, OUE REIT has strengthened its governance framework by aligning with IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures and conducting TCFD climate scenario analyses. The Manager tables climate-related risks as agenda items during Board meetings and has developed an ESG Investment Due Diligence Checklist to ensure climate considerations are integrated into new acquisitions. While progress has been made with commercial segment energy intensity reduced by 20.9% (against the 25% target by FY 2030), the company acknowledges challenges as evidenced by a 17.8% increase in hospitality segment energy intensity, demonstrating the ongoing need for targeted interventions across different property types.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 79-85 and 111-112. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 and 2) with limited specific details on Scope 3. Contains concrete initiatives with implementation status and performance metrics. Strategy aligns with TCFD framework and IFRS S2 standards. FY 2023 performance data shows mixed progress against targets.",
      "status": null
    },
