      "summary": "ART's decarbonization strategy for 2021 is anchored in CapitaLand's 2030 Sustainability Master Plan and aligned with Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) validation, focusing on integrating climate action across the real estate lifecycle. The strategy emphasizes transitioning to a low-carbon business model through operational efficiency, renewable energy adoption, and embedding sustainability in asset design and management. Key focus areas include reducing carbon emissions intensity, enhancing portfolio resilience, and aligning with global climate science frameworks such as the 1.5°C scenario. \n\nSpecific initiatives driving decarbonization in 2021 include mandatory Environmental, Health, and Safety (EHS) Impact Assessments for all new investments and development projects to identify climate-related risks and opportunities, with findings incorporated into investment approvals. The company implemented Sustainable Building Guidelines (SBG) to enforce energy efficiency standards, green rating targets, and onsite renewable energy adoption where feasible. By 2021, ART achieved a 40% reduction in carbon emissions intensity (from the 2008 baseline) and certified 35% of its global portfolio under green building standards, reflecting progress toward its 2030 targets. Additionally, carbon emissions reduction metrics were integrated into executive compensation through the Performance Share Plan Awards, incentivizing leadership accountability. \n\nSupporting these efforts, ART leveraged TCFD-aligned climate scenario analysis to assess physical and transition risks, while maintaining third-party certified ISO 14001 Environmental Management Systems to monitor and mitigate operational emissions. The company also disclosed Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions data in its Global Sustainability Report, aligning with international standards to ensure transparency and accountability. These structured mechanisms—combined with SBTi-validated targets and a focus on renewable energy integration—form a cohesive approach to decarbonization across ART's portfolio.",
