    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Ascendas Reit's 2021 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based approach aligned with the Paris Agreement, implementing concrete initiatives across its real estate portfolio. The company has secured SBTi-approved carbon emissions reduction targets for a 'well-below 2°C' scenario, with its strategy spanning the entire real estate life cycle from investment to redevelopment. Key focus areas include renewable energy adoption, sustainable building operations, and climate risk management, with specific energy use and carbon reduction targets established for operational assets alongside green certification targets. The strategy is anchored by Capitaland's 2030 Sustainability Master Plan, which explicitly outlines pathways for transition to a low-carbon business aligned with climate science.\n\nThe company is executing several specific decarbonization initiatives, including the completion of solar installations at 37A Tampines Street 92 in FY2021, with further solar projects planned to expand its renewable energy capacity. Four properties in Singapore and four co-location data centers in the UK/Europe are already fully powered by renewable energy. Ascendas Reit has increased its exposure to green-certified assets through acquisitions of Galaxis in Singapore and 1-5 Thomas Holt Drive in Australia, as well as the development of the Grab Headquarters in Singapore. The company has also launched the Capitaland Sustainability X Challenge (CSXC), an innovation program sourcing global sustainability technologies for the built environment. All new investments undergo EHS Impact Assessment during due diligence to identify environmental risks and opportunities related to climate change.\n\nTo support its decarbonization efforts, Ascendas Reit has established robust financial and governance mechanisms. The company has approximately S$1.2 billion worth of green financing instruments (green bonds, green loans, and green perpetual securities) as of December 2021, and targets securing $6 billion through sustainable finance by 2030. Implementation of the Capitalland Sustainable Building Guidelines (SBG) identifies climate change risks from the design stage, while the Environment, Health and Safety Management System (EHSMS) - certified to ISO 14001 standard - monitors transition risks and operational issues related to climate change. The company also conducts annual portfolio reviews to identify assets suitable for redevelopment with sustainability features, ensuring continuous improvement in its decarbonization approach.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across all documents. Strategy focuses on both operational and portfolio-level decarbonization with specific initiatives and measurable targets. Implementation details include renewable energy projects, green financing instruments, and science-based targets. The strategy is integrated with Capitaland's broader sustainability framework.",
      "status": null
    },
