    "strategy": {
      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy for 2021 centers on integrating climate-related financial considerations into its investment processes and leveraging investment opportunities in the low-carbon economy. Through its Responsible Investing (RI) Policy and dedicated Climate Change Policy, the company systematically assesses climate risks and opportunities across all asset classes, focusing on greenhouse gas emission reductions (mitigation) and climate change adaptation. This approach is embedded in governance structures, with the Board overseeing implementation and the Executive Directors ensuring alignment with climate-related objectives. The strategy prioritizes identifying material climate-related risks and opportunities at every stage of the investment process, from screening to eventual exit, while aligning with TCFD recommendations and sector-specific considerations like pharmaceuticals, water, and waste.\\n\\nIn 2021, the company executed concrete initiatives to advance decarbonization. It introduced prohibitions on direct investments in companies generating majority revenue from coal, oil, and gas exploration, extraction, production, or transportation. New investment strategies, such as the Europe Fund VIII (which requires portfolio companies to improve energy efficiency and reduce greenhouse gas emissions) and the ICG-Real Estate Debt Fund VI (operating under a green loan framework), were launched to channel capital toward climate-resilient opportunities. The company also joined Initiative Climat International (iCI) to actively engage portfolio companies globally in reducing carbon emissions intensity and securing sustainable investment performance. Additionally, it conducted transition-risk screening across 10 key investment strategies (covering 90% of AUM) and implemented the Climate Risk Assessment Tool to evaluate climate-related financial risks and opportunities using business-as-usual and 2°C scenarios.\\n\\nSupporting these efforts, the company set a target to reduce Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 80% by 2030, reports emissions per the GHG Protocol, and participates in iCI working groups to develop standardized tools for measuring private equity emissions. These mechanisms ensure alignment with science-based targets and enhance transparency in tracking decarbonization progress across the investment portfolio.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found; strategy focuses on investment processes and portfolio company engagement, with specific targets, prohibitions, and partnerships. Implementation details include transition-risk screening, green loan frameworks, and emissions reduction targets.",
      "status": null
    },
