    "strategy": {
      "summary": "LMIR Trust's 2021 decarbonization strategy centers on operational energy efficiency improvements and enhanced climate risk management, with a primary focus on reducing Scope 2 emissions which constitute approximately 97% of its total GHG emissions. The company recognizes electricity consumption for lighting, air conditioning, lifts, and escalators as its main emissions source and has implemented targeted energy-saving measures across its portfolio. The strategy integrates TCFD (Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures) principles to systematically identify and manage climate risks while improving transparency in climate-related reporting. LMIR Trust acknowledges the critical importance of addressing climate-related financial risks to strengthen risk management and strategic planning, with energy efficiency serving as the cornerstone of its emissions reduction approach.\n\nThe company executed several concrete energy efficiency initiatives in 2021, including the replacement of existing corridor lights with LED lighting at Sun Plaza and the conversion of TL lights in Lippo Mall Puri's parking area to LED, achieving up to 70% improvement in energy and cost efficiency. Additionally, the switch to inverter-based chiller pumps resulted in a 14% decrease in electricity consumption. LMIR Trust also conducted energy audits of chillers to ensure operational efficiency and is working with an external consultant to perform pre-assessments for Green Mark Certification for Lippo Mall Puri and Sun Plaza. These initiatives directly address the significant increase in electricity consumption (21.2% year-over-year) that occurred due to mall acquisitions and post-pandemic reopenings, while simultaneously working to reduce energy intensity metrics.\n\nTo support its decarbonization efforts, LMIR Trust established robust governance structures with Board-level oversight of climate-related risks and opportunities. The Board underwent specialized training on climate risk management conducted by an external consultant and committed to regular updates on climate-related issues. The Sustainability Committee provides strategic direction for managing sustainability risks, with the CEO and Senior Asset Director specifically assigned to initiate and monitor climate footprint programs. The company is also developing its Scope 3 carbon inventory for future disclosure and has begun identifying climate-related risks and opportunities through stakeholder engagement, recognizing energy and GHG emissions as material topics requiring strategic attention.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found focusing primarily on operational emissions (Scope 2). Strategy includes specific implementation details with quantifiable results from 2021 initiatives. Strong emphasis on energy efficiency as primary decarbonization approach with concrete examples of LED lighting and chiller improvements. TCFD framework integration and Board-level governance structure are key supporting mechanisms. Document provides context on emissions composition (97% Scope 2) and explains consumption increases due to business growth factors.",
      "status": null
    },
