    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Lonza’s decarbonization strategy for 2021 focuses on achieving net-zero GHG emissions by 2050 through a structured approach targeting operational (Scope 1 and 2) and value chain (Scope 3) emissions. The company prioritizes concrete actions aligned with global and site-specific roadmaps, emphasizing renewable energy adoption, supply chain collaboration, and operational efficiency. These efforts are embedded within broader sustainability goals, including the 2030 waste intensity reduction target and SDG 13 (Climate Action) commitments.\n\nKey initiatives include launching a global project to source 100% renewable electricity by 2025, directly addressing Scope 2 emissions. For Scope 3, Lonza engaged top suppliers to reduce their carbon footprint, building on a 2020 program to identify value chain emission sources. Site-level actions demonstrated immediate impact: in Visp (CH), pretreating wastewater avoided over 900 tons CO₂-eq in 2021, while solvent recycling and process optimizations—such as redesigning production lines and streamlining workflows—reduced emissions from manufacturing. Additionally, the company committed to leveraging green building techniques and technology in growth projects to cut carbon emissions and resource use across facilities.\n\nSupporting these efforts, Lonza’s Environmental Risk Management (ERM) program provides a systematic framework for identifying and mitigating climate-related risks, with annual steps including cross-functional risk assessment, executive committee reviews, and Board oversight. Membership in the PSCI (Pharmaceutical Supply Chain Initiative) enables supplier audits and industry collaboration to address supply chain emissions, ensuring alignment with sector-specific standards. These governance mechanisms and partnerships ensure decarbonization efforts are integrated into strategic planning and operational execution.",
      "notes": "Strategy spans multiple pages (Images 3 and 4), with specific 2021 initiatives (e.g., Visp site CO₂-eq reduction) and planned actions (renewable electricity by 2025). Focuses on both operational efficiency and value chain engagement, supported by structured governance (ERM program, PSCI membership).",
      "status": null
    },
