      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy for 2021 focuses on operational decarbonization through targeted energy and waste management initiatives aligned with Singapore’s climate action plan 2030. At properties like Balestier Tower, energy and water consumption are systematically tracked and managed under CapitaLand’s Sustainable Buildings Guidelines and Environmental Health & Safety (EHS) Policy, with monthly usage data monitored via the Environmental Tracking System (ETS). Annual EHS targets are set in parallel with Singapore’s climate action roadmap, ensuring energy efficiency efforts directly support national decarbonization goals. This structured monitoring enables data-driven reductions in operational emissions from building operations. \n\nTo address waste-related emissions, the company implements concrete 3R (reduce, reuse, recycle) measures, including waste segregation into dedicated recycling streams, replacing photocopied documents with electronic circulation, using 100% recycled paper for printing, and transitioning to email-based correspondence and electronic drafting. Additional actions include deploying non-disposable utensils, conserving existing furniture and materials during renovations, and encouraging tenants to adopt green building materials for retail fit-outs. These initiatives reduce emissions linked to waste disposal and resource-intensive production processes. \n\nThe Board affirms that sustainability practices supporting Singapore’s climate action and waste reduction are integral to business strategy, with transparent reporting aligned with the Singapore Exchange Guide and GRI guidelines. By embedding these measures into property management workflows—such as standardized energy tracking and on-site waste reduction protocols—the company demonstrates a practical, operationally focused approach to decarbonization rather than relying on aspirational statements alone.",
