    "strategy": {
      "summary": "NTT DATA's decarbonization strategy for 2021 centers on a science-based approach aligned with the 1.5°C pathway of the Paris Agreement, with specific, certified targets for fiscal 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2050. The company has established concrete greenhouse gas reduction targets: a 60% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions and a 55% reduction in Scope 3 emissions by FY2030 from FY2016 levels, which have already achieved 31% and 28% reductions respectively by FY2020. This science-based target approach is formalized through SBTi certification and supports their broader Carbon-neutral Vision 2050 and Climate Action Plan for 2030. The strategy is structured around four key pillars: Green Business (establishing global presence as a top-level green innovation partner), Green Power (achieving 50% emissions reduction through technology-driven energy conservation and transitioning to 100% EVs for business fleet), Green Procurement (reducing emissions across the supply chain), and Workstyle Innovation (developing resilient workstyles combining online and offline venues).\n\nTo implement this strategy, NTT DATA is executing specific, measurable actions across their operations. The company is transitioning to high-efficiency electrical and air-conditioning systems while installing photovoltaic power generation and high-voltage direct current (HVDC) power supply systems at data centers, with the Mitaka Data Center EAST serving as a key example incorporating outdoor air-cooling systems that utilize photovoltaic power and natural energy. They are actively purchasing renewable energy across Japan, North America, and EMEA regions, with approximately 700 MWh generated in Japan during the reporting year. The company has also implemented district heating and cooling (DHC) systems at multiple facilities to reduce carbon emissions by consolidating high-efficiency heating and cooling equipment. Additionally, NTT DATA has committed to reducing electricity consumption by around 30% at their Mitaka Building through these efficiency measures.\n\nThe company's decarbonization efforts are supported by robust governance structures and strategic partnerships. The Climate Action Committee, chaired by the Representative Director and Senior Executive Vice President, oversees strategy planning and risk evaluation, with the Eco Activity Promotion Committee managing implementation. NTT DATA participates in multiple external initiatives including the TCFD, SBTi, Japan Climate Initiative, and Challenge Zero campaign led by the Japan Business Federation. The company conducts regular climate scenario analyses (1.5°C and 4°C scenarios) to assess financial impacts and prioritize climate-related risks, with a specific focus on addressing transition risks related to carbon pricing and market changes. This comprehensive approach integrates decarbonization into both their operational practices and strategic business development, positioning them as a green innovation partner for clients while systematically reducing their environmental footprint.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several pages (054-076) with specific implementation details. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 and 2) while also addressing Scope 3. Includes concrete initiatives with specific technologies, partnerships, and quantifiable targets. Strategy is detailed with implementation timelines and governance structures. The company has already achieved significant progress toward their 2030 targets (31% reduction for Scope 1 and 2, 28% for Scope 3 by FY2020).",
      "status": null
    },
