    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Yangzijiang Shipbuilding’s decarbonization strategy, titled the 'Two Carbon Strategic Plan,' aligns with China’s 2060 carbon neutrality target and focuses on two integrated pillars: green plant construction and green shipbuilding. This approach emphasizes operational transformation to reduce emissions while advancing sustainable manufacturing and vessel design. The company’s strategy is grounded in active collaboration and concrete actions to address both energy efficiency and low-carbon innovation across its value chain.\n\nFor green plant construction, the company implemented a 659,000 square meter energy storage power station with 48.75 million kW photovoltaic capacity, enabling a 4,906 tonnes coal-equivalent annual emissions reduction. It also introduced innovative production processes that increased steel utilization to an industry-leading 92.3%. In green shipbuilding, dual-fuel ships accounted for over 30% of 2021 new orders, supported by digital innovation that reduced mainstream ship construction cycles by up to 30%. Energy-saving technologies facilitated the independent development of specialized vessels, including 82,000-DWT fan boosters, 82,300-DWT bulk carriers, and 1,800-TEU to 24,000-TEU container ships. Additionally, over 50 sustainability training courses were organized to educate employees on low-carbon practices.\n\nThese initiatives are reinforced by a low-carbon innovation strategy encompassing continuous policy learning, participation in carbon emissions trading, and fostering employee adoption of low-carbon lifestyles. Measurable outcomes include a 0.3% year-on-year decline in energy consumption per unit product, a 2.7% reduction in industrial production energy use, and a 7.7% decrease in energy consumption per unit of industrial energy increment. The ultimate goal is transitioning to a green energy and low-carbon model to achieve energy efficiency, green manufacturing, and broader sustainability objectives.",
      "notes": "Strategy detailed in a single-page section of the 2021 Sustainability Report, with specific initiatives, measurable outcomes, and clear focus areas for operational decarbonization.",
      "status": null
    },
