    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Larsen & Toubro's decarbonization strategy centers on a dual approach of reducing emissions from current operations while strategically transitioning toward green energy businesses. The company has established clear net zero targets, aiming to achieve net zero carbon footprint by 2040 and net zero water consumption by 2035. In the short term, L&T is focused on flattening its emission curve within the next five years through improved energy efficiency and increased renewable energy adoption across operations. A key strategic pillar involves expanding its green business offerings, which currently constitute approximately 38% of its portfolio, while simultaneously reducing its presence in the fossil fuel space and building new businesses around green energy.\n\nTo implement this strategy, L&T is actively evaluating and developing prospects in multiple green energy sectors, including green hydrogen, battery storage, and offshore wind power. The company is pursuing operational efficiency improvements through increased off-site fabrication, greater emphasis on pre-cast technology, and enhanced mechanization and automation capabilities for on-site work. These initiatives are designed to reduce manual work components, increase productivity, minimize wastage, and ultimately improve the cost competitiveness of the business while reducing emissions. The company recognizes that energy transition from fossil fuels to green energy is an established global mega trend, and some of its businesses like thermal power have already felt this impact over recent years.\n\nSupporting these efforts, the company has established governance mechanisms with active Board and Management oversight of ESG performance on a regular basis. L&T has committed to reporting on its business responsibility and sustainability practices from FY22 onwards, ahead of the mandatory BRSR reporting requirements from FY23. The company has periodically reassessed key policies including its Sustainability Policy and Supplier Code of Conduct to strengthen its overall framework for environmental responsibility, recently adopting additional policies such as Equal Opportunity Policy and 'Public Policy Advocacy' Policy to further strengthen its policy framework.",
      "notes": "Strategy details provided within a single-page section of a broader sustainability report. Strategy includes specific near-term and long-term targets with concrete focus areas. Implementation details are moderately detailed with specific green energy sectors identified and operational efficiency measures outlined. Strategy focuses on both reducing emissions from current operations and transitioning to green energy businesses.",
      "status": null
    },
