    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CapitaLand China Trust's decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on a science-based approach aligned with CapitaLand's 2030 Sustainability Master Plan (SMP), targeting a 1.5°C trajectory with the ultimate goal of achieving Net Zero by 2050. The strategy focuses on operational efficiency improvements and systematic integration of sustainability throughout the real estate lifecycle. In 2022, CLCT elevated its Scope 1 and 2 carbon emissions reduction targets, validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), and began transitioning from a 2008 baseline to a 2019 baseline for more accurate measurement of progress. The company has established specific environmental targets including reducing carbon emissions intensity by 78%, energy consumption intensity by 35%, and water consumption intensity by 45% by 2030, with measurable progress already achieved in 2022 (63.0%, 56.9%, and 55.5% reductions respectively).\n\nCLCT implemented several concrete decarbonization initiatives in 2022, including the installation of 253 solar panels at Kunshan Bacheng Logistics Park to generate 92 megawatt hours of energy annually. The company also deployed multiple energy conservation measures across its portfolio such as natural ventilation systems, sun shades to reduce solar heat, upgrades to more efficient air-conditioning equipment, time sensors on AC systems, and LED lighting integrated with smart controls. Additionally, CLCT launched an IoT platform at its Business Parks for centralized monitoring and data analytics to optimize equipment performance. The company began tracking Scope 3 emissions for the first time, including corporate air travel and tenants' energy consumption in retail malls and business parks, recording 91,404 tonnes CO2e in 2022.\n\nTo support its decarbonization strategy, CLCT has embedded sustainability throughout its real estate lifecycle via the Capitaland Sustainable Building Guidelines, which govern investment, design, construction, and operations phases. The company utilizes its Environmental Tracking System (ETS) for continuous monitoring of energy, water usage, and carbon emissions across properties. CLCT's approach is further strengthened by its ISO 14001 certified Environmental Management System and annual Risk and Control Self-Assessment (RCSA) exercise, which identifies and mitigates climate-related risks. The company also conducts Environmental, Health and Safety Impact Assessments (EHSIA) for all new investments to identify environmental risks and opportunities from the earliest stages of development.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across 9 images; Strategy focuses on operational emissions with specific 2022 implementation details; Clear connection between targets and specific initiatives; Comprehensive approach covering entire real estate lifecycle; Limited information on Scope 3 emissions reduction strategy beyond initial tracking",
      "status": null
    },
