    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CICT's decarbonization strategy for 2022 is structured around CapitalLand's 2030 Sustainability Master Plan with a science-based 1.5°C trajectory, aiming for Net Zero by 2050. The company implements a comprehensive Carbon Mitigation Hierarchy framework that prioritizes avoidance through low-consumption design, reduction through high energy efficiency measures, replacement with renewable energy sources, and compensation through carbon offsets as a last resort. This approach spans the entire real estate life cycle, from investment through design, construction, operations, and divestment.\n\nTo operationalize this strategy, CICT leverages specific initiatives including the Environmental Tracking System (ETS) for monitoring energy, water, and carbon emissions across its portfolio, with enhanced cloud-based capabilities improving data accuracy and benchmarking. The company has installed solar photovoltaic systems at properties like IMM Building (3,633 panels in phase 1, with additional 672 panels planned) and participates in the CapitalLand Sustainability X Challenge (CSXC) to pilot innovative technologies, including water leak detection systems. CICT also adopted CapitalLand's internal carbon price implemented in 2021 to quantify climate-related risks and opportunities for all new investments.\n\nThe strategy is supported by robust governance mechanisms including alignment with CLI's Board-approved sustainability targets, performance-linked remuneration for executives, and regular assessments through the Environmental, Health and Safety Management System (EHSMS). CICT has established a Green Finance Framework to support sustainability-linked borrowing, with approximately 30% of group borrowings already sustainability-linked as of December 2022. The company's 2030 targets include reducing carbon emissions intensity by 78%, energy consumption intensity by 35%, water consumption intensity by 45%, and achieving 35% renewable energy contribution to total energy consumption.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple report sections. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (scope 1 and 2) with clear 2030 targets. Implementation details include specific technologies, partnership programs, and governance structures. Strategy is comprehensive with both short-term (2030) and long-term (2050) horizons.",
      "status": null
    },
