      "summary": "Fraser Logistics & Commercial Trust's (FLCT) decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on achieving net-zero carbon emissions across their portfolio by 2030 through a structured, multi-faceted approach. The company has submitted carbon reduction targets to the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) for validation and finalized an action plan aligned with the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosure (TCFD) recommendations. Recognizing the 'narrowing window for action to mitigate climate change,' FLCT emphasizes partnering with stakeholders to accelerate the transition to a low-carbon economy. Their strategy is organized around three pillars: 'Acting Progressively,' 'Consuming Responsibly,' and 'Focusing on People,' with specific emphasis on energy efficiency and emissions reduction throughout their building lifecycle.\n\nTo implement this strategy, FLCT has taken several concrete actions in FY2022. They retrofitted 100% of their Australian industrial assets with high-efficiency lighting and secured 65% of total borrowings through green, sustainable, or sustainability-linked financing. The company maintains the highest Green Star Performance rated industrial portfolio in Australia and has retained their 5-Star GRESB rating with an improved score of 89 out of 100. Implementation of a Responsible Sourcing Policy is underway to reduce negative impacts in their supply chain. FLCT is actively working to 'decarbonise at every phase of building construction and operation, from maximising energy efficiency to increasing our use of renewable energy,' despite challenges posed by tenant-controlled properties limiting direct emissions control.\n\nThe company's decarbonization efforts are supported by robust governance structures, including the Sponsor's Sustainability Steering Committee that meets six times annually to drive sustainability strategy. A dedicated sustainability manager oversees the REIT's sustainability performance, ensuring alignment with their goals. FLCT also established an advisory group comprising senior management representatives from various corporate functions to support their net carbon zero by 2050 ambition. Their strategic engagement with key sustainability frameworks—including the United Nations Global Compact, Science Based Targets initiative, and various Green Building Councils—further strengthens their approach to reducing emissions and promoting sustainable practices across their portfolio.",
