    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Hong Leong Bank's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a clear net zero roadmap with specific targets and financial mechanisms to accelerate the transition to a low carbon economy. The bank has updated its key GHG emissions reduction targets, establishing FY2019 as the baseline year, with a short-term target of 15% to 25% reduction of GHG emissions by 2026, a medium-term target of net zero emissions for operational Scope 1 and 2 by 2030, and a long-term commitment to achieve net zero for all emissions (Scope 1, 2, and 3) by 2050. To operationalize this commitment, the bank has established a comprehensive framework for measuring customers' carbon footprints and is targeting the establishment of a baseline for Scope 3 financing portfolio emissions by the end of FY2024.\n\nThe bank is implementing concrete financial initiatives to drive decarbonization, having approved over RM 2.4 billion worth of renewable energy financing in FY2022, which surpassed the 5-year target of RM 500 million. It has also established a new target of additional RM 1.5 billion to finance renewable energy projects by FY2025. To support this financing, the bank launched its Green Bond Framework, which sets guidelines for bond issuance where proceeds are used to finance or refinance green assets and projects meeting specific eligibility criteria. This framework led to the issuance of the bank's first Green Additional Tier 1 (\"AT1\") Bond worth RM 900 million in April 2022, marking a key milestone as the first issuance of a green AT1 bond by a bank in Malaysia.\n\nBeyond financing, the bank is implementing operational initiatives including a carbon offsetting project with the Malaysian Nature Society to restore degraded forest land in Kuala Selangor Nature Park by planting approximately 50,000 new mangrove trees. The bank also achieved a 6% reduction in Scope 2 emissions compared to FY2021 through its Energy Efficiency & Conservation measures. To support customers' transitions, the bank has developed green financing products across commercial, SME, and retail segments including Renewable Energy Financing, Property Mortgage, and Green Car Financing options, while also building a Greenhouse Gas Emissions calculator to help customers measure their carbon footprints.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with concrete targets, financial mechanisms, and implementation details. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions and financing portfolio emissions. Includes specific monetary targets, timeline commitments, and actual achievements from 2022. Comprehensive approach covering internal operations, customer financing, and carbon offsetting initiatives.",
      "status": null
    },
