    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Keppel's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a dual approach: running the business sustainably while making sustainability integral to business operations. The company committed to halving absolute Scope 1 and 2 carbon emissions by 2030 (compared to 2020 levels) and achieving net zero by 2050, with specific targets for 50% renewable electricity by 2025 and 100% by 2030. In 2022, they achieved a 17.6% absolute reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions, bringing them to 142,004 tCO2e from 172,282 tCO2e in 2020, while expanding Scope 3 emissions tracking from 10 to 15 categories to improve comprehensive measurement.\n\nThe company executed several concrete initiatives to advance decarbonization, including growing its renewable energy portfolio from 1.1 GW to 2.6 GW by year-end 2022. Specific projects included building Singapore's first hydrogen-ready 600 MW power plant, developing the Keppel Sakra Cogen Plant (designed to be Singapore's most energy-efficient power plant), and establishing Keppel MET Renewables with Swiss-based MET Group to pursue greenfield and brownfield solar projects. They also pioneered cross-border renewable energy trade into Singapore through the Laos PDR-Thailand-Malaysia-Singapore Power Integration Project and developed a 500+ MW solar project in Australia.\n\nTo support these efforts, Keppel implemented a shadow carbon price (SCP) in 2020, starting at US$20 per tonne of CO2e, to better understand carbon footprints and encourage mitigation measures. The company secured approximately $3.1 billion in green and sustainability-linked financing since 2019 and committed $2.8 billion to energy and environment-related investments. Business units like Keppel Land and M1 announced Science-Based Targets initiative (SBTi)-validated emissions reduction targets, while Keppel Data Centres aims for net zero Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2030. Additionally, they expanded district cooling systems in Singapore's Jurong Innovation District and Bangkok's Sam Yan commercial area to improve energy efficiency across operations.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across TCFD Disclosures, Scenario Planning, and Decarbonisation Strategy sections. Strategy includes specific targets, implementation details, and measurable outcomes for 2022. The company demonstrates both operational decarbonization (reducing emissions from own operations) and enabling decarbonization (providing solutions for others). Detailed implementation plans with timelines and specific technologies are provided.",
      "status": null
    },
