      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy centers on transitioning to renewable energy and optimizing operational energy efficiency to reduce its carbon footprint. Key focus areas include leveraging solar energy as the primary renewable source and implementing campus-wide energy-saving measures to minimize reliance on non-renewable electricity. This approach aligns with Singapore’s Green Plan 2030 and the target of achieving net-zero emissions by 2050, reflecting a commitment to both national climate goals and operational sustainability. \n\nA core initiative is the installation of Solar Photovoltaic (PV) panels, which were commissioned on 3 March 2023, with the goal of generating up to 25% of the school’s total electricity from renewable sources. Additionally, the company has deployed full-spectrum mercury-free LED lighting across all classrooms and study areas, supported by energy-saving features such as efficient air distribution systems, smart lifts, escalators, timer-switches, and sensors to reduce energy waste and improve environmental quality. These measures directly address emissions from electricity consumption, which previously relied entirely on non-renewable sources as of 2022. \n\nTo advance this strategy, the company plans to explore additional feasible spaces for solar PV expansion and review other renewable energy options. Governance oversight is provided by the Chief Executive Officer and Sustainability Team Lead, ensuring alignment with sustainability reporting requirements and strategic accountability. The strategy emphasizes actionable, technology-driven steps to reduce carbon emissions while maintaining a safe and effective learning environment.",
