      "summary": "Sasseur REIT’s 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on integrating climate risk and opportunity assessment into core business operations, guided by TCFD recommendations and scenario analysis. The company prioritized establishing foundational climate governance and data systems, including the creation of a Sustainability Committee (SC) in July 2022 to strengthen climate-related governance. A key focus was conducting climate scenario analysis to evaluate physical risks (e.g., floods, heatwaves) and transition risks (e.g., policy shifts, market trends) using frameworks from the IPCC (RCP8.5, RCP2.6) and IEA (STEPS, NZE), which informed risk mitigation and opportunity identification. The company also initiated its decarbonization journey by establishing a greenhouse gas (GHG) inventory to monitor Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions, as detailed in its Sustainability Report.\n\nSpecific 2022 initiatives included assessing renewable energy opportunities through cost-saving analyses of solar photovoltaic (PV) and wind power, comparing Levelized Cost of Electricity (LCOE) across scenarios to identify viable pathways. For instance, the company explored deploying on-site PV systems and Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs) for Sasseur (Kunming) Outlets, leveraging China’s renewable energy policies and declining LCOE trends. Concurrently, Sasseur REIT engaged tenants through face-to-face ESG dialogues to promote energy and water conservation, reduce waste, and encourage recycling, recognizing tenant behavior as critical to emissions reduction. These efforts were complemented by ongoing assessments of transition risks, such as potential revenue loss from shifting tenant preferences toward zero-carbon buildings, ensuring strategic alignment with market dynamics.",
