      "summary": "Sino Land's decarbonization strategy is anchored in their 'Decarbonisation Blueprint,' launched in June 2022 following extensive research collaboration with HKUST. This comprehensive roadmap supports their commitment to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2050 and aligns with the Business Ambition for 1.5°C initiative. The strategy is structured around three key pillars: Development, Operations, and Collaboration, with specific initiatives designed to reduce emissions across all scopes.\n\nUnder the Development pillar, Sino Land is implementing climate-resilient design practices including procuring low-carbon construction materials, achieving sustainable building certifications for new developments, and conducting climate risk assessments for new buildings. The company has established sustainable construction sites through deploying more efficient equipment and reducing reliance on diesel generators. For Operations, the company has deployed specific technologies such as Huawei's iCooling@AI platform and CLP PlantPro smart platform for chiller plants, while implementing energy efficiency measures like modernizing lifts, expanding green roofs, and installing photovoltaic panels, solar-wind turbines, and energy-generating paving.\n\nIn the Collaboration pillar, Sino Land is engaging stakeholders through resource management initiatives including community recycling networks, reverse vending machines, and smart food waste collection systems. The company has set concrete targets to reduce Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions per square metre by 53.1% from the 2018 baseline by 2030, and is working with HKUST to incorporate Scope 3 emissions into this target using SBTi methodology. As of June 30, 2022, Sino Land had already achieved a 39.68% reduction in GHG emissions from the 2012 baseline. The company has also engaged PricewaterhouseCoopers to evaluate climate resilience across over 170 properties and established an ESG Steering Committee to oversee implementation.",
