      "summary": "VICOM's decarbonization strategy for 2022 is centered on operational optimization and regulatory compliance, aligning with Singapore's national climate goals and the Paris Agreement commitment to achieve net-zero emissions by 2050. The company focuses on managing its environmental impact through resource management systems that specifically target emissions reduction and energy consumption. VICOM's approach emphasizes systematic implementation of environmental management frameworks across its operations, with particular attention to ensuring vehicles stay within emission limits through their inspection services, while also providing customers with emission testing services to support broader sustainability efforts.\n\nTo execute this strategy, VICOM has implemented various internal management systems, policies, and measures to optimize energy use and regulate resources, ultimately reducing emissions and limiting pollution. The company is actively working toward ISO 14001:2015 certification by FY 2023, which will formalize their environmental management system requirements. Additionally, VICOM is introducing emission reduction technologies to reduce both fuel and electricity usage, with operations optimization serving as a key pillar of their approach. SETSCO, a subsidiary, has already achieved ISO 50001 certification for its Energy Management System and is an Energy Efficiency National Partner (EENP) with Singapore's National Environment Agency (NEA).\n\nThe company's decarbonization efforts are supported by strategic partnerships and certifications that provide external validation and guidance. Both VICOM and SETSCO attained Eco-Office certifications from the Singapore Environment Council in 2022, with VICOM receiving the Champion award and SETSCO the Elite award. These certifications complement their alignment with ComfortDelGro Group's Science Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) commitment. SETSCO's Bukit Batok building is also Green Mark Certified by Singapore's Building and Construction Authority, demonstrating their commitment to sustainable infrastructure. Through these interconnected initiatives and certifications, VICOM is building a systematic approach to emissions management that supports both their operational needs and Singapore's national climate ambitions.",
