      "summary": "ANAN INTERNATIONAL LIMITED, through its operational entity Dyneff, has established a structured decarbonization strategy aligned with France's Climate and Resilience Law, targeting carbon neutrality by 2050 with a critical 2030 milestone requiring a 55% reduction in carbon footprint. This strategy centers on three integrated pillars: renewable energy adoption, alternative fuel deployment, and data-driven emissions management, with a focus on operational emissions reduction across Scope 1 and 2 categories. The approach prioritizes tangible implementation over aspirational statements, leveraging national policy frameworks to guide concrete actions within the French market context.\n\nIn 2024, Dyneff executed specific, measurable initiatives including the reduction of approximately 36,160 tons of CO2 emissions through biofuel and solar energy integration. The company established hydrogen green stations at Toulouse Nord and Toulouse Sud motorway stations as part of the regional Green Hydrogen Plan, while partnering with SNCF (French National Railway Company) to replace diesel with HVO100 synthetic biofuel at multiple stations, achieving 50-90% greenhouse gas reductions. This collaboration also included commissioning an experimental hybrid trainset for one-year testing across commercial rail lines, with HVO100 now operational at Dyneff's EPPLN depot in Port-La-Nouvelle.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, Dyneff conducted its first comprehensive carbon emissions assessment in France through a partnership with Swee to establish baseline Scope 1 and 2 data, detailed on Page 16 of the report. This data-driven foundation will inform quantified reduction targets set in coming years, ensuring targets remain both ambitious and grounded in real operational data. The strategy demonstrates a proactive transition pathway through technology adoption (HVO100, hydrogen infrastructure), strategic partnerships (SNCF, regional hydrogen initiatives), and rigorous emissions measurement, directly supporting national decarbonization goals while building scalable operational models for future expansion.",
