    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Annica Holdings Limited's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers around a structured Climate Change Transition Plan with specific, measurable targets. The company has committed to reducing its aggregated absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 23% by FY2035, using FY2022 as the baseline, with the ultimate goal of achieving carbon neutrality by FY2050. This approach is organized around three strategic levers: 'Reduce and Produce,' 'Produce,' and 'Neutralise,' which form a comprehensive framework for emissions reduction.\n\nThe company is implementing specific initiatives across these levers, including energy efficiency measures such as LED lighting and motion sensors in their lighting systems, as well as behavioral changes and clean energy adoption. In the 'Produce' category, they are focusing on solar energy and energy storage solutions. For 'Neutralise,' the company utilizes renewable energy certificates (REC) and carbon credits to address remaining emissions. Through their H2EI Group subsidiary, they are actively developing green hydrogen projects, including partnerships with Universiti Kebangsaan Malaysia for hydrogen technology research and a memorandum of understanding with ISURE and Universiti Malaysia Sarawak to develop a green hydrogen system for Kampung Assum, Sarawak.\n\nSupporting this strategy is a robust monitoring system where the company tracks and measures Scope 1, 2, and certain Scope 3 GHG emissions in alignment with the GHG Protocol. The Climate Change Transition Plan is developed with an internal review process to ensure accurate reporting. Additionally, the company is expanding its renewable energy capabilities through strategic partnerships and has received recognition for its efforts, including the National Energy Award 2023 for Renewable Energy - Special Submission. The waste tyre recycling business, set to commence in FY2025, further diversifies their decarbonization initiatives beyond energy-focused solutions.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found in Sustainability Report (pages 23 and 38). Strategy includes specific targets (23% reduction by FY2035, carbon neutrality by FY2050) and three strategic levers with concrete implementation details. The company demonstrates commitment through specific partnerships, technology investments, and external recognition. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions reduction and renewable energy development.",
      "status": null
    },
