      "summary": "Allied Universal's 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on advancing science-based targets through concrete operational and supply chain actions, with a specific focus on Scope 3 emissions assessment and fleet electrification. The company initiated a comprehensive global program to assess Scope 3 GHG emissions in partnership with TRC, a global consultancy specializing in engineering and information processing. This involves identifying material Scope 3 categories, defining accurate data collection processes, and completing the first global Scope 3 emissions inventory for 2025. Concurrently, the company maintains its annual carbon intensity reduction target of 3.5% (t/CO2e per $M revenue) while addressing operational emissions through fleet decarbonization initiatives. In the UK and Ireland region specifically, G4S is implementing near-term emissions reductions across its value chain, building toward 2030 targets of 42% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions and 25% reduction in Scope 3 emissions from a 2020 baseline.\n\nTo execute this strategy, Allied Universal is taking several specific 2024 actions. The company has accelerated fleet decarbonization, with the UK and Ireland fleet now comprising 753 low-emission vehicles and 218 fully electric vehicles. A notable pilot program with Ford Motor Company successfully trialed fully electric ambulances within Patient Transport Services, utilizing a 'home-start' framework supported by branch-based charging and Shell's public charging network. Additionally, the company is enhancing data management for value chain GHG emissions and addressing Scope 1 and 2 reductions through operational adjustments, including a 2,600 t/CO2e reduction resulting from the transfer of financial control for certain operations during 2024. These actions contributed to measurable 2024 progress, with operational emissions (Scopes 1 and 2) decreasing to 19,120 t/CO2e and supply chain emissions (Scope 3) falling to 98,575 t/CO2e.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a structured governance approach that integrates emerging legislative requirements and regional experience, particularly leveraging the UK and Ireland region's implementation of science-based targets. The company is using 2024 Scope 3 assessment data to develop a science-based decarbonization roadmap that includes validation processes and sustainability strategies for achieving net-zero emissions by 2050. This integrated approach connects immediate operational improvements with long-term strategic planning, ensuring that near-term reductions in emissions categories (which formed approximately 76% of UK and Ireland Scope 3 emissions in 2024) directly inform the development of comprehensive decarbonization pathways.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across Environment sections of ESG Report 2024; Strategy includes specific 2024 initiatives with measurable progress data; Focus on Scope 3 assessment and fleet electrification as primary action areas; Contains concrete partnerships (TRC, Ford, Shell) and implementation details; Strategy integrates near-term 2024 actions with 2030 targets and 2050 net-zero commitment",
