      "summary": "Atika’s decarbonization strategy for FY2024 centers on establishing a data-driven foundation and aligning with global climate frameworks to guide future emission reduction efforts. The company completed tracking of Scope 1 and Scope 2 greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions to establish a baseline, which serves as a critical reference point for shaping decarbonization initiatives. To align with the Paris Agreement, Atika adopted a 1.5°C warming scenario as its climate transition pathway, recognizing this as a more stringent approach to mitigate long-term physical climate impacts compared to higher temperature rise scenarios (>3°C). This strategic choice emphasizes the urgency of proactive climate action while acknowledging the heightened risks associated with less ambitious pathways.\n\nTo operationalize this approach, Atika engaged an independent third-party consultant to support the development of its climate strategy, marking a structured effort to formalize decarbonization planning. As part of this process, the company conducted its first climate change scenario analysis, assessing exposure to both physical and transition risks while identifying potential climate-related opportunities. This analysis is designed to inform targeted actions by evaluating how different climate scenarios could impact operations, ensuring the strategy addresses both immediate vulnerabilities and long-term decarbonization needs. While the current focus remains on foundational steps like baseline establishment and strategic planning, these efforts lay the groundwork for future implementation of specific emission reduction measures.",
