      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy for 2024 is anchored in the refreshed CLI 2030 Sustainability Master Plan (SMP), which integrates Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi)-validated carbon reduction targets aligned with a 1.5°C climate scenario and a Net Zero commitment. Central to this approach is embedding ESG considerations into financial strategy through a $200 million Sustainability-Linked Loan (SLL) from the International Finance Corporation (IFC), which requires a 40.5% reduction in absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions for its IT Business Park Portfolio by 31 December 2023. As of 2024, 65% of the company’s total loans are sustainability-linked, demonstrating a direct alignment between financing and decarbonization goals. The strategy also emphasizes TCFD-aligned governance, with climate-related disclosures covering governance, strategy, risk management, and metrics since 2017.\n\nKey operational initiatives include commissioning a 21-megawatt solar power plant in Tamil Nadu in 2024, generating 29 million kilowatt-hours annually to meet the power needs of 2 million square feet of office space. This project enabled the company to surpass two 2030 SMP environmental targets: achieving over 50% green energy usage and a 46% reduction in absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions. Additionally, 94% of the portfolio (38 buildings) holds Platinum or Gold green building certifications (IGBC/USGBC LEED), with a commitment to secure such certifications for all new and existing high-value buildings by 2030. The company validates sustainability performance through annual Sustainability Performance Target (SPT) certificates, including Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions metrics as required by the IFC SLL.\n\nTo ensure strategic resilience, the company conducts climate scenario analyses across 1.5°C to 3°C pathways to assess financial material risks and inform mitigation plans. Since 2021, it has engaged external consultants to verify green certifications and renewable energy adoption per Singapore Standard 4400 (Revised), while integrating stakeholder feedback—such as tenant suggestions—into environmental strategy to drive continuous improvement in resource efficiency and emissions reduction.",
