    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CapitalLand Integrated Commercial Trust (CICT) has implemented a comprehensive decarbonization strategy centered around its 2030 Sustainability Master Plan (SMP), which establishes science-based targets for reducing emissions across its real estate portfolio. The strategy follows a structured approach organized into key focus areas: Low-carbon Transition, Water Conservation and Resilience, Waste Management and Circular Economy, and Sustainable Innovation and Technology. CICT's decarbonization approach is guided by the CLI Avoid, Reduce, Replace, and Compensate hierarchy, with emphasis on avoiding emissions through low-consumption design and reducing emissions through high-energy efficiency measures and intelligent building platforms. The company has established concrete initiatives including implementation of TCFD reporting since 2021, climate scenario analysis using 1.5°C to 3°C scenarios, and EHS Impact Assessment during due diligence for new investments to identify environmental risks.\n\nCICT's specific decarbonization actions include installing solar PVs on building rooftops where feasible, exploring new technologies like micro-wind turbines and waste-to-energy solutions, and implementing intelligent building platforms with IoT-driven monitoring systems for energy optimization. The company is actively transitioning to renewable energy through on-site generation and power purchase agreements with off-site solar and wind farms. For existing properties, CICT has implemented the Environmental, Health and Safety Management System (EHSMS) certified to ISO 14001 and 45001 standards, which monitors transition risks related to climate change and manages operational issues through a systematic framework. The portfolio has achieved 100% green-rated status as of March 2025, with properties certified through various green rating systems including BCA Green Mark, BREEAM, and LEED.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a robust governance framework with established board oversight in ESG strategies, dedicated board and management training on climate-related issues, and annual trust-wide RCSA exercises. CICT has also developed a detailed Carbon Mitigation Hierarchy that prioritizes avoiding emissions through low-consumption design, reducing emissions through high-efficiency equipment and smart building analytics, replacing fossil fuel consumption with renewable energy sources, and using carbon offsets only as a last resort for residual emissions. The company's 2024 progress shows 8% reduction in absolute Scope 1 & 2 GHG emissions and 17% reduction in carbon emissions intensity, demonstrating the implementation of these strategic approaches.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across environmental and ESG sections. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) with specific implementation details provided. Strategy integrates with CLI's 2030 SMP and includes both targets and concrete initiatives. Carbon Mitigation Hierarchy provides structured approach to decarbonization. Implementation details are specific and actionable, not just high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
