    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Digital Core REIT's decarbonization strategy centers on reducing emissions across all scopes while enhancing energy efficiency and renewable energy adoption. The company has committed to Science-Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) goals to decrease Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 68% and Scope 3 emissions by 24% by 2030 from a 2018 baseline, having already achieved a 60% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions per square foot as of FY 2024. With 40% of their portfolio now fully matched with renewable energy sources through renewable attestations for specific locations like 44520 Hastings, 3011 Lafayette, and 8217 Linton, they are expanding their renewable portfolio by adding properties such as Wilhelm-Fay-Straße 15 and 24 in Frankfurt to their reporting scope. The strategy encompasses both operational improvements and strategic partnerships, with the company collaborating with its Sponsor to integrate sustainability goals and engaging customers to implement energy-efficient solutions such as procuring renewable energy certificates.\n\nThe company is implementing concrete initiatives including an AI Platform that detects performance variances and prevents energy leakages, sustainable building design practices, and collaboration with customers for sustainability upgrades and CapEx. They utilize the ENERGY STAR® Portfolio Manager and Envizi platform to automate data capture and consolidation across hundreds of data types, creating a robust sustainability data system. Additionally, they've integrated sustainability key performance indicators into the remuneration scorecard for key management personnel, aligning executive incentives with decarbonization goals. Digital Core REIT is also working toward achieving ISO management certification for all assets under-reporting scope by 2030, with several properties already certified to standards including ISO9001, ISO14001, ISO27001, and ISO50001.\n\nThe strategy is underpinned by comprehensive governance and risk management frameworks. The Digital Core REIT Board oversees the overall business strategy including sustainability targets, while their Enterprise Risk Management Framework identifies and addresses climate-related risks. They conduct climate scenario analysis using IPCC RCP scenarios (RCP 2.6, RCP 4.5, and RCP 8.5) with defined time horizons for assessing climate impacts: short-term (next three years), medium-term (by 2030), and long-term (by 2050). Looking ahead, they plan to enhance their strategy by extending reporting to include Scope 3 emissions coverage, expanding renewable energy coverage, and investing in better-performing assets to be added to the portfolio.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 105, 108, 109, and 117. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 and 2) while addressing Scope 3. Includes concrete implementation details with specific technologies (AI Platform, ENERGY STAR®), partnerships, and governance mechanisms. Strategy is well-structured around TCFD pillars with defined time horizons and specific targets.",
      "status": null
    },
