      "summary": "GDS’s decarbonization strategy in 2024 is anchored in its Environmental Policy, which integrates climate action across operational, supply chain, and innovation frameworks. The company prioritizes a circular economy model, rigorous greenhouse gas (GHG) monitoring with a compensation plan targeting zero emissions by 2050, and embedding sustainability into business strategies—particularly within the supply chain and Green Tech sector, which delivers energy transition support for clients. These efforts are guided by a commitment to environmental, social, and governance (ESG) principles, ensuring financial and operational decisions align with long-term climate goals.\n\nA cornerstone 2024 initiative is the €7.5 million investment in a ground-based photovoltaic system in Veronella, Italy, designed to increase renewable energy production and improve energy efficiency; the project, launched in 2024, is scheduled for completion in 2025. Concurrently, GDS leverages Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) to evaluate product environmental impacts from production to disposal, using 2024 to analyze prior results and prepare Environmental Product Declarations (EPDs) for 2025. The company also maintains ISO-certified Management Systems to uphold environmental and social standards, ensuring consistent oversight of emission reduction and resource efficiency.\n\nTo operationalize this strategy, GDS combines targeted technology investments—such as photovoltaic infrastructure and LCA tools—with governance mechanisms like annual progress reporting in financial documents and independent audits. Its Green Tech sector directly supports client energy transitions through energy efficiency solutions, while the broader focus on sustainable innovation and supply chain integration ensures decarbonization efforts extend beyond internal operations to industry-wide impact.",
