    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Grand Venture Technology Limited's 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on a phased approach to climate action, focusing on both immediate operational improvements and strategic planning for long-term transition. The company is progressively working toward full Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) alignment through quantitative scenario analysis and has initiated its decarbonization journey with concrete steps including the installation of solar panels to supplement energy consumption, integration of digital technologies to enhance factory efficiency and productivity, and the purchase of Renewable Energy Certificates (RECs) to support a just transition. The Board oversees these climate-related initiatives as part of its governance structure, with climate considerations integrated into the company's comprehensive strategy and risk management framework.\n\nThe company is implementing specific initiatives to enhance climate resilience, including plans to implement an ESG digital data collection and calculation platform in the second quarter of 2025, which will enable Scope 3 emissions reporting. GVT is also developing location-specific risk mitigation plans to address extreme weather events, carbon taxes, and workforce productivity losses, while exploring renewable energy investments in its China and Malaysia operations to mirror Singapore's success. To strengthen their approach, the company is working to improve data accuracy for scenario modeling by incorporating real-time data tracking and more precise climate and economic modeling tools.\n\nSupporting these efforts, GVT is strengthening the link between mitigation investments and financial outcomes to demonstrate return on investment, with particular focus on solar and automation initiatives. The company is expanding the quantification of transition risks and cost savings to improve reporting transparency and is developing climate resilience strategies that align with the latest international climate agreements. The Board receives quarterly updates on climate strategy and GHG emission reduction progress, ensuring climate considerations remain integrated into the company's overall strategic decision-making process.",
      "notes": "Strategy focuses on operational emissions with concrete initiatives already in progress (solar panels, digital technologies, RECs). The company is in early stages of decarbonization with planned investments in data systems for improved reporting. Strategy is detailed with specific actions and timelines, particularly around ESG data platform implementation in Q2 2025. The approach integrates climate considerations into governance structure with Board oversight.",
      "status": null
    },
