    "strategy": {
      "summary": "IIH Healthcare's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a multi-pronged approach focused on reducing emissions intensity while maintaining healthcare quality. The company is implementing targeted initiatives across its operations with specific emphasis on anesthetic gas management, energy efficiency, and renewable energy adoption. A key focus has been reducing desflurane usage - an anesthetic gas with significantly higher global warming potential than alternatives - achieving up to 55% reduction across core markets through localized approaches that involved close collaboration with anesthesiology teams and comprehensive staff training on sustainable practices. This strategic reduction in high-GWP anesthetic gases represents one of their most impactful emission reduction measures for 2024.\n\nTo support operational decarbonization, IIH Healthcare is advancing energy efficiency through chiller system replacements with higher-efficiency technologies like magnetic bearing chillers, while simultaneously deploying renewable energy sources. The company signed a contract for a large-scale solar farm in Türkiye expected to cover up to 80% of annual energy needs by 2025, and expanded rooftop solar installations across 10 hospitals in Malaysia and Hong Kong with six additional facilities scheduled for installation by end of 2025. These initiatives contributed to a 3.2% year-on-year reduction in emissions intensity per patient-bed-day in 2024.\n\nThe company is strengthening its climate resilience through comprehensive risk assessment and responsible sourcing practices. IIH implemented a Global Responsible Sourcing Policy in 2024 to guide vendors toward climate-conscious practices, while conducting climate scenario analyses to identify physical risks like floods and heatwaves, as well as transition risks related to policy changes. To support these efforts, they launched an environmental sustainability data platform to track progress and established a structured pathway toward Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) readiness by 2025, with plans to announce 2030 sustainability goals in 2026 as part of their roadmap to achieve Net-Zero by 2050.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 7-64; Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) and supply chain engagement; Specific implementation details provided for key initiatives including desflurane reduction and renewable energy deployment; Strategy includes clear timelines and measurable targets; Company has established a structured pathway toward SBTi validation",
      "status": null
    },
