      "summary": "HG Metal’s decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on integrating climate risk management into core operations while pursuing phased renewable energy adoption and value chain engagement. The company has embedded climate-related risks and opportunities into its strategic planning, focusing on mitigating both physical and transitional risks through a three-dimensional sustainability approach (environmental, social, and governance). Key focus areas include transitioning to renewable energy sources, enhancing supply chain sustainability, and optimizing operational efficiency to reduce carbon intensity. The strategy is aligned with global climate goals and informed by scenario analysis conducted in FY2023 using the IPCC AR-6 Report and TCFD recommendations.\n\nSpecific initiatives include a phased shift to renewable energy, with solar power targeted to constitute at least 30% of total energy consumption in FY2024 and FY2025, rising to 35% by FY2030. The company is actively exploring solar energy substitution for non-renewable sources in the short to medium term (2024–2030) and expanding supplier environmental assessments to evaluate and mitigate climate-related risks across the value chain. Additionally, efforts to minimize operational waste and monitor technological advancements in electric vehicles (EVs), particularly for heavy-load lorries, form part of mid-term decarbonization actions. Baseline Scope 1 and 2 emissions were established in 2023 at 1,267.72 tCO₂e, with annual reviews to track progress against these metrics.\n\nSupporting this strategy is a dedicated Sustainability Committee, chaired by the Board, which oversees climate-related risk management and reports directly to the Board to ensure alignment with corporate strategy. The committee’s regular meetings integrate sustainability into organizational practices, while scenario analysis and adherence to frameworks like the Steel Industry Development guidelines ensure the strategy remains responsive to evolving climate science and industry standards. Annual reviews of initiatives further reinforce accountability and continuous improvement in reducing carbon emissions across all operations.",
