      "summary": "iWOW TECHNOLOGY LIMITED's decarbonization strategy for 2024 is built around a structured approach to climate risk management and emissions reduction, with clear targets and specific operational initiatives. The company has established a phased reporting framework aligned with TCFD recommendations, focusing on identifying, assessing, and mitigating climate-related risks across their operations. Their strategy centers on transitioning to a low-carbon economy through resource efficiency improvements and leveraging their core IoT technology solutions to help customers reduce emissions. The company has set concrete targets including net-zero emissions by 2050, a 50% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2030 (using FY2024 as baseline), and a 10% electricity reduction per employee by FY2025. These targets are supported by specific initiatives such as implementing Smart Metering solutions, exploring AI technology to optimize energy consumption, and incorporating product refurbishment into their business model to reduce supply chain dependencies and associated climate risks. To support this transition, iWOW is integrating climate-related risks into their enterprise risk management framework, with the Board maintaining ultimate oversight and Senior Management serving as climate risk owners. They have also established a Sustainability Committee to monitor and manage climate-related risks, while conducting scenario analysis across different climate pathways (SSP1-2.6 and SSP3-7.0) to ensure their strategy remains resilient across potential future conditions. The company recognizes that addressing both physical risks (like supply chain disruptions from extreme weather) and transition risks (including reputational concerns and shifting consumer preferences) is critical to maintaining business resilience while advancing their decarbonization journey.",
