    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Keppel Infrastructure Trust (KIT) has established a comprehensive decarbonization strategy centered on specific targets, concrete initiatives, and robust governance structures. The company is committed to achieving net zero emissions across Scope 1 and 2 by 2050, with an interim target to increase its absolute renewable energy capacity to 2 GW by 2030. KIT's strategy is structured around expanding its renewable energy portfolio while simultaneously reducing emissions from existing operations, with a particular focus on energy transition assets that constitute 59% of its total portfolio. The company has conducted a double materiality assessment to update its material ESG factors and is actively addressing Scope 3 emissions, which may involve broadening the range of targets applied across its operations.\n\nKIT is implementing several specific initiatives to advance its decarbonization goals, including increasing renewable capacity through strategic acquisitions like the German Solar Portfolio (approximately 55,000 PV panels), European Onshore Wind Platform (275 MW), and Borkum Riffgrund 2 (465 MW). The company is also reducing emissions through operational changes such as decreasing the use of naphtha as town gas feed and implementing fleet electrification across its transportation services. KIT has developed strategic roadmaps that include installing high-efficiency systems and implementing solar power and electric vehicle conversions to reduce emissions and improve efficiency. These initiatives are supported by climate scenario analysis used to stress-test business resilience and inform decision-making processes.\n\nThe company's decarbonization strategy is underpinned by a strong governance framework where the Trustee-Manager's Board of Directors, supported by the Board ESG Committee (BEC), oversees sustainability matters. The Sustainability Committee implements the ESG strategy and reports on performance to the BEC, which meets quarterly to evaluate the effectiveness of KIT's ESG strategy, policies, and initiatives. KIT has integrated climate considerations into its Enterprise Risk Management framework to identify, assess, and monitor climate-related risks. The Trustee-Manager also leverages transition planning frameworks informed by international standards and Singapore's regulatory expectations to guide its decarbonization roadmap, ensuring alignment with evolving climate policies and market conditions.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several images, with most detailed information in the Environmental Stewardship section. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions reduction and renewable energy expansion with specific targets and timelines. The company has established concrete initiatives with measurable outcomes rather than just high-level commitments. Strategy is supported by robust governance structures and regular assessment mechanisms.",
      "status": null
    },
