    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Midas Safety's decarbonization strategy is firmly anchored in the Science Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) framework, with alignment to the 1.5°C pathway of the Paris Agreement. The company has established a clear trajectory toward net-zero emissions by 2050, with interim targets planned for 2030. In 2024, the company successfully surpassed its greenhouse gas emissions reduction targets in both absolute and per-unit terms, achieving significant reductions of 419 tons of CO₂e in Scope 1 emissions and 4,982 tons of CO₂e in Scope 2 emissions compared to the 2023 baseline. The strategy focuses on both operational emissions reduction and product lifecycle carbon footprint management, with increasing attention to Scope 3 emissions through supplier engagement.\n\nTo operationalize this strategy, Midas Safety implemented several concrete initiatives in 2024. The company added more than 4,000 Kilowatt of installed solar power capacity as a significant financial investment in renewable energy. A comprehensive product lifecycle assessment approach has been established, with the company completing 120 product carbon footprint calculations by Q4-2024. This includes third-party verification of estimation methods to ensure accuracy and reliability. The company also developed tools for carbon footprint estimation during the design phase, enabling real-time footprint measurements and supporting the development of products with progressively lower environmental impacts.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a systematic integration of carbon considerations into core business processes. Midas Safety is connecting with major suppliers to measure the carbon footprint of raw materials, targeting reductions in Scope 3 emissions. The company has established a clear timeline for continued progress, with plans to deploy carbon estimation tools across the organization by Q4-2025. Additionally, the company is preparing to set near-term 2030 targets alongside its Net Zero ambition for 2050, demonstrating a structured, phased approach to decarbonization that balances immediate action with long-term strategic vision.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 01, 08, and 36. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) while beginning to address Scope 3 through supplier engagement. Strong implementation details provided for 2024 including specific metrics, timelines, and technologies. Strategy includes concrete numbers (419 tons Scope 1, 4,982 tons Scope 2 reductions) and specific program names (Science Based Targets Initiative).",
      "status": null
    },
