      "summary": "NTT DATA's decarbonization strategy centers on the NTT DATA NET-ZERO Vision 2040, which was revised from 2050 to 2040 in fiscal 2023 and incorporates Science Based Targets (SBT) certification obtained in March 2024. The strategy follows a phased approach with specific, measurable milestones: achieving net-zero for Scope 1 and 2 emissions in data centers by 2030 (68% reduction compared to FY2021), across all company offices and facilities by 2035 (100% reduction), and for the entire supply chain (Scope 1-3) by 2040 (100% reduction). This comprehensive approach addresses both direct emissions from operations and indirect emissions across the value chain, with Scope 3 emissions targeted for a 42% reduction by 2030.\n\nTo implement this vision, NTT DATA conducts detailed climate change scenario analyses using frameworks like SSP1-1.9 and SSP5-8.5 to assess risks and opportunities. The company is accelerating its transition by promoting renewable energy deployment in data centers and offices globally, with specific focus on achieving net-zero in service use at data centers by fiscal 2030 and at offices by fiscal 2035. The company is also developing sustainability-related offerings linked to social systems and regulations, including IT services and systems that support sustainability initiatives.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, NTT DATA has established strategic partnerships through affiliations with key organizations including the Science Based Targets initiative, Business Ambition for 1.5°C, and the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures. The company is investing in joint R&D with external innovators, technical support, and training of engineers, while increasing investments in sustainability-related offerings from fiscal 2023 to fiscal 2025. These efforts are informed by scenario analysis that helps manage financial risks associated with carbon pricing and reputational damage.",
