      "summary": "Sino Land's 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based approach aligned with the 1.5°C pathway, building upon their net-zero carbon emissions commitment by 2050. The company has established concrete, near-term targets through their Sustainability Vision 2030 framework, including reducing absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 46.2% by FY2030 from the FY2019 baseline, and decreasing Scope 3 emissions from capital goods, fuel, energy-related activities, and waste by 51.6% per square foot by FY2030 from the FY2022 baseline. These specific targets were developed in collaboration with HKUST academics using the SBTi methodology, reflecting the latest climate science necessary to meet Paris Agreement goals.\n\nThe company is implementing a multi-faceted approach to achieve these targets through their Decarbonisation Blueprint, which includes optimizing properties and construction sites for energy efficiency and climate resilience during construction. Sino Land has engaged an external consultant to evaluate the resilience of over 170 existing and new properties under different climate scenarios, aligning with TCFD recommendations. They are also conducting in-depth financial impact analysis for key risks and opportunities, using scenario analysis that considers different climate-related scenarios including the NGFS Net Zero 2050 scenario and Current Policies scenario.\n\nTo support their strategy, Sino Land has joined the Science Based Targets Network's Corporate Program to collaborate with other organizations on developing tools and methodologies for nature-based targets. The company is also leveraging their Climate Action Report series to systematically address climate-related risks and opportunities across their operations. Their approach integrates climate considerations into financial planning and decision-making processes, with specific focus on building climate resilience as a core component of their decarbonization efforts.",
