      "summary": "Southern Company’s decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a balanced, reliability-focused transition in electric generation, prioritizing coal reduction, clean energy expansion, and modernized infrastructure. The company has significantly reduced coal capacity—from 20,457 MW (66 units) in 2007 to 8,523 MW (15 units) in 2024—while reshaping its annual energy mix to 18% coal, 49% natural gas, 19% nuclear, and 14% renewables/other by 2024. Core focus areas include optimizing natural gas use, expanding clean energy resources (nuclear, renewables, hydroelectric, renewable natural gas, and energy storage), and deploying modern energy distribution systems adaptable to evolving customer needs. The strategy emphasizes maintaining safety, reliability, and affordability throughout the transition, with a commitment to environmental impact considerations in all planning processes.  \n\nTo execute this approach, Southern Company implements concrete initiatives such as enhanced demand response and energy efficiency programs, continued investment in research and development for emerging clean energy technologies (including carbon capture, storage, sequestration, and advanced nuclear), and systematic assessment of coal-fired assets using environmental control technologies. The company’s integrated resource planning process, operational since 2008, ensures strategic resource deployment by regularly updating assumptions around load forecasts, GHG reduction pressures, fuel prices, and policy indicators. This process informs state-level integrated resource plans, new resource development, and retirement analyses, enabling a data-driven transition that balances short-term operational needs with long-term decarbonization goals.  \n\nSupporting these efforts, Southern Company navigates regulatory oversight from public service commissions (PSCs) and environmental agencies, which guide infrastructure evolution across jurisdictions. The company’s planning process accounts for regulatory frameworks while ensuring fleet transitions and infrastructure investments align with customer interests. By integrating scenario-based planning with regulatory compliance and technology innovation, Southern Company’s strategy demonstrates a structured, multi-faceted approach to reducing emissions while maintaining grid reliability.",
