    "strategy": {
      "summary": "TSH's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on integrating renewable energy sources, enhancing operational efficiency, and implementing circular economy principles to reduce carbon footprint across operations. The company has established a comprehensive approach that includes monitoring and managing Scope 1-3 emissions through a Group Corporate Greenhouse Gas Inventory based on the Greenhouse Gas Protocol for 2019-2024. The strategy prioritizes concrete actions over aspirational statements, with a focus on both direct emissions reduction and climate resilience building. TSH has completed a comprehensive re-assessment of material sustainability matters in FY2024, prioritizing 13 material matters and developing climate scenario analyses to assess potential risks related to climate change, informing business decisions and ensuring proactive adaptation.\n\nKey operational initiatives include the Bio-Integration Complex in Kunak, Sabah, which operates a 14 MW biomass co-generation power plant and a 3 MW biogas power plant that convert palm oil mill by-products (POM) and methane into renewable electricity. The company has also connected two mills in Indonesia to the PLN national grid, reducing diesel consumption while improving energy reliability. In FY2024, TSH generated 296,096 GJ of renewable energy, with 138,345 GJ utilized within operations and 154,307 GJ exported to the national grid. Waste management is integral to the strategy, with 99.90% of total waste diverted from disposal in FY2024, including 1,208,490 MT of biomass waste repurposed for energy generation and agricultural applications. Specific by-product utilization includes EFB as organic mulch, PKS and Fibres as biofuel in biomass boilers, and POME converted to biogas for renewable energy generation.\n\nTo strengthen climate resilience, TSH implements land-based initiatives including agroforestry programs that integrate reforestation with sustainable land use, planting various seedlings to enhance carbon absorption and soil health. The company also contributed to tree planting initiatives at Zoo Negara, planting three plant species that support carbon absorption and improve urban air quality. These efforts are supported by the company's Group Sustainability Policy and collaboration with organizations like Badan Pengelolaan Daerah Aliran Sungai (BPDAS) for seedlings. The strategy demonstrates a comprehensive approach that aligns operational needs with sustainability goals through concrete actions, with a focus on energy efficiency, renewable energy adoption, and circular economy principles.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across sustainability report pages. Strategy includes specific implementation details with measurable outcomes and concrete initiatives rather than just high-level commitments. Strategy focuses on operational emissions reduction through renewable energy adoption, waste repurposing, and land-based climate resilience initiatives. Governance mechanisms including GHG inventory and climate scenario analyses support the strategy.",
      "status": null
    },
