    "strategy": {
      "summary": "United Group's decarbonization strategy for 2024 is built on science-based targets validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), with a clear pathway toward net-zero greenhouse gas emissions across the value chain by 2040. The company has set ambitious near-term targets including reducing absolute scope 1 and 2 emissions by 90% by 2030 from a 2020 base year, and using 100% renewable electricity from 2027 onward. Their approach centers on three key pillars: renewable energy transition, operational efficiency improvements, and supply chain engagement, with specific commitments to ensure that 50% of supplier spend is with suppliers formally committed to SBTi-validated carbon reduction targets by 2030.\n\nThe company is implementing concrete initiatives across its operations to achieve these targets. In 2024, United Group has prioritized renewable electricity procurement, purchasing over 250GWh of high-quality Guarantees of Origin (GOs) through the European Energy Certificate System. They've deployed building optimization measures including LED energy-saving light fixtures at 40 locations, HVAC system upgrades, and consolidation of operational sites, resulting in significant energy savings. The company has also invested in renewable energy production, including large-scale solar and wind projects in Bulgaria with a combined peak capacity of 120 MWp, and small-scale solar panels producing over 700MWh of green electricity in Serbia, Slovenia, and Bulgaria. Current renewable electricity percentages range from 41% to 94% across different operating companies, with United Cloud leading at 94%.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a robust governance framework that integrates climate risk assessments into the Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) framework, following Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) recommendations. The company conducts annual climate scenario analysis across multiple risk types and timeframes to evaluate business resilience. United Group has also established strategic partnerships with organizations including the Science Based Targets initiative, European Green Digital Coalition, and Responsible Business Alliance to advance its decarbonization efforts and leverage collective expertise in sustainable practices.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across environmental performance and responsible governance sections. Strategy focuses on operational emissions with specific targets and implementation details. Includes both short-term actions (2024) and long-term targets (2030, 2040). Strategy includes specific metrics, technologies, and partnership details rather than being purely aspirational.",
      "status": null
    },
