    "strategy": {
      "summary": "AAK's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a comprehensive Science-Based Targets (SBTi) approach aligned with limiting global warming to 1.5°C. The company developed detailed decarbonization roadmaps for raw materials and submitted Scope 1, 2, and 3 non-FLAG targets to SBTi for approval. Their strategy spans the entire value chain, with specific targets including a 50% reduction in absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 2030 from a 2019 base year, a 46% reduction in Scope 3 non-FLAG emissions, and a 23% reduction in Scope 3 FLAG emissions by the same timeframe. AAK is also working toward 100% renewable electricity procurement by 2025, having already achieved a 9% increase in renewable electricity sourcing during 2022.\n\nTo implement this strategy, AAK developed specific action plans including decarbonization roadmaps for key raw materials, with palm, palm kernel, coconut, and rapeseed covering 80% of emissions in their upstream supply chain. The company is progressing toward 100% traceability to plantation and verified deforestation-free palm oil by 2025, partnering with Satelligence for satellite mapping of coconut production areas in the Philippines and Indonesia. Additionally, AAK committed to ensuring 10% of suppliers by emissions covering purchased goods and services will have science-based targets by 2027.\n\nAAK's strategy includes specific initiatives to address emissions from land use through the FLAG (Forest, Land and Agriculture) framework. In 2023, they planned to submit Scope 3 FLAG targets following the new standard launched in September 2022. The company also completed climate risk assessments for operations and raw materials, implementing the TCFD framework to identify and manage climate-related risks across their value chain. These efforts support their broader commitment to building climate resilience while reducing their carbon footprint.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 16-18, 22-24, 47. Strategy focuses on science-based targets with detailed implementation roadmap. Strategy includes specific initiatives for Scope 1-3 emissions, FLAG guidance, and supply chain engagement. Implementation details provided for 2022 activities with clear 2023-2030 targets.",
      "status": null
    },
