    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Hong Leong Bank's decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on a structured net zero pathway with specific, measurable targets across multiple time horizons. The bank updated its climate pledge in FY2022 to commit to achieving net zero carbon emissions by 2050, establishing a clear roadmap with a baseline year of FY2019, a short-term target of 15-25% reduction in GHG emissions by 2026, and a medium-term target of net zero for operational emissions (Scope 1 and 2) by 2030. The strategy focuses on two complementary approaches: enabling customers to transition to a low carbon economy through green financing solutions while simultaneously reducing the bank's own environmental impact.\n\nThe bank is implementing concrete initiatives across multiple fronts to advance its decarbonization goals. In FY2022, it approved over RM 2.4 billion in renewable energy financing, surpassing its five-year target of RM 500 million, and established an additional RM 1.5 billion target for renewable energy projects by FY2025. It launched a Green Bond Framework and issued its first Green Additional Tier 1 Bond worth RM 900 million in April 2022, marking a key milestone as the first issuance of a green AT1 bond by a Malaysian bank. The bank achieved a 6% reduction in Scope 2 emissions through Energy Efficiency & Conservation measures and embarked on a carbon offsetting project with the Malaysian Nature Society to plant approximately 50,000 mangrove trees in Kuala Selangor Nature Park. Additionally, the bank is developing a framework to measure customers' carbon footprints and establish a baseline for Scope 3 financing portfolio emissions by the end of FY2024.\n\nSupporting these initiatives are comprehensive governance structures and workforce engagement programs. The bank actively participates in the Joint Committee on Climate Change (JC3) and contributed to developing the BNM Climate Change Preparedness Tool (CCPT) and the Malaysian TCFD Application Guide. To build internal capacity, over 8,000 employees completed mandatory sustainability e-learning courses, and 1,875 new hires received sustainability training as part of onboarding. The bank also launched the HLB Sustainability Expert Engagement Session and the HLB Employee CSR Programme to foster a culture of environmental responsibility. These efforts are organized around five pillars: Environment, Food Security, Festive (Community), Financial Literacy, and Social Enterprise, creating an integrated approach to decarbonization that combines operational changes with stakeholder engagement and industry leadership.",
      "notes": "Comprehensive multi-page strategy section found across images 2, 3, 8, and 9. Strategy includes specific targets, concrete initiatives, and supporting mechanisms. The bank demonstrates a structured approach with clear short-term, medium-term, and long-term goals with measurable outcomes. Focus is on both operational emissions reduction and enabling customer transition to low carbon economy through green financing.",
      "status": null
    },
