    "strategy": {
      "summary": "RHB Banking Group's decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on a dual approach: reducing its own operational emissions while influencing the emissions profile of its financed activities through strategic financial decisions. The cornerstone of this strategy is the Group Climate Action Programme (GCAP), launched in the first quarter of 2022 and implemented over a two-year period. GCAP establishes clear targets of achieving carbon-neutral operations by 2030 and developing a pathway to net zero by 2050. Phase 1 of GCAP, completed in 2022, focused on climate risk management, ambition setting, and blueprint benchmarking against industry best practices and regulatory requirements. The company is now in Phase 2 of implementation, which covers the end-to-end spectrum of climate risk strategy, governance, risk management, and disclosure aligned with Bank Negara Malaysia's guidelines.\n\nTo drive decarbonization through its financial activities, RHB has implemented concrete policies including a formal stance against financing new thermal coal projects and the institutionalization of a No Peat, Deforestation, and Exploitation (NDPE) policy as part of its Group Credit Policy on Prohibited Credits. The company has extended over RM12 billion in Sustainable Financial Services as of December 2022, setting it strongly on track to mobilize RM20 billion in sustainable financial products and services by 2026. It has also enhanced its ESG Risk Assessment Tool (ERA) to better assess and manage climate risks in its portfolio, aligning it with BNM's Climate Change and Principles-based Taxonomy (CCPT).\n\nRHB has established a robust governance structure to ensure effective implementation of its decarbonization strategy. In August 2022, it formed a Board Sustainability Committee (BSC) comprising three Independent Non-Executive Directors and one Non-Executive Director to provide strategic oversight and integrate sustainability considerations into the Group's long-term corporate strategy. This is supported by the Group Sustainability Committee (GSC) and the Group Climate Action Programme Project Steering Committee (GCAP PSC), which work together to drive the integration of climate-related considerations into decision-making processes while monitoring progress toward carbon reduction targets.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several documents. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions and financed emissions as a financial institution. Strategy is detailed with specific programs (GCAP), concrete policies (NDPE), and clear governance structures. Implementation details are provided for both 2022 activities and future plans.",
      "status": null
    },
