    "strategy": {
      "summary": "IHH Healthcare Berhad's decarbonization strategy centers on establishing a science-based approach to reduce greenhouse gas emissions across their healthcare operations. In 2022, they focused on establishing accurate baselines for Scope 1 and 2 emissions, with verification starting at two IHH Singapore hospitals to ensure robust quantification and reporting. Their core strategy includes capping Scope 1 and 2 emissions at the 2022 baseline level by 2025 (inclusive of business growth) while simultaneously reducing carbon intensity per patient bed-day year-on-year. This dual approach allows for business growth while ensuring emissions do not increase. The company has established a clear 2022 baseline with total carbon footprint of 236,734.45 tCO2e, comprising Scope 1 emissions at 55,463.35 tCO2e and Scope 2 at 181,271.10 tCO2e, with a carbon intensity of 0.13 tCO2e per patient bed-day.\n\nTo operationalize this strategy, the company is implementing several concrete initiatives. They are collecting and analyzing energy usage data across their 83 hospitals in 10 countries to better manage consumption patterns. They're monitoring industry trends and emerging technologies to identify opportunities for energy efficiency improvements. The company has set a long-term target to achieve Net-Zero emissions by 2050 and is working toward Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) readiness by 2025, which will provide a scientifically validated pathway for emissions reduction. Supporting these efforts, they plan to establish Scope 3 emissions baselines across their value chain in 2023 and aim to have their sustainability report meet Task Force on Climate-Related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) standards by 2025. They're also rolling out sustainability awareness training modules in 2023 to engage their organization and evaluating collaborative opportunities to explore renewable energy sources in markets where they operate.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple report pages. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 and 2) with clear 2025 interim targets and 2050 Net-Zero goal. Strategy includes verification processes, science-based approach, and concrete implementation plans. The company has established specific metrics and is developing Scope 3 accounting.",
      "status": null
    },
