    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Kenanga Investment Bank Berhad's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on operational efficiency improvements and systematic climate risk integration across business functions. The bank has established concrete near-term targets with a commitment to achieve carbon neutrality by 2025 through transitioning operational energy needs from renewable sources, and Net Zero emissions by 2050 as its long-term goal. Their approach focuses on reducing the organization's direct carbon footprint while incorporating climate risk considerations into investment decisions and business operations through their established CCRM Framework, which was aligned with BNM's CCPT in 2021.\n\nIn 2022, the bank implemented specific, measurable decarbonization initiatives at their Kenanga Tower headquarters. These included upgrading Air Handling Unit (AHU) and Air Conditioning (AC) systems with multiple technical enhancements: upgrading the CH1 Centrifugal Chiller with Inverter Driven Screw Chiller, implementing Cooling Tower Fans for Systems 1 & 2, installing Inverter Driven Fan Motors, introducing enhanced sensors and monitoring devices, and implementing inverters to control motor speed based on demand. Additionally, they completed a full transition to LED lighting across all conventional lighting at Kenanga Tower, targeting an energy reduction of up to 8%. The bank also launched the #GreenAtHome initiative (previously #GreenAtWork), a month-long interactive campaign designed to educate employees on adopting environmentally-friendly mindsets and responsible resource usage.\n\nTo support these operational initiatives, Kenanga has established robust governance mechanisms including their Climate Change Risk Management (CCRM) Framework, which integrates climate risk assessment into investment processes through their Climate Change RAC. The bank actively participates in industry committees such as Bursa Malaysia's Sustainability Development Committee and the Joint Committee on Climate Change, while providing over 50 hours of ESG training across 18 courses in 2022. Their approach combines immediate operational improvements with strategic risk management to systematically reduce emissions while preparing for climate-related business transitions.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several documents. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) with specific 2022 implementation details. Limited Scope 3 information provided. Strategy includes concrete initiatives with measurable outcomes alongside longer-term targets.",
      "status": null
    },
