    "strategy": {
      "summary": "KPS Berhad's decarbonization strategy for 2022 is structured around a comprehensive 2022-2035 roadmap approved by the Board in August 2022, with 2024 specifically targeted as the year the Group commences GHG reduction measures. The company's approach addresses all three emission scopes (1, 2, and 3) through a phased implementation plan, aligning with Malaysia's national agenda to reduce emissions by 45% by 2030. The strategy emphasizes embedding sustainability into business operations while progressively enhancing climate-related initiatives across the organization. The roadmap positions climate action as a central pillar alongside social empowerment, capacity building, and sustainability reporting, establishing clear milestones through 2035 to guide the transition to a low-carbon economy.\n\nThe company is implementing specific operational initiatives to drive decarbonization, including redesigning and rethinking production processes to improve energy efficiency, transitioning to local procurement to minimize transportation emissions, and advancing decarbonization through renewable energy adoption. Additionally, KPS Berhad is actively switching to electric vehicles as part of its fleet modernization strategy. These concrete actions represent the initial phase of their sustainability journey, with the 2022-2024 period focused on fostering sustainable development by embedding ESG risks and opportunities into business strategy, culture, and risk frameworks across all departments and subsidiaries.\n\nTo support this transition, KPS Berhad has established robust governance structures, including the Sustainability Board Committee (SBC) that directly oversees implementation of sustainability policies and strategies. The Board Governance Risk Committee (BGRC) provides oversight for climate-related risk management, analyzing and mitigating business risks associated with climate change. This governance framework ensures that decarbonization efforts are integrated into the company's strategic planning process, with the Board conducting annual in-depth strategy reviews and requiring directors to attend sustainability training to build capacity for effective implementation.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 36-37, 38-39, and 80-81. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions with specific initiatives for energy efficiency, local procurement, renewable energy, and electric vehicle transition. The roadmap provides clear timelines with 2024 as the target year for commencing GHG reduction measures. Strategy includes governance structure specifically designed for climate action oversight.",
      "status": null
    },
