      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy centers on three integrated approaches: operational efficiency improvements, renewable energy adoption, and embedding climate considerations throughout business operations. The strategy emphasizes both adaptation and mitigation measures through concrete actions to cut greenhouse gas emissions, enhance infrastructure resilience, and drive continuous innovation. The company specifically addresses key climate risk areas including changing stakeholder demand for low-carbon products, emerging government policies and regulatory changes, and reputational risks from inadequate climate management. This comprehensive approach is designed to align with the Task Force on Climate-Related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) guidelines while responding to stakeholder expectations.\n\nThe company has implemented specific, measurable initiatives including expanding solar energy capacity by 135kWp across its operations and establishing year-on-year reduction targets for business units to decrease energy, water usage, and GHG emissions. Strategic investments in energy-efficient lighting, heating systems, and plant machinery form part of their infrastructure adaptation program. These efforts have yielded measurable results, with the company reporting a significant 40% reduction in GHG emissions intensity in the Plantation division (from 7.78 to 4.68 tCO2eq/RM million revenue) and notable improvements across other divisions in FYE2022. The renewable energy initiatives enabled the avoidance of 265 tCO2eq in FYE2022, equivalent to 32 homes' annual electricity use.\n\nTo support implementation, the company has integrated climate-related targets into Group MD's KPIs and established a dedicated Risk Steering Committee that considers climate risk as part of its key enterprise risk review. The company is also developing internal climate-risk reporting formats and climate-risk training programs to build organizational capability. The strategy identifies opportunities for developing new 'green' products and reducing operating costs through greater resource and energy efficiency, creating a dual benefit of emissions reduction and business value creation.",
