    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Malakoff Corporation's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a gradual, multi-pronged transition toward a low-carbon future through its Malakoff 2.0 Strategic Transformation. The company is pursuing three main pathways: expanding renewable energy capacity, decarbonizing existing thermal power plants, and enhancing waste management systems. The strategy is grounded in specific, measurable targets including achieving 1,400 MW of renewable energy capacity by 2031, reducing greenhouse gas emissions intensity by 30% by 2031 from a 2019 baseline, and reaching a 15-20% recycling rate by 2025. The company recognizes the need to balance energy security, affordability, and sustainability throughout this transition period.\n\nThe company implemented several concrete initiatives in 2022 to advance its decarbonization goals. It completed eight rooftop solar PV projects for commercial and industrial clients with a total capacity of 17.1 MWp, signed a solar PPA with Senai Airport for a 0.615 MWp facility, and secured 12 new solar PV projects totaling 10.4 MW. To address coal-based emissions, Malakoff conducted a successful 10-day trial at Tanjung Bin Power Plant using 1.5% biomass (oil palm empty fruit bunch pellets) as fuel and signed a Memorandum of Understanding with ITOCHU Corporation to study the feasibility of co-firing coal plants with hydrogen/ammonia. Additionally, the company launched an Inert Waste Management facility in Kuantan and partnered with Petronas Chemicals Group to repurpose plastic waste for food packaging and other applications.\n\nTo support these initiatives, Malakoff is leveraging digital technologies through its Digital Blueprint & Roadmap 2023-2037, implementing a Centralised Monitoring System that integrates waste management, asset facilities, and energy monitoring. The company is also exploring emerging technologies including battery energy storage systems (BESS), carbon-free mobility infrastructure, and virtual power purchase agreements. Malakoff's strategy emphasizes partnerships with industry players, government entities, and technology providers to accelerate its decarbonization journey while maintaining energy reliability and affordability for consumers.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple report pages. Strategy details specific initiatives with concrete metrics and timelines. Includes both operational changes and technology investments. Strategy acknowledges the need for gradual transition while balancing energy security and affordability.",
      "status": null
    },
