    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Maybank's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a three-pillar approach aligned with its Net Zero by 2050 goal, with specific focus on reducing both operational and financed emissions. The bank established its Scope 3 financed emissions baseline, becoming the first bank in Malaysia to identify a transition strategy that shapes its future business portfolio. The strategy emphasizes client partnership in decarbonization, accelerated sustainable financing, and industry leadership development. Maybank committed to mobilizing RM80 billion in sustainable finance by 2025, recognizing the financial sector's critical role in directing capital toward green and sustainable activities, while targeting carbon neutrality for its Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2030.\n\nThe bank implemented concrete initiatives across multiple markets to support its decarbonization goals. In Malaysia, Maybank launched the Solar Panel Financing Campaign in partnership with Petronas, offering preferential financing for staff to install solar panels, and introduced preferential rates for electric and hybrid vehicle financing. Singapore saw the relaunch of the Green Home Loan based on BCA Green Mark GoldPLUS standards, while Indonesia featured collaboration with Hyundai Motor Indonesia for electric vehicle financing. Maybank also established the Sustainable Product Framework (SPF) in September 2022 to classify and report sustainable financial products, and introduced innovative offerings like the first-in-Malaysia insurance coverage for EV home chargers and the 'Drive Less Save More' initiative providing rebates for reduced driving.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, Maybank strengthened its governance structure through Board-level climate oversight, with the Board Sustainability Committee (BSC) overseeing climate-related considerations. The bank conducted climate risk assessments for key sectors and provided climate-related training for Board members. Executive remuneration was linked to sustainability KPIs, ensuring climate considerations were integrated into leadership incentives. Maybank achieved significant progress in 2022, reducing Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 41% against the 2019 baseline, exceeding its annual target of 40% reduction. The bank also mobilized RM20.69 billion in sustainable finance in FY2022, surpassing its annual target of RM9 billion, demonstrating concrete progress toward its decarbonization commitments.",
      "notes": "Comprehensive multi-page strategy section found across multiple pages. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scopes 1 & 2) and financed emissions (Scope 3). Contains specific initiatives with country-specific implementations and measurable outcomes. Strategy is well-structured with three clear pillars and supporting governance mechanisms. Includes concrete financial targets and implementation details.",
      "status": null
    },
