      "summary": "OSK's decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on a comprehensive approach integrating renewable energy adoption, operational efficiency improvements, and ecosystem-based carbon sequestration. The company established an emissions baseline and began tracking Scope 1 (1,934.0 metric tonne CO2e) and Scope 2 (18,184.6 metric tonne CO2e) emissions in 2022, creating a foundation for future reduction efforts. The strategy aligns with Malaysia's target of net-zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050 as outlined in the 12th Malaysia Plan (2021-2025), with specific focus on transitioning toward a low-carbon economy while maintaining business resilience.\n\nThe company implemented a multi-faceted operational strategy beginning with a Group-wide solarisation initiative launched in 2021. This included completing the Olympic Cable factory in Melaka (May 2021) and expanding solar installations to OSK Property sales galleries in Puchong, Iringan Bayu, and Sungai Petani, as well as Plaza OSK. OSK targeted increasing solar power capacity to over 1.8 MWp to enhance utility savings and carbon avoidance. The company also promoted green practices through integrated building design, harvested rainwater utilization, and active efforts to minimize resource consumption across business operations. Additionally, OSK began nurturing trees in parks as natural carbon sequesters and prepared to include Scope 3 emissions (employee commute) in its reporting starting from the 2023 financial year.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, OSK engaged in strategic ecosystem conservation through the preservation of the Iringan Bayu Wetland Park, recognizing wetlands as critical carbon sinks that trap carbon dioxide through natural processes. The company also aligned with national sustainability frameworks by supporting the launch of Bursa Carbon Exchange (December 2022) and preparing for the Enhanced Sustainability Reporting Framework announced by Bursa Malaysia, ensuring its decarbonization strategy remains integrated with evolving regulatory requirements and market mechanisms.",
