    "strategy": {
      "summary": "PETRONAS Chemicals Group (PCG) has established a comprehensive decarbonization strategy centered around its Net Zero Carbon Emissions (NZCE) 2050 Roadmap, which was developed in 2021 with specific interim targets: 20% emission reduction by 2030, more than half by 2040, and net zero by 2050. The company's approach is structured around a four-stage reduction pathway: Operational Optimisation (~15-25% reduction), Asset Decarbonisation (~50-60% reduction), Switching to Renewables (15% reduction), and Carbon Offset (10% reduction). In 2022, PCG published its first Task Force on Climate-Related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) standalone report, applying the four key TCFD recommendations—Governance, Risk Management, Strategy, and Metrics & Target—to manage climate-related risks and opportunities. The company has enhanced its Sustainability Agenda with a 'Sustainability at the Core' aspiration to better embed climate action across the organization and established dedicated governance structures including the Board Sustainability and Risk Committee (BSRC) and Sustainability and Risk Management Committee (SRMC).\n\nPCG is implementing several concrete initiatives to achieve its decarbonization goals. At the operational level, the company is implementing fuel and steam optimisation, power consumption conservation, Advanced Process Control (APC), and Real-Time Optimizer (RTO) systems across manufacturing plants. The company has initiated low carbon technology assessments and installed solar panels on asset rooftops to evaluate renewable energy integration. For long-term decarbonization, PCG is assessing the feasibility of carbon capture, utilisation & storage (CCUS) integration with current and future assets. The company is also conducting detailed assessments of Scope 3 emissions across 15 categories to develop accurate baselines and identify reduction opportunities across the supply chain.\n\nTo support its decarbonization journey, PCG is evaluating various low carbon transition opportunities including carbon capture, utilisation & storage, circular economy through chemical recycling, and sustainable low carbon products such as bio-based and renewable-based products. The company is also enhancing its reporting framework by aligning with international standards including the Greenhouse Gas Protocol, IPIECA Climate Change Reporting Framework, and ISO 14064-1:2018. PCG has integrated climate risk identification and management into its Corporate Risk Profile and is leveraging digitalization to track and optimize energy consumption in real-time, translating directly into GHG emissions reduction.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several pages of the sustainability report. Strategy details specific reduction pathways with percentage targets and concrete implementation initiatives. The company focuses on both operational emissions reduction and Scope 3 emissions management. The strategy is supported by governance changes, technology adoption, and alignment with international standards.",
      "status": null
    },
