      "summary": "Reach Subsea’s decarbonization strategy in 2022 emphasizes technological innovation and strategic diversification to reduce emissions and transition toward renewable energy production. A central initiative is the development of unmanned vessels, which aim to cut emissions by 90-100% while lowering client costs, with the first two vessels fully funded for a 2023 launch targeting the 2024 high season. This effort is part of the Reach Remote project, positioned as the industry’s future to advance zero-emission goals. The company also expanded into non-Oil & Gas sectors—specifically offshore wind, subsea power cabling, tidal turbines, subsea mining, and offshore aquaculture—to reduce reliance on fossil fuels and capitalize on renewable energy opportunities, recognizing that 82% of its 2022 turnover came from the Oil & Gas segment. \n\nTo operationalize this transition, Reach Subsea acquired Octio to provide environmentally friendly solutions for monitoring carbon storage reservoirs below the ocean floor, directly supporting carbon management efforts. The company prioritized competence building and technological advancement to retain skilled employees during the sector shift, with the Board of Directors and Group Management actively monitoring organizational capabilities. By increasing engagement in offshore wind projects and leveraging the Reach Remote initiative, the company aims to reduce its Oil & Gas segment activity (which comprised 70% of project days in 2022) and secure long-term competitiveness in emerging renewable markets. \n\nThese initiatives are underpinned by a structured approach to competence development and strategic partnerships, ensuring assets and expertise remain relevant in a transitioning energy landscape. The company’s focus on measurable progress—such as the unmanned vessels’ emission reduction targets and sector diversification—reflects a commitment to moving beyond aspirational goals toward actionable decarbonization pathways.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across CEO Foreword and Environment section. Strategy focuses on operational emissions reduction through technological innovation (unmanned vessels, Octio acquisition) and sector diversification into renewables. Specific initiatives with timelines (e.g., 2023 vessel launch) and sector targets provided, though implementation details beyond project scope are limited.",
