    "strategy": {
      "summary": "RHB's decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on a dual approach: reducing its own operational carbon footprint while supporting customers' transition to low-carbon practices. The company established a clear timeline with its commitment to achieve carbon-neutral operations by 2030 and develop a pathway to net zero by 2050, formalized through the 'Pathway to a Climate-Resilient Future' sub-pillar. A key component of this strategy is the Group Climate Action Programme (GCAP), which was advanced in 2022 with Phase 1 completed in Q2 and Phase 2 launched in November. GCAP Phase 2 focuses on calculating Scope 3 financed emissions baseline to identify key high-emitting clients and sectors, developing strategic pathways for sector decarbonization, and creating commercial opportunities for clients to accelerate their decarbonization efforts. The company also implemented a 'No Deforestation, No Peat and No Exploitation (NDPE)' stance effective January 2022, restricting support to only responsible companies in key sectors like Palm Oil, Forestry and Agriculture.\n\nTo reduce operational emissions, RHB is implementing concrete initiatives including energy/carbon audits, energy optimization through equipment retrofit and renewable energy installation, and promoting virtual meetings and remote working to minimize energy consumption. The company is also developing its climate risk management framework to integrate climate-related risks into its risk management processes, with specific focus on both physical risks (from climate events) and transition risks (from economic shifts). Supporting these efforts, RHB has committed to mobilizing RM20 billion in sustainable financial products and services by 2026, building on its existing RM5 billion Green Financing Commitment by 2025.\n\nRHB's governance structure for decarbonization was significantly enhanced in 2022 with the establishment of the Board Sustainability Committee (BSC) in August, the appointment of a Group Chief Sustainability & Communications Officer in May, and implementation of a RACI Framework for sustainability governance. These organizational changes ensure strategic oversight at the highest level while enabling effective implementation across business units. The company is also aligning its climate-related financial disclosures with TCFD recommendations, demonstrating transparency in its decarbonization journey while developing the necessary capabilities to measure, monitor, and report on climate performance.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 12, 15, 21, 25, 26, 37, 38, 45, 54, and 55. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions reduction and financed emissions management. Strategy includes specific initiatives with timelines and governance structure. GCAP program is the central implementation mechanism with clear phases. Limited details on specific technologies or exact emission reduction targets beyond the 2030 carbon-neutral goal.",
      "status": null
    },
