    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Sarawak Energy's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based approach aligned with the Paris Agreement, focusing on both operational transformation and regional leadership. The company has committed to achieving net zero carbon emissions by 2050 and is actively working toward the 1.5°C business ambition through science-based targets validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi). In 2022, they reported that their Scope 1 Main Grid CO₂ emissions intensity of 0.199 tCO₂eq/MWh was 77% lower than the global average of 450 gCO₂eq/kWh, demonstrating significant progress in reducing emissions intensity while maintaining reliable electricity supply.\n\nThe company's strategy implementation includes specific technological initiatives and research projects. Sarawak Energy progressed several R&D projects including a Microalgae Production Facility with carbon capture and utilization at Sejingkat Power Corporation, a Containerised Solar Hydrogen Research Project in collaboration with PESTECH Energy, and research on Balingian's fly ash utilization with Swinburne Sarawak. The company has invested more than RM10 billion in low-carbon generation technologies, with 74% of their 2022 generation mix coming from renewable sources (24,168 GWh), primarily hydroelectric power. They also successfully completed the Tanjung Kidurong Combined Cycle Power Plant and are progressing the 1,375MW Mentarang Induk HEP in North Kalimantan to support Indonesia's Tanah Kuning Green Energy Park.\n\nSarawak Energy's decarbonization approach extends beyond operational changes to include strategic partnerships and regional integration. The company is exploring opportunities to export up to 1,000MW of electricity to Singapore, demonstrating their commitment to regional clean energy collaboration. They have also established comprehensive monitoring systems for Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions in accordance with global standards, with specific targets to reduce emissions intensity further. The company's transmission network expansion, including eight transmission projects completed in 2022, supports their transition to a more integrated and efficient low-carbon energy system across Sarawak.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 110-111, 132-133, and 138-139. Strategy focuses on science-based targets, renewable energy expansion, and specific R&D projects. Strategy includes detailed emissions data and specific initiatives rather than just high-level commitments. The company has already achieved their 2°C target and is working toward the 1.5°C target with specific investment figures (RM10+ billion) and measurable outcomes.",
      "status": null
    },
