      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy is structured around a formal Climate Change Policy that supplements their broader Sustainability Policy, creating a mandate for the Group to adapt to climate-related risks and mitigate GHG emissions. This policy establishes a comprehensive framework for emissions measurement and reporting across all scopes, with particular emphasis on understanding their carbon footprint through detailed assessment of energy-intensive business segments. The strategy centers on three key pillars: achieving Net Zero emissions, adopting renewable energy and green technologies where operationally feasible, and aligning with the TCFD framework to establish meaningful near- and medium-term emission reduction targets. The company recognizes the critical importance of climate resilience as part of their overall business strategy, with climate-related risk management falling under the purview of the Board of Directors supported by the Sustainability Steering Committee.\n\nTo implement this strategic approach, the company has established systematic emissions tracking across all business divisions, measuring Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions to identify priority areas for intervention. They have conducted carbon footprint assessments specifically for their most energy-intensive business segments, which has enabled them to set emission reduction targets. The organization is actively working to improve their GHG emissions reporting practices while integrating climate considerations into their operational decision-making. Their emissions data shows they are tracking progress year-over-year, with Scope 2 emissions representing the majority of their total emissions footprint.\n\nThe company's strategy emphasizes practical implementation where feasible, focusing on adopting renewable energy solutions and green technologies within their operations. They have embraced risk mitigation strategies that include continuous improvement of emissions reporting and the introduction of specific emission reduction initiatives. While the strategy outlines clear direction and measurement frameworks, specific implementation details beyond the reporting period and concrete project-level timelines for decarbonization initiatives are not fully elaborated in the provided materials.",
