    "strategy": {
      "summary": "RHB's 2022 decarbonization strategy follows a comprehensive two-pronged approach addressing both operational emissions and financed emissions. The company committed to achieving carbon-neutral operations by 2030 and developing a pathway to net zero by 2050, with the Group Climate Action Programme (GCAP) serving as the core implementation vehicle. In November 2022, the company launched GCAP Phase 2, which spans two years and addresses four key dimensions: Governance and Strategy, Risk Management, Disclosures, and Enablers. The strategy explicitly prohibits financing for new thermal coal mine projects and coal-fired power plant projects effective from 2022, while adopting a No Deforestation, No Peat and No Exploitation (NDPE) stance for relevant sectors including Palm Oil, Forestry and Agriculture.\n\nTo reduce operational emissions, RHB implemented specific initiatives including energy/carbon audits, equipment retrofitting, replacement of old infrastructure, and installation of renewable energy systems. The company also promoted virtual meetings, remote working, and energy-saving campaigns to minimize its carbon footprint. Simultaneously, RHB is calculating its Scope 3 financed emissions baseline to identify high-emitting clients and sectors, with the aim of developing strategic pathways for sector decarbonization. The company has mobilized RM12 billion in sustainable financial services as of December 2022, working toward its RM20 billion target by 2026, while maintaining a RM5 billion Green Financing Commitment through 2025 to support the transition to a low-carbon economy.\n\nThe decarbonization strategy is supported by robust governance structures including the Board Sustainability Committee (BSC) established in August 2022 and the Group Sustainability Committee (GSC). RHB also engaged with targeted customer segments to better understand their decarbonization strategies and provide financial support for their transition plans. The company's approach aligns with regulatory expectations from BNM, the Securities Commission, and Bursa Malaysia, while integrating climate considerations into risk management frameworks and financial decision-making processes.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 12, 25, 37, 38, 45, 55. Strategy focuses on both operational and financed emissions with specific implementation phases. GCAP Phase 2 launched in November 2022 with concrete actions for operational footprint reduction. The strategy includes both prohibitions (thermal coal) and positive actions (green financing).",
      "status": null
    },
