    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Top Glove's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on establishing a robust foundation for measuring and reducing carbon emissions across its operations. The company refined its emissions data calculation methodology in line with GHG Protocol guidelines, recalibrating its base year from FY2021 to FY2022 for more accurate carbon emissions tracking. This refinement included specific changes: removing 'Biomass' from Scope 1 (as it's considered carbon neutral), adding 'Petrol & Diesel' and 'Fleet Vehicles' to Scope 1 for transportation fuels, including Top Glove Tower electricity consumption in Scope 2, and adding 'Employee Commuting' to Scope 3 emissions. These changes demonstrate a comprehensive approach to accurately measuring emissions across all relevant categories.\n\nThe company implemented concrete operational initiatives in 2022 to reduce its carbon footprint. Top Glove achieved a 56.9% reduction in paper usage (to 27,907kg), significantly exceeding its 20% target of reducing to 50,400kg. The company also made progress on material consumption reduction, with 50% of latex suppliers receiving Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) certification, supporting responsible material sourcing. Additionally, Top Glove began exploring alternative materials and methods for stretch film packing to reduce virgin plastic resin usage, with a specific target of 40% reduction. These initiatives reflect a practical approach to decarbonization through operational efficiency and sustainable material selection.\n\nSupporting these efforts is a structured governance framework. The Board Sustainability Committee (BSC), established in March 2019, provides oversight of sustainability strategy, while the Sustainability Steering Group (SSG) comprising all department heads holds operational responsibility. This structure ensures decarbonization efforts are integrated across the organization and regularly monitored. Top Glove has also committed to submitting net zero carbon targets to the Science Based Target initiative (SBTi) by FY2024 and establishing its Net Zero Carbon initiative (NZTI) Roadmap in the same year, demonstrating a clear pathway toward long-term carbon reduction.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across environmental and governance sections. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions measurement and reduction with specific 2022 achievements. Implementation details provided for paper reduction, material sourcing, and emissions tracking methodology. Governance structure supports decarbonization efforts with clear oversight mechanisms.",
      "status": null
    },
