    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Tune Protect Group’s 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on reshaping its investment and underwriting portfolio to align with low-carbon growth while integrating climate risk management into core operations. The company prioritized exiting hydrocarbon-dependent sectors, including oil, gas, and coal-related businesses, and redirected focus toward Health, Lifestyle, and SME segments. A key pillar of this approach was the formal commitment to phase out coal by 2030, which translated into concrete 2022 actions: amending underwriting and investment policies to exclude coal mining, coal-fired power plants, and coal power producers for future private mandates. By 2023, the company had ceased underwriting coal mining risks entirely and ensured two remaining coal-fired plant policies would expire without renewal. Additionally, the group excluded tobacco and weapons manufacturing industries, aligning with UN SDGs to support social responsibility and reduce exposure to harmful sectors.\n\nTo advance sustainable finance, Tune Protect allocated 10.5% of total investments to ESG-focused equity and fixed income assets in 2022, exceeding its target of up to 10% for sustainable funds. The company also developed climate-conscious insurance products to drive behavioral change, including the Pay-As-You-Drive (PAYD) program, which rewards reduced carbon footprints through usage-based premiums, and free personal accident coverage for electric vehicle (EV) owners to incentivize EV adoption. These initiatives were supported by a 19.24% share of gross earned premiums in 2022 from climate risk management products, such as flood coverage and hydro/solar energy production policies.\n\nThe strategy is underpinned by robust governance and partnerships. The Board-level Investment and Risk Management Committees oversee climate-related risks, while the company adopted TCFD recommendations for climate-related financial disclosures and joined Climate Governance Malaysia to strengthen climate governance. It also became a founding member of PIAM’s Climate Change Action Committee and committed to the UN Global Compact, leveraging collaborative platforms to share knowledge and align with national sustainability goals. These efforts collectively position Tune Protect to support Malaysia’s transition to a low-carbon economy while mitigating climate-related financial risks.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with specific 2022 actions (e.g., 10.5% ESG allocation, coal exclusion, PAYD implementation). Strategy covers portfolio restructuring, insurance innovation, governance, and partnerships, demonstrating a comprehensive approach beyond high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
