    "strategy": {
      "summary": "AmBank Group’s 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on enabling a low-carbon transition through targeted sectoral pathways, SME support, and rigorous emissions monitoring. The company is developing customized sectoral pathways for hard-to-abate industries—such as manufacturing, electricity, and gas—to gradually reduce financed emissions intensity, aligning with Malaysia’s National Energy Transition Roadmap (NETR) and Bank Negara Malaysia’s regulatory frameworks. A key focus is enterprise emissions management, with quarterly tracking of Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions and a detailed study underway to refine reduction strategies, aiming to validate and develop a transition plan for hard-to-abate sectors by FY2025 to achieve Net Zero by 2050. Additionally, the group targets ensuring at least 70% of its non-retail loan/financing portfolio (with limits of at least RM10 million) achieves low Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) Risk Ratings by FY2030, embedding climate risk into its core risk management framework.\n\nTo drive implementation, AmBank has launched several concrete initiatives. For SMEs, it provides GHG management tools through Bank Negara Malaysia’s Low Carbon Transition Fund and collaboration with Pantas Climate Solutions, alongside adopting the Capital Market Malaysia’s Simplified ESG Disclosure Guide to support ESG reporting. The AmBank BizCLUB Season 4 program focuses on sustainability and Industry 4.0 (IR4.0) for MSMEs, while partnerships with Bank Simpanan Nasional offer financial literacy and digital transformation training. The group also established an Enterprise Risk and Climate Risk Unit to monitor portfolio emissions and integrate climate risk into business continuity management (BCM), using licensed analytical tools to assess physical and transition risks across operations.\n\nSupporting these efforts, AmBank leverages strategic partnerships and governance structures to operationalize its strategy. It collaborates with entities like Bank Negara Malaysia and Pantas Climate Solutions to enhance SME decarbonization capabilities and integrates climate risk into its Board-approved Risk Appetite Statement (RAS). The group employs BNM’s Climate Risk Management and Scenario Analysis (CRMSA) framework for risk assessment, with findings informing its upcoming Net Zero Roadmap. By combining sector-specific pathways, SME empowerment, and data-driven risk management, AmBank aims to bridge the funding gap for sustainable projects while ensuring its financing portfolio aligns with global climate goals.",
      "notes": "Strategy is detailed across multiple pages with concrete initiatives (sectoral pathways, SME programs, emission targets), governance structures (Enterprise Risk Unit), and partnerships. Focus includes both operational (enterprise) and financed emissions, with specific FY2024 actions and FY2030 targets. Multi-page strategy section found with implementation details.",
      "status": null
    },
