      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a structured approach that integrates climate considerations into core business operations through a multi-tiered governance framework. The strategy focuses on active emissions management, renewable energy transition, and enhanced climate resilience, with specific attention to reducing GHG emissions across Scope 1, 2, and 3. Key focus areas include transitioning to renewable energy sources, improving energy efficiency, and implementing comprehensive climate risk assessments to identify material risks and opportunities.\n\nThe company has implemented several concrete initiatives to advance its decarbonization efforts. In 2024, it initiated a thorough climate-related risk and opportunities (R&Os) assessment aligned with ISSB IFRS S2 standards, using a structured prioritization framework that evaluates risks based on likelihood and financial impact, while assessing opportunities across desirability, occurrence, technical feasibility, and resource feasibility. The company is actively monitoring and reporting GHG emissions across all scopes, with specific emphasis on reducing operational carbon footprint through investments in green technologies and sustainable market expansion. Notably, renewable energy contributions from three solar projects increased by 75.9% despite an 8.4% rise in energy consumption to support business growth.\n\nTo support these initiatives, the company has established a robust governance structure where the Board drives strategic alignment and the Sustainability Committee (RSC) provides oversight. At the management level, the Group Sustainability Management Committee (GSMC) identifies and manages climate-related R&Os, while the Group Sustainability Technical Committee (GSTC) conducts risk assessments and develops emissions reduction strategies. This multi-tiered governance framework ensures that climate considerations are integrated into all levels of decision-making, from strategic planning to operational execution, creating a systematic approach to managing climate-related challenges while advancing decarbonization goals.",
