      "summary": "The company’s 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on reducing Scope 1 and 2 greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions through targeted operational efficiency improvements and renewable energy integration, underpinned by its long-term commitment to achieve net zero emissions by 2050. The approach prioritizes direct action on energy-intensive systems, recognizing that Scope 2 emissions (primarily from electricity consumption for air-conditioning and production machinery) and Scope 1 emissions (from company-owned vehicles) constitute the majority of its carbon footprint. By focusing on minimizing energy waste and accelerating the transition from fossil fuel dependence, the strategy aligns with its role as a responsible corporate citizen in addressing environmental impact from manufacturing operations.\n\nTo advance this, the company executed specific, measurable initiatives during the fiscal year ending December 2024. These include the completed implementation of auto-switching scheduling for Air-Conditioning (AHU) systems to reduce electricity use and GHG emissions, alongside in-progress efforts such as automated scheduling for water pumps, office lighting switches, and collaboration with technical experts to enhance energy-efficient induction motors with real-time monitoring. These initiatives directly target energy consumption reduction across critical infrastructure. Concurrently, the company expanded renewable energy adoption, evidenced by rooftop solar operations launched in September 2023, which contributed to a renewable energy consumption of 3,047.59 MWh in FYE December 2024, as reflected in its detailed energy consumption reporting.\n\nSupporting these actions, the company tracks energy metrics such as total and renewable consumption per build quantity, with methodology refinements ensuring accurate data transparency. While the strategy emphasizes near-term operational emissions reduction, it is structured to build momentum toward the 2050 net zero target through continuous improvement in energy management practices and scalable renewable energy integration.",
