    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Awantec’s decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on integrating climate action into operational frameworks through TCFD alignment, science-based target setting, and systematic risk management. The company measures and reports Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions to identify improvement areas, linking these metrics to departmental ESG key performance indicators (KPIs) to ensure accountability. This approach is anchored in the TCFD framework and the Paris Agreement’s 2°C goal, with science-based reduction targets driving emissions mitigation across all operations. By embedding climate considerations into core business processes, Awantec prioritizes transparency and data-driven decision-making to reduce environmental impact.  \n\nSpecific initiatives include a 10% reduction in total GHG emissions per employee (from 3.83 tCO₂e in FY2022 to 3.43 tCO₂e in FY2024) and a 25% reduction in energy intensity (to 1,694 kWh/employee), achieved through targeted energy efficiency programs. The company advanced TCFD integration by completing all thematic areas, including governance, strategy, and risk management, and implemented supply chain initiatives such as cloud migration and green screening. To assess climate risks, Awantec utilizes Representative Concentration Pathways (RCP) analysis to update risk assessments, identifying impacts on operations, expenses, and financial planning.  \n\nSupporting these efforts, the strategy emphasizes continuous improvement through phased targets: a 15% GHG reduction by FY2025 and 25% by FY2030, alongside energy intensity reductions of 10% and 20% over the same periods. By aligning decarbonization with ESG KPIs and leveraging RCP-based risk modeling, Awantec ensures climate action is woven into operational resilience, balancing immediate progress with long-term sustainability goals.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found; Strategy details operational emissions reduction with specific targets, progress metrics, and implementation mechanisms including TCFD integration and RCP-based risk assessment.",
      "status": null
    },
