      "summary": "Bursa Malaysia Berhad's decarbonization efforts in 2024 appear primarily focused on community-based renewable energy initiatives rather than a comprehensive corporate decarbonization strategy for their own operations. The company has implemented a concrete project installing 117 solar panels across five villages in indigenous Orang Asli communities in Perak and Sabah, specifically in Kg. OA Kepayang, Kg. OA Lapan, Batang Padang, and Ranau. This initiative, executed in May 2024 by Bursa VIBE volunteers alongside technical teams from Suncrox Malaysia and students from Kolej Vokasional Slim River, aims to improve electrification access in underserved communities through clean energy solutions. The company has also provided hands-on training for Bursa VIBE volunteers in solar panel installation and solar hybrid technology, equipping them with practical knowledge of solar PV systems, installation techniques, and maintenance procedures. While the company's Sustainable Supply Chain Management section mentions supporting climate resilience and advocating for 'efficient and sustainable supply chain practices to reduce environmental impact,' the provided materials do not disclose specific corporate decarbonization targets, comprehensive emission reduction plans, or detailed strategies for reducing the company's own operational carbon footprint. The solar panel installations represent community investment projects rather than elements of an integrated corporate decarbonization strategy.",
