    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Carlsberg Malaysia's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a structured, multi-year approach to eliminate carbon emissions from their brewery by 2030, with dual focus on carbon neutrality and renewable energy adoption. The company has established robust governance structures including the Risk Management and Sustainability Committee (RMSC), Chief Sustainability Officer (CSO), and the Sustainability Steering Committee (SSC) established in 2023 to drive sustainability-focused initiatives. Their strategy follows a three-phase transition approach (short, medium, and long term) to manage the transition to a low-carbon economy, with specific attention to both physical climate risks and transition risks. The company aligns its net-zero pathway with the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), focusing on reducing emissions before addressing any remaining carbon through removal or offsetting measures.\n\nThe company is implementing several concrete decarbonization initiatives in 2024. They have invested RM108 million in upgrading their state-of-the-art bottling line to optimize energy usage and reduce waste management, achieving zero waste to landfill. Additionally, they've installed a RM11.6 million new Beer Membrane Filtration System to reduce energy usage in processing operations, and invested RM80.4 million in a new energy-efficient canning line. They've also implemented a new Cleaning in Place (CIP) plant that centralizes tank cleaning to enhance energy efficiency and optimized groundwater purification to utilize less energy. The company is actively exploring renewable energy boilers and purchasing low-carbon electricity supply from TNB to reduce reliance on fossil fuels. For physical climate risks, they're allocating resources for infrastructure upgrades including flood-resistant buildings and drainage systems to address riverine and rainfall-driven flooding risks.\n\nTo support their decarbonization efforts, the company has begun collecting data for Scope 3 carbon emissions and aims to reduce value chain emissions per hectolitre by 30% by 2030 from a 2015 baseline. In 2024, they've achieved Cradle to Cradle Certified™ at the Silver level for better recycling, with over 95% of bottles collected from trade for recycling and recycled content reaching 60% and 50% in bottles and cans respectively. The company is also converting natural gas boilers to renewable energy boilers within the next two years and investing RM8 million in groundwater purification capacity to ensure water security. Their approach integrates climate considerations into business strategy, with specific mitigation efforts for both physical and transition risks across short, medium, and long-term horizons.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 93-106 of the report. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions and value chain emissions. Specific financial investments and implementation details provided for 2024 initiatives. Strategy includes both mitigation efforts for climate risks and proactive decarbonization initiatives. The company has moved beyond high-level commitments to concrete actions with specific investments and timelines.",
      "status": null
    },
