      "summary": "Deleum’s 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on a structured low-carbon transition, anchored by its refreshed sustainability framework and rigorous emissions accountability. The company has adopted an Operational Control approach to consolidate Scope 1 and 2 emissions data across all entities under direct operational control, ensuring 100% coverage of GHG emissions. This is integrated into a refreshed sustainability framework aligned with evolving EESG goals, with managing carbon footprint identified as a critical material matter among 17 prioritized focus areas. The strategy is formalized in the Sustainability Roadmap 2025-2029, which establishes interim targets for short-, medium-, and long-term climate action to address today’s challenges while building a legacy of responsible stewardship.\n\nSpecific initiatives include third-party verification of FY2024 Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by BSI, confirming data accuracy and alignment with ISO 14064 standards. The company is also aligning with Malaysia’s National Sustainability Reporting Framework (NSRF), launched in September 2024, to meet new climate-related disclosure requirements (CRRO and SRRO). These efforts ensure compliance with global EESG standards and transparent reporting, while the roadmap outlines actionable steps to reduce emissions and strengthen climate resilience across operations.\n\nSupporting mechanisms include reinforcing partnerships such as the CEO Action Network (initiated in FY2023) to drive industry-wide collaboration and consolidating energy and emissions data in line with TCFD/IFRS S2 recommendations. Additionally, Deleum is prioritizing investments in low-carbon technologies and renewable energy to advance decarbonization, while maintaining data governance and accuracy to inform strategic decisions. The company’s focus on operational emissions, verified reporting, and strategic partnerships forms a cohesive approach to achieving its net zero commitments.",
