      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on an integrated approach that combines forest protection with operational decarbonization, recognizing climate action as fundamental to long-term business resilience and growth. The strategy employs qualitative scenario analysis across business-as-usual and net-zero pathways, enabling assessment of climate-related risks and opportunities. This data-driven approach informs strategic decisions on capital allocation, operational resilience, and supply chain adaptation, with the goal of developing a transition plan that is both ambitious and operationally viable while maintaining business competitiveness.\n\nSpecific initiatives include significant investments in renewable energy, with a cumulative solar installation of 7.93 MWp and biomass boilers powered by cocoa shells that have successfully reduced reliance on grid energy. Renewable energy utilization increased by 90% to 126,057 gigajoules, with solar-powered electricity usage almost tripling since FY2023. The company has implemented a comprehensive energy management system to monitor and reduce energy waste, while enhancing supply chain traceability through active engagement with suppliers and local governments. A dedicated team in origin countries strengthens supplier assessments on deforestation and legality, and the GC&B Programme advances nature-based solutions through forest conservation and agroforestry initiatives in cocoa farms. The company is also gathering data to enhance the accuracy of Scope 3 emissions across the value chain, aligning with evolving standards and upcoming international climate disclosure requirements.\n\nSupporting these efforts is a robust governance structure where the Board oversees climate-related risks and opportunities, supported by the ERM Committee. The SSC, chaired by an executive director, manages these risks and incorporates them into business operations, while the Sustainability Department oversees all sustainability activities and supervises Sustainability Committees. In FY2025, the company plans to intensify its decarbonization strategy through market intelligence, regulatory landscape assessment, and solution feasibility analysis, with a dedicated Carbon Committee overseeing implementation while cross-functional teams execute mitigation strategies spanning energy efficiency, renewable energy adoption, and supplier engagement.",
