      "summary": "Kelington Group Berhad's decarbonization strategy for 2024 is structured around a comprehensive net zero transition pathway with clearly defined short, medium, and long-term targets. The company has established specific emissions reduction goals, including reducing Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 10% by 2030, lowering emission intensity by 5% by 2030 for its Industrial Gas Division, and cutting Scope 3 emissions by 10% by 2035. The strategy centers on transitioning to a low-carbon future through three phased approaches: short-term foundation building (2025-2030), medium-term decarbonization scaling (2031-2040), and long-term net-zero achievement (2041-2050), with a commitment to 100% renewable electricity for Malaysia operations by 2045 and net zero Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2050.\n\nTo achieve these targets, Kelington is implementing concrete initiatives across multiple fronts. In the short term, the company is monitoring energy efficiency across major facilities, increasing renewable energy adoption through on-site generation and procurement strategies, and collaborating with suppliers, customers, and partners to drive industry-wide decarbonization. For medium-term implementation, the company is identifying high-emission industrial hubs to partner with for large-scale carbon capture and storage projects, developing CO2 transport infrastructure, and establishing an internal carbon offset strategy. The long-term phase focuses on implementing on-site solar, wind, or PPAs to transition to fully renewable energy by 2045, mandating low-carbon sourcing requirements, and leading cross-sector partnerships to advance carbon-neutral technologies.\n\nSupporting this strategy, Kelington has already installed solar photovoltaic panels at its Shah Alam office since FY2011, with its FY2024 solar PV system generating 12,589 kWh of renewable energy. The company is leveraging data analytics to track and optimize energy consumption, conducting feasibility studies for mini and micro-hydro projects in Malaysia and ASEAN, and securing Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs) with green energy providers. Additionally, Kelington is collaborating with renewable energy providers, government agencies, and sustainability-focused investors to develop climate-friendly technologies while implementing Renewable Energy Certificates (RECs) to support its transition toward full renewable adoption.",
