      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a structured, asset-specific approach aligned with their Sustainability Plan 2030. The strategy is built around their 'Asset-by-Asset Decarbonisation Plan' which identifies carbon-lowering initiatives for each operating unit to achieve targeted 10% Scope 1 and 2 operational emissions reduction by 2030. In 2024, they are conducting a comprehensive materiality assessment of all 15 Scope 3 categories to ensure completeness and transparency of carbon emissions accounting while aligning with the National Sustainability Reporting Framework and updated Bursa Malaysia Main Market Listing Requirements. This approach follows their four-pillar framework (Planet, People, Peace and Prosperity) with specific focus on reducing greenhouse gas emissions and promoting decarbonization as Goal 1 of their sustainability strategy.\n\nThe company has already reduced energy consumption by 11% from their 2019 baseline, resulting in a corresponding 11% reduction in overall GHG emissions. To build on this progress, they are implementing several concrete initiatives including setting up internal carbon pricing on product and service procurement to identify lower carbon options, structuring tenancy and lease agreements to allocate carbon-related costs, and establishing climate-related disclosure protocols. They are also conducting physical and transition risk assessments using IEA scenarios (APS as low-carbon and STEPS as business-as-usual) to identify relevant transition drivers such as carbon pricing, renewable energy adoption, and compliance with building sector regulations.\n\nSupporting these efforts, the company has established a robust governance framework with the Sustainability Steering Committee (SSC) monitoring progress quarterly. They have also developed a comprehensive ESG training plan covering specific topics like GHG accounting, Human Rights, and Circular Economy to ensure all employees understand their role in decarbonization efforts. The company is actively working with partners in the KLCC Precinct to contribute toward the UN Sustainable Development Goals, while also conducting internal stakeholder consultations to evaluate the impact of transition drivers on their business operations and value chain.",
