      "notes": "Total fuel: Property/HQ (24137 L) + Plantation (18338 L) = 42475 L. Mobile fuel: Property/HQ petrol (6348 L) is mobile (company vehicles), Plantation diesel (18338 L) is mobile (vehicles/machinery). Property/HQ diesel (17789 L) partially mobile/stationary but not split. Used methodology: Mobile = Property/HQ petrol + Plantation diesel + (Property/HQ diesel * 50%) = 6348 + 18338 + (17789 * 0.5) = 24931 L. Stationary = Property/HQ diesel * 50% = 17789 * 0.5 = 8894.5 L? But note: Property/HQ diesel total 17789 L, and Plantation has no stationary. However, the report states Property/HQ diesel includes both mobile and stationary. Since exact split not provided, used proportional calculation based on typical industry practice (50% mobile, 50% stationary) as last resort per instructions. Fuel type breakdown: Petrol only in Property/HQ (6348 L), Diesel in both (17789 L + 18338 L = 36127 L).",
