      "summary": "MISC Berhad's decarbonization strategy centers on a structured, multi-phase transition plan aligned with IMO targets and their own 2050 net-zero commitment. The company has established clear short-term (2024-2027), medium-term (up to 2030), and long-term (2031-2050) horizons to reduce GHG intensity by 50% by 2030 and achieve net-zero emissions by 2050. Their approach focuses on fleet renewal, technology adoption, and value chain transformation across shipping and non-shipping operations, with particular emphasis on transitioning to dual-fuel vessels powered by LNG, ammonia, and other low-carbon alternatives while developing carbon capture and storage capabilities. The strategy integrates both operational efficiency improvements and investment in new energy solutions to maintain competitiveness during the energy transition.\n\nThe company is actively implementing several concrete initiatives to advance decarbonization. MISC has committed to deploying zero-carbon emission vessels by 2030 and is progressively renewing its fleet with high-efficiency LNG dual-fuel vessels, with plans to introduce ultra-low emissions ammonia vessels by or after 2027. They've formed strategic partnerships including a collaboration with Gentari to develop integrated shipping and floating solutions for ammonia, and participate in the CarbonStrike consortium (with PETRONAS, Samsung E&A, TechnipFMC, and Honeywell UOP) to provide carbon capture services across the Asia-Pacific region. MISC is also exploring ammonia as a marine fuel through potential ammonia carriers, floating production facilities, and bunkering hubs, while implementing energy-saving devices like propeller modifications and hull optimization for existing vessels.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a robust governance framework led by the NED (Nominations and Executive Development) committee, with oversight from the Board Sustainability & Risk Committee. The company has established the MISC Group Transition Plan with specific milestones for each timeframe, including fleet renewal, value chain reduction, and GHG removal technologies. MISC is investing in technological advancements for decarbonization, with a focus on developing low- to zero-carbon offshore assets and renewable energy solutions. Their strategy acknowledges the need for both immediate operational improvements and long-term investments in carbon capture and storage to address residual emissions, ensuring they maintain business continuity while transitioning to a low-carbon future.",
