    "strategy": {
      "summary": "RHB Bank's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a structured, data-driven approach to achieving Net Zero by 2050, with clear interim targets for 2030. The strategy is built around three strategic pillars: reducing financed emissions in high-impact sectors, driving growth in green financial services, and integrating sustainable practices into their own operations. The company has launched their Net Zero Strategy and Roadmap, focusing on accelerating the transition to a low-carbon economy while embedding sustainability at the core of their business operations. Their approach specifically targets five high-impact sectors: Energy Supply, Palm Oil, Oil & Gas, Property & Construction, and Transportation, with a 2030 target to achieve 20% reduction in financed emissions for the top five high-impact sectors within their business.\n\nTo support the transition to a low-carbon economy, RHB is mobilizing significant capital through targeted financial instruments. In 2024, they achieved RM17.8 billion in sustainable financing, with green financing reaching RM8.8 billion (50% of the total). The company has launched several innovative financing initiatives including the RM1 billion Sustainable Trade Finance Programme for renewable energy and energy efficiency projects, an RM400 million portfolio guarantee with RM100 million allocation for the Low Carbon Transition Facility, and Malaysia's first ESG Incentive Scheme offering up to RM4,000 in financial rewards for SMEs. They have cumulatively mobilized RM5.3 billion to support SMEs' transition through product bundling and have achieved zero coal exposure as of December 2024.\n\nThe company is also decarbonizing its own operations, having reduced operational greenhouse gas emissions by 45.5% from baseline through energy efficiency measures and increased renewable energy adoption. With 930 kWp of solar capacity already installed across two main premises and 20 branches, they plan further installations in 2025 to achieve carbon neutrality by 2030. Their comprehensive approach is supported by robust governance structures including a Board Sustainability Committee and Group Sustainability Committee, along with active stakeholder engagement through industry partnerships such as the Joint Committee on Climate Change (JC3).",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 10, 16, 28, 37, 46, 47, 66, 75, 104, and 105. Strategy focuses on financed emissions reduction and green financial services growth with specific 2030/2050 targets. Implementation details provided for 2024 including specific financing amounts and operational emission reductions. Strategy includes concrete initiatives with measurable outcomes rather than just high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
