    "strategy": {
      "summary": "S P Setia Berhad's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a structured, science-based approach to achieve net zero emissions by 2050, with clear interim targets for Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions. The company has established 2024 as the baseline year for emissions tracking and committed to a 45% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 carbon emissions by 2030 and 70% by 2040. For Scope 3 emissions, they target a 20% reduction in embodied carbon emissions (measured by intensity) by 2030 for landed properties. The strategy is grounded in the GHG Protocol framework with specific baselines of 487 kgCO₂e/m² for landed properties and 1,044 kgCO₂e/m² for high-rise properties, and incorporates Malaysia-specific climate data for scenario analysis to identify physical and transition risks.\n\nThe company is implementing several concrete initiatives to drive emissions reduction. They established the eDew system in 2024 to digitalize emissions data collection and monitoring across business units, enhancing accuracy and transparency. The Setia eGreenLiving initiative integrates EV-ready infrastructure, solar panel installations, and energy-efficient building designs across developments. Their sustainable landscaping approach prioritizes native plants, green corridors, and water-efficient practices like rainwater harvesting, while composting vegetation waste for fertilizer use. The company also implemented the Setia Biodiversity Policy (to be finalized by mid-2025) and introduced Tree Planting Guidelines for Carbon Sequestration aligned with IUCN Red List standards.\n\nTo support this strategy, S P Setia has established a comprehensive governance framework with the Sustainability Committee overseeing strategy and targets, and the Sustainability Working Group implementing ESG initiatives across business units. The company is aligning with TCFD recommendations and progressively adopting IFRS S2 standards for climate-related financial disclosures. Their climate risk assessment process, embedded within the Enterprise Risk Management Framework, evaluates both physical and transition risks through scenario analysis, with specific attention to heat impacts in coming decades. The Setia Green Roadmap provides the structured pathway for achieving emissions reduction targets while maintaining business resilience.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across Sustainability Statement pages. Strategy focuses on operational emissions (Scopes 1-2) and includes specific Scope 3 targets for landed properties. Clear metrics and timelines provided with 2024 baseline established. Implementation details include specific technology (eDew system) and building features (EV-ready infrastructure, solar integration). Governance structure well-defined with specific committees and working groups. Biodiversity and sustainable landscaping initiatives are integrated with decarbonization goals.",
      "status": null
    },
