    "targets": {
      "json": "[{\"target_reduction\": \"34% reduction\", \"target_reduction_scope\": \"Total GHG emissions\", \"classification_of_target\": \"Absolute reduction, Science-Based Target (SBTi)\", \"target_year\": \"2025\", \"baseline_year\": \"2019\", \"baseline_value\": \"379,914 tCO2e\"}, {\"target_reduction\": \"45% reduction\", \"target_reduction_scope\": \"Total GHG emissions\", \"classification_of_target\": \"Absolute reduction\", \"target_year\": \"2030\", \"baseline_year\": \"2019\", \"baseline_value\": \"379,914 tCO2e\"}, {\"target_reduction\": \"Net zero\", \"target_reduction_scope\": \"Total GHG emissions\", \"classification_of_target\": \"Net-zero target\", \"target_year\": \"2050\", \"baseline_year\": \"2019\", \"baseline_value\": \"379,914 tCO2e\"}]",
      "notes": "Three sustainability targets extracted from Environmental Management section (page 116). Targets include 2025 interim target (34% reduction) explicitly validated by SBTi guidelines, 2030 medium-term target (45% reduction), and 2050 net-zero target. All targets use 2019 as baseline with 379,914 tCO2e baseline value. Targets cover total GHG emissions (Scope 1, 2, and 3) as indicated by 'GHG Emission (tCO2e)' in Carbon Reduction Roadmap. 2025 target is explicitly labeled as Science-Based Target (SBTi) per text; 2030 and 2050 targets are part of the same roadmap but only 2025 target has explicit SBTi reference. Quantifiable metrics provided for all targets.",
      "status": null
    },
    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Telekom Malaysia's decarbonization strategy centers on a clear net-zero commitment by 2050, with an interim target of 45% carbon reduction by 2030 using 2019 as a baseline. The company has established science-based targets for 2025, aiming for a 34% reduction in emissions, guided by industry standards from the Global Enabling Sustainability Initiative (GeSI), International Telecommunication Union (ITU), and Science Based Targets Initiative (SBTI). TM has refined and expanded its Scope 1 (direct emissions from fuel consumption), Scope 2 (indirect emissions from electricity), and Scope 3 (indirect emissions from waste production) baselines to enhance emissions tracking and reporting accuracy across its operations. The company's approach integrates climate risk assessment into business planning cycles, addressing both physical risks from extreme weather events and transition risks from policy shifts and market dynamics.\n\nSpecific implementation initiatives include increasing renewable energy mix by 20.9% through Green Energy Tariff (GET) subscription, collaborating with GENTARI for solar energy generation at six TM sites, and certifying three data centers with ISO 14001 and ISO 50001 standards. TM is actively decommissioning legacy network elements and migrating to high-efficiency networks to reduce energy consumption while enhancing performance. The company conducted a comprehensive climate scenario analysis in 2022 that assessed 50,587 material assets across Malaysia, identifying high-risk flood areas, and has allocated more than RM490,000 through the BCM program specifically for enhancing climate resilience against climate-related disruptions.\n\nThe strategy is supported by robust governance structures, including Sustainability Working Group 6 (SWG6) under Environmental Management, which drives climate-related initiatives. TM leverages scenario-based assessments to align with global best practices and enhance adaptability, engaging leadership and C-suite executives to assess climate exposure and drive strategic mitigation efforts. The company has also embedded climate considerations into decision-making processes, with climate-related KPIs cascaded across managerial tiers to ensure sustainability performance is integrated into business functions. These integrated approaches ensure that decarbonization efforts are comprehensive and aligned with TM's long-term business strategy while addressing both operational and systemic climate challenges.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 115-119, 49, and 116. Strategy focuses on operational emissions with clear targets (45% by 2030, net zero by 2050) and specific implementation details including renewable energy adoption, emissions baseline refinement, and climate risk management. The company has established concrete initiatives with measurable outcomes and governance structures to support decarbonization efforts.",
      "status": null
    },
