    "strategy": {
      "summary": "United Plantations Berhad (UP) has established a comprehensive decarbonization strategy centered around rigorous measurement and continuous improvement of greenhouse gas emissions throughout its palm oil production lifecycle. The company utilizes Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) as its primary analytical framework, having completed the world's first peer-reviewed LCA study on refined palm oil in 2006 and subsequently finalizing the first comprehensive LCA in accordance with ISO 14040 and 14044 standards in 2008. Since then, UP has maintained annual LCA updates conducted by 2.0-LCA Consultants, with the most recent 2023 update incorporating the EXIOBASE background database and refined assessments of indirect land use change, peat emissions, and nature conservation factors. This systematic approach has enabled UP to achieve a 60% reduction in GHG emissions per metric ton of refined palm oil by 2021, four years ahead of their initial 2025 target, with 2024 emissions at 1.47 kg CO2-eq per kg NBD palm oil compared to 2004 levels.\n\nTo advance their decarbonization journey, UP has set an ambitious new target of 66% GHG emissions reduction by 2030 compared to 2004 levels, incorporating indirect land use change and nature conservation factors. The company is currently pursuing alignment of their GHG calculations with Science Based Target initiative (SBTi) requirements and anticipates achieving SBTi-approved GHG reduction targets before the end of 2025. Their strategy emphasizes investments in green technology as a key contributor to emissions reductions, while maintaining a balanced approach that addresses both agricultural practices and broader operational activities that impact deforestation and global warming. UP's approach demonstrates a commitment to evidence-based decarbonization through continuous measurement, transparent reporting, and progressive target-setting based on their LCA findings.",
      "notes": "Strategy focuses primarily on measurement and target-setting through LCA methodology. The company has achieved early success with their 60% reduction target and has set more ambitious goals. Limited specific implementation details for 2024 are provided, with most emphasis on measurement methodology and targets rather than concrete action plans. Strategy demonstrates strong focus on lifecycle assessment as the foundation for decarbonization efforts.",
      "status": null
    },
