      "summary": "TSH Resources Berhad’s decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on integrating renewable energy, optimizing operational efficiency, and managing emissions across all scopes while strengthening climate resilience. The company prioritizes transitioning from fossil fuels through biomass and biogas initiatives, such as the Bio-Integration Complex in Kunak, Sabah, which operates a 14 MW biomass co-generation plant and a 3 MW biogas plant to convert palm oil mill by-products and methane into renewable electricity. Additionally, TSH connected two Indonesian mills to the PLN national grid to reduce diesel consumption and enhance energy reliability, while expanding renewable energy generation to 296,096 GJ in FY2024—138,345 GJ for internal operations and 154,307 GJ supplied to the national grid. These efforts are complemented by circular waste management practices, with 99.9% of total waste (1,208,490 MT in FY2024) diverted from disposal for energy generation, composting, and repurposing by-products like EFB, PKS, and POME into soil enhancers, biofuels, and biogas. To address broader climate risks, TSH implements land-based initiatives such as agroforestry (planting durian, avocado, and mahogany seedlings) and urban greenery projects (e.g., tree planting at Zoo Negara) to enhance carbon sequestration and ecosystem stability. Supporting this approach, the company actively monitors Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions through comprehensive GHG inventories aligned with the Greenhouse Gas Protocol, and the CASA team drives decarbonization by establishing baselines, setting targets, and conducting climate scenario analyses to ensure operational adaptability and long-term resilience.",
