    "strategy": {
      "summary": "WCT’s 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on integrating climate action into core operations and capital expenditure, leveraging green financing, national policy alignment, and supply chain engagement. The company prioritizes decarbonizing capital expenditure by securing green financing, aligning with Malaysia’s National Construction Policy 2030 through initiatives like implementing Building Information Modelling (BIM) in the Sultan Ismail Petra Airport project, and extending climate focus to suppliers and contractors to embed eco-friendly practices across the value chain. This approach is grounded in recognizing climate change as a top priority, with governance oversight from the Board Risk and Sustainability Committee to ensure strategic alignment and risk management.\\n\\nOperationally, WCT adopts concrete measures to reduce emissions and enhance resilience. The company implements sustainable building materials, energy-efficient lighting, and water-saving fixtures across projects while addressing physical climate risks through targeted action plans. For sea level rise, it evaluates landbanks to strategically dispose of flood-prone properties and integrate nature-based solutions like mangrove and wetland restoration in coastal development. To combat reduced water availability, WCT optimizes water usage via adjusted cleaning practices, landscaping, rainwater harvesting, and recycling, alongside developing advanced water treatment technologies to reduce reliance on freshwater sources. These initiatives are paired with opportunities to expand environmental protection in urban development and supply chain collaboration.\\n\\nSupporting these efforts, WCT strengthens governance through its Board Risk and Sustainability Committee, which oversees climate-related strategy implementation, monitors performance via Quality, Environment, Safety, Security and Health (QESSH) programs, and ensures alignment with international standards like IFRS S2 and the National Sustainability Reporting Framework. Membership in Climate Governance Malaysia further demonstrates commitment to collaborative climate action, while the company’s focus on transitioning to a low-carbon economy drives awareness and eco-friendly integration across consumer and supply chain interactions.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found; Strategy focuses on operational emissions, physical risk mitigation, and value chain engagement; Concrete action plans for sea level rise and water scarcity included; Governance structure and policy alignment detailed",
      "status": null
    },
