    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CIMB's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a comprehensive approach that addresses both its operational emissions and financed emissions across its portfolio. The bank has committed to achieving net zero operational greenhouse gas (GHG) scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2030 and net zero overall GHG emissions by 2050, with Paris-aligned climate targets established at the portfolio level for carbon-intensive sectors. Their strategy integrates climate risk management with business operations, recognizing the need to avoid 'carbon tunnel vision' by considering broader environmental, social, and governance factors alongside carbon reduction.\n\nThe company implemented several concrete initiatives in 2022, including forming a dedicated Climate Risk unit under Group Risk to deepen understanding of climate-related exposures. They reduced scope 1 and 2 emissions by 22% compared to 2019 baseline and implemented an internal carbon pricing mechanism for scope 2 emissions. CIMB completed the financed emissions baseline for nine carbon-intensive sectors, covering 61% of the Group's total gross financing, and expanded PACTA scenario analysis to include cement and steel manufacturing sectors. The bank mobilized RM379 million in new climate supporting financing to help clients decarbonize and build climate resilience, while also committing RM100 million through Bank Negara Malaysia's Low Carbon Transition Facility specifically to assist SMEs in decarbonizing their operations.\n\nTo support implementation, CIMB developed the Green, Social, Sustainable Impact Products and Services (GSSIPS) Framework and rolled out the GSSIPS Tool to business units. They established a structured approach to measuring financed emissions using PCAF methodology and aligned their disclosures with the Financial Stability Board's Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD). The bank also signed a memorandum of understanding with YTL-SV Carbon to develop carbon-related projects and services for clients, demonstrating a strategic partnership approach to decarbonization. These initiatives collectively form a multi-faceted strategy that integrates risk management, client engagement, and internal operational changes to advance the transition to a low-carbon economy.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 10, 22, 32, 48, 52, 54, 55, 58, and 61. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions and financed emissions, with specific implementation details provided. The company demonstrates a structured approach with clear targets, measurement frameworks, and concrete initiatives rather than just high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
