      "summary": "KB Financial Group's 2022 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based, multi-pronged approach through its 'KB Net Zero S.T.A.R.' framework, which establishes concrete targets for internal emissions by 2040 and financed emissions by 2050. The strategy is implemented through three key initiatives: 'KB Green Wave 2030' for ESG finance expansion, 'KB Diversity 2027' for social inclusion, and a comprehensive climate risk management system. The company has positioned itself as a leader in climate action by becoming the first financial institution in Asia and Korea to receive Science-based Target Initiative (SBTI) approval, demonstrating its commitment to aligning with the Paris Agreement.\n\nThe group is executing four specific initiatives to achieve net-zero: supporting SMEs' eco-friendly management through ESG consulting services and preferential financing; expanding green investment in renewable energy and eco-friendly technologies with a target of KRW 25 trillion in environment sector products by 2030; implementing direct GHG reduction through RE100 (converting 100% of business electricity consumption to renewable energy); and managing asset portfolios by regularly monitoring financed emissions. KB Financial Group has also expanded its corporate financing emissions measurement target from KRW 3 billion to KRW 2.5 billion, using the PCAF methodology as the first financial institution in Korea to adopt this standardized approach.\n\nTo support these efforts, KB Financial Group has joined multiple global climate initiatives including the Net-Zero Banking Alliance (NZBA), RE100, Glasgow Financial Alliance for Net Zero (GFANZ), and PCAF. The company has established a comprehensive climate change stress test methodology to assess transition and physical risks, while developing scenario analysis to evaluate the impact of stronger carbon regulations on its portfolio. This integrated approach demonstrates KB Financial Group's commitment to transforming its business model while supporting clients' transition to a net-zero society.",
