    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Hellenic Cables' decarbonization strategy for 2022 is anchored in science-based targets validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), with a clear focus on transitioning to renewable energy and reducing emissions across its value chain. The company has committed to reducing absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 50% by 2030 from a 2020 base year, while simultaneously increasing renewable electricity sourcing from 24% in 2020 to 80% by 2025 and 100% by 2030. To operationalize this transition, Hellenic Cables initiated a significant EUR 80 million investment program over a two-year horizon to address growing demand for offshore cables driven by renewable energy deployment. This program includes a major expansion of their sophisticated subsea cable plant in Corinth, Greece, which will double production capacity and enhance their manufacturing excellence center for a wide range of subsea cables needed in offshore wind and interconnection projects.\n\nThe company is implementing concrete actions to accelerate its energy transition, including securing 100% hydropower electricity through power purchase agreements at their Romanian facility and planning to supply all production with 80% renewable electricity by 2025 and 100% by 2030. Hellenic Cables has also implemented Environmental Management System (ISO 14001:2015) and Energy Management System (ISO 50001:2018) across all business locations to systematically monitor and reduce emissions. These systems support their annual five-year improvement action plan for occupational health and safety, which includes specific measures for emissions reduction.\n\nTo address Scope 3 emissions, the company has developed a 'Responsible sourcing' initiative to identify sustainability risk areas in the supply chain and support improvements in product life cycle journeys. Additionally, Hellenic Cables has commenced processes to assess climate-related risks and opportunities in line with TCFD recommendations, demonstrating a comprehensive approach to managing both transition and physical climate risks. The company's decarbonization strategy is further supported by their digitalization efforts, which enhance data collection and analytics capabilities to monitor emissions and improve energy efficiency across operations.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several images. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) and value chain emissions (Scope 3). Concrete investment program and renewable energy sourcing plans provided with specific timelines. Implementation details include ISO certifications, facility expansions, and specific renewable energy procurement mechanisms. Strategy demonstrates alignment with SBTi and Paris Agreement goals.",
      "status": null
    },
