    "strategy": {
      "summary": "United Tractors' decarbonization strategy for 2022 centers on a comprehensive transition from coal-dependent operations to a balanced portfolio of renewable energy and low-carbon business segments, aligned with Indonesia's energy transition program and their UT 2030 Sustainability Aspirations. The company has stopped expanding its coal-based business, focusing instead on making existing operations more efficient while strategically developing new environmentally friendly energy sectors. This approach is structured around three key pillars: renewable energy development, non-coal mining sector expansion, and cleaner equipment production.\n\nThe company has implemented several concrete initiatives to advance this transition. In the renewable energy sector, they acquired a 31.49% stake in PT Arkora Hydro Tbk, which operates mini-hydro power plants through their subsidiary PT Energi Prima Nusantara (EPN). They also committed to installing 15.77 MWp of rooftop solar PV in 2022, building on their existing 6.2 MWp capacity installed between 2018-2022. Their mini-hydro portfolio includes the operational Kalipulus MHP (0.5 MW) and the Besai Kemu MHP (7 MW), with plans to operate the latter in 2023 and develop additional mini-hydro projects in Sumatra with over 20 MW total potential capacity. Additionally, they implemented a fuel switch from fossil diesel to B30 biodiesel since 2020 and signed a Memorandum of Understanding with PLN for Renewable Energy Certificates.\n\nTo support the energy transition, United Tractors expanded into non-coal mining sectors that supply critical minerals for clean energy technologies. In Q4 2022, they signed agreements for shares in nickel mining companies PT Stargate Pacific Resources and PT Stargate Mineral Asia, recognizing nickel's importance in clean manufacturing technology. The company also developed electricity-powered and hybrid construction and transportation equipment products, including low-emission engines for heavy mining equipment and large-capacity buses, to help customers reduce greenhouse gas emissions. These initiatives form a cohesive strategy to balance their traditional coal business with sustainable growth areas while supporting Indonesia's national energy transition goals.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple pages of the sustainability report. Strategy focuses on operational transition with concrete investments in renewable energy (solar PV, mini-hydro), non-coal mining (nickel), and cleaner equipment production. The company has stopped expanding coal-based business while maintaining existing operations. Strategy aligns with Indonesia's Presidential Regulation No. 112 of 2022 on renewable energy development.",
      "status": null
    },
