    "strategy": {
      "summary": "APP's decarbonization strategy centers on comprehensive emissions management, climate resilience initiatives, and strategic partnerships to reduce its carbon footprint. In 2023, the company implemented a Continuous Emissions Monitoring System (CEMS) to track gas emissions in real-time across its mills, monitoring pollutants including Particulate Matters, Sulfur Oxide, Nitrogen Oxide, Mercury, and Carbon Dioxide. APP has set a concrete target to reduce its carbon footprint by 30% by 2030 and is actively aligning with Indonesia's national goal of achieving Net Zero emissions by 2060. The company successfully achieved compliance with applicable emission regulations in 2023, demonstrating its commitment to environmental compliance.\n\nTo support these goals, APP is implementing multiple specific initiatives: incorporating Spent Desulfurization Tail Gas (SDT) emissions treatment into Recovery Boiler units, optimizing Electrostatic Precipitator (ESP) control devices, and replacing wet scrubbers with more efficient NaOH scrubbers to minimize emissions. The company is also engaged in significant climate resilience efforts through strategic partnerships, including collaboration with Winrock International to manage approximately 4,000 hectares of peatlands in Riau Province, and with PUSTANDPI to study mycorrhizal inoculants for restoring climate-resilient ecosystems. These partnerships aim to accelerate native plant growth and support ecosystem restoration.\n\nAPP is further strengthening its decarbonization approach through participation in the Net Zero Hub program by KADIN (Indonesian Chamber of Commerce and Industry), preparing to submit science-based targets to the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) in 2024. The company is developing carbon-neutral photocopy paper products through its subsidiary Tjiwi Kimia and conducting studies on potential internal carbon insetting. These initiatives are guided by key policies including Environmental Policy, Forest Conservation Policy, and Governance Policy, with regular monitoring and evaluation against pre-defined targets.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several pages. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions reduction with specific implementation details provided. Includes both current actions (CEMS implementation, emissions treatment) and future plans (SBTi targets submission in 2024). Strategy integrates technology, partnerships, and policy frameworks to support decarbonization goals.",
      "status": null
    },
