    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CIMB Niaga's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based, sector-specific approach to reducing greenhouse gas emissions across its financing portfolio while advancing toward net zero emissions (NZE) by 2050. The bank has established concrete 2030 interim targets for four high-emission sectors: reducing thermal coal mining financing to 50% of the 2021 baseline, decreasing cement sector emission intensity by 36% (from 0.72 to 0.46 tonnes CO2e/tonne cement), lowering palm oil portfolio emission intensity by 16% from the 2022 baseline, and achieving a 38% reduction in power sector emission intensity through low-carbon and renewable alternatives. These targets align with the Science-Based Target Initiative (SBTi) and the International Energy Agency's Net Zero Emission 2050 pathway, reflecting the bank's commitment to a just transition while maintaining operational continuity.\n\nTo implement these targets, CIMB Niaga has launched several specific initiatives. The bank is implementing the Net Zero Strategy & Climate Risk Management Project in collaboration with CIMB Group, which includes developing climate scenario analysis (CSA) models and participating in the Financial Services Authority's climate risk stress testing (CRST) pilot project. The bank has established an Integrated & Climate Risk Unit to integrate climate risk aspects into its overall risk management framework and has implemented Internal Carbon Pricing (ICP) to assign monetary value to Scope 2 emissions. Additionally, CIMB Niaga is transitioning to renewable energy through purchasing Renewable Energy Certificates (REC) and installing solar panels at branch offices, while also acquiring carbon units through the Indonesia Carbon Exchange (IDX Carbon) to offset unavoidable emissions.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, the bank has expanded its sector guidance framework to include manufacturing, palm oil, construction & infrastructure, oil & gas, and mining & quarrying sectors, providing a basis for debtors to develop decarbonization plans. The bank has also implemented Sustainability Due Diligence (SDD) in commercial banking and adopted a 'No Deforestation, No Peat, and No Exploitation' (NDPE) commitment for palm oil and forestry sectors. These efforts are integrated into CIMB Niaga's sustainable finance portfolio, which reached Rp55.45 trillion (26% of total financing) in 2023, with specific focus on financing sectors that positively contribute to environmental, social, and governance (ESG) performance.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple images. Strategy focuses primarily on financed emissions reduction through sector-specific targets and sustainable finance products. Implementation details include specific percentages, baselines, and methodologies. Strategy is well-defined with concrete actions rather than just high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
