    "strategy": {
      "summary": "BNI's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a comprehensive approach to reduce greenhouse gas emissions through both operational improvements and financing portfolio transformation. The bank has established concrete targets to achieve Operational Net Zero Emissions by 2028 and Financing Net Zero Emissions by 2060, with a clear roadmap for implementation. BNI's strategy focuses on three main pillars: green portfolio management, climate risk integration, and operational emission reduction. The bank has already exceeded its 2023 green portfolio target of 5.2% with a 13.6% realization, demonstrating strong commitment to financing sustainable projects. BNI has developed a climate-related framework encompassing governance, strategy, risk management, matrix, and targets, with specific initiatives to reduce emissions across its operations and financed activities.\n\nTo advance its decarbonization efforts, BNI is implementing several specific initiatives. The bank launched Sustainability Linked Loans to encourage debtors to implement ESG practices and develop green transition plans. BNI allocated 77.0% of green bond yields to five key sectors, with 61.8% directed to Renewable Energy, 11.2% to Sustainable Transportation, 10.3% to Green Buildings, 15.3% to Waste-to-Energy Management, and 1.4% to Natural Resources Use. The bank also developed a Climate Risk Stress Test (CRST) for high-emission sectors including coal power plants, oil palm plantations, and pulp & paper. BNI has identified 3 GHG emissions from its credit portfolio and is building emission data infrastructure to monitor operational emissions across all offices by the end of 2023.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, BNI established a dedicated ESG Management Department under the Enterprise Management Division in June 2022. The bank has implemented energy-saving measures in its operations, including switching off lights during breaks, using solar energy for emergency exits, optimizing AC usage, and conducting online meetings to reduce emissions. BNI is also strengthening Risk Acceptance Criteria for 18 sectors and has developed a climate-related risk management framework aligned with IFRS S2. These efforts have already shown impact, with green bond disbursements reducing emissions by 233,749 tCO₂eq and producing 54,355.2 MWh of clean energy in 2023.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 24-33. Strategy includes specific targets (Operational NZE by 2028, Financing NZE by 2060), concrete initiatives (Sustainability Linked Loans, green bond allocation), and implementation details (CRST, Risk Acceptance Criteria). The strategy focuses on both operational emissions and financed emissions with clear metrics and sector-specific approaches.",
      "status": null
    },
