    "strategy": {
      "summary": "KB Financial Group's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on its mid- to long-term net-zero implementation strategy 'KB Net Zero S.T.A.R.,' which received Science-based Target Initiative (SBTi) approval—the first among financial institutions in Asia and Korean companies. The strategy is implemented through a structured three-phase roadmap: 2019-2021 for establishing foundational climate risk management, 2022-2024 for advancing climate strategies, and 2025-2030 for securing climate change leadership. The company has also established complementary strategies including 'KB Green Wave 2030' and 'Environmental and Social Risk Management (ESRM)' to create a sustainable low-carbon society. KB Financial Group has committed to expanding its ESG financial products and services with a target of KRW 50 trillion in ESG products, investments, and loans by 2030, building on the KRW 36.4 trillion already achieved as of 2023.\n\nThe company is implementing concrete decarbonization initiatives across multiple fronts. KB Financial Group has developed an Environmental and Social Risk Management (ESRM) Policy Framework at the group level and is reviewing environmental and social risks based on the Equator Principles. They are developing SBTi-based net-zero strategies for both operational emissions (Scope 1&2) and financed emissions (Scope 3, Category 15), and have declared 'Exiting Coal Financing.' The organization is measuring and disclosing GHG emissions while expanding targets for financed emissions, with specific focus on corporate finance, real estate, and other asset classes. Their climate risk management system follows a four-step process: identifying transition and physical climate risks, evaluating financial impacts through scenario analysis, establishing response strategies with GHG reduction targets, and monitoring/reporting results.\n\nKB Financial Group supports its decarbonization strategy through robust governance and strategic partnerships. The Board of Directors serves as the central decision-making body, with dedicated ESG, Audit, and Risk Management Committees. The Group CEO and CSO oversee ESG management while each subsidiary maintains its own ESG council and dedicated organization. The company leverages multiple climate scenario analyses (NGFS, RCP, and SSP scenarios) to assess transition and physical risks across its portfolio. To strengthen implementation, KB Financial Group participates in 17 major ESG initiatives including SBTi (since April 2021), Net-Zero Banking Alliance (since April 2021), RE100 (since September 2021), and GFANZ (since May 2022), demonstrating their commitment to industry-wide climate action standards and collaborative decarbonization efforts.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 31-51. Strategy focuses primarily on financial sector decarbonization through sustainable finance products and climate risk management. The company has implemented a structured roadmap with specific timelines and measurable targets. Strong emphasis on governance structure and scenario analysis for climate risk assessment. The strategy is comprehensive with clear implementation pathways, not just high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
