    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Maybank Indonesia's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on financing the transition to a low-carbon economy through targeted risk management and sustainable financial products. The bank has committed to achieving carbon neutrality by 2030 and net zero carbon emissions by 2050, with a specific focus on mitigating environmental risks in its lending portfolio. Their approach is structured around three pillars of sustainability, with 'Responsible Transition' as the cornerstone, which involves supporting the transition to a low-carbon economy by balancing environmental and social imperatives with stakeholder expectations. The strategy emphasizes developing sustainable products and services, implementing systemic risk management, and integrating ESG factors into financial analysis to guide financing decisions toward environmentally friendly sectors.\n\nTo operationalize this commitment, Maybank Indonesia has implemented the Group Climate Risk Policy (CRP) with five key principles: Orderly Transition Pathway, Operational Efficiency and Flexibility, Sustainable Business Activity, Navigating Complex Regulatory Landscape, and Pursuing Climate Social Justice. The bank conducts Climate Risk Stress Tests (CRST) as part of OJK's pilot project, analyzing three distinct scenarios (Net Zero 2050, Delayed Transition, and Current Policies) to understand climate change risks to financial performance. They've also established specific risk mitigation strategies for environmental risks, including requirements for borrowers to protect High Conservation Value (HCV) areas and High Carbon Stock (HCS) areas, implement 'No Deforestation, No Peat, No Exploitation (NDPE)' policies, and commit to biodiversity protection.\n\nThe bank supports its decarbonization efforts through dedicated governance structures, with the Risk Management Directorate overseeing climate resilience activities. Maybank Indonesia has adopted Maybank Group's sustainability principles at the core of business operations, ensuring credibility as a responsible financial institution. They're raising necessary financing with ESG awareness and developing sustainable financial products and services to support the transition. The bank also engages in community activities like tree planting and eco-village initiatives, though these represent supplementary efforts to their core financing-focused decarbonization strategy. By implementing these measures, Maybank Indonesia aims to balance economic growth with environmental responsibility while managing climate-related financial risks.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several pages (4, 12, 125, 146, 147, 160). Strategy focuses primarily on financing aspects of decarbonization rather than operational emissions. Detailed risk mitigation strategies provided for environmental risks including climate change, deforestation, and biodiversity loss. Implementation details include specific policy frameworks (CRP), stress testing methodologies, and risk mitigation requirements for borrowers. Strategy is comprehensive with clear governance structure and specific actions, not just high-level commitments.",
      "status": null
    },
