    "strategy": {
      "summary": "OCBC's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on a science-based approach to reducing financed emissions across six key high-emission sectors while supporting client transitions through innovative financial solutions. The bank unveiled sector-specific net-zero targets covering Power, Oil & Gas, Real Estate, Steel, Aviation, and Shipping, which collectively represent 42% of their corporate and commercial banking loan portfolio. For these sectors, OCBC established quantitative targets including 55% emissions reduction in Power by 2030 (100% by 2040), 35% reduction in Oil & Gas by 2030 (95% by 2050), and 13% reduction in Steel by 2030 (94% by 2050). Notably, the bank has committed to not extending project financing to upstream oil and gas projects approved after 2021.\n\nTo drive client decarbonization, OCBC introduced the innovative 1.5°C loan product, which offers reduced interest rates to corporates that meet or exceed science-based emissions reduction targets. This was demonstrated through their first 1.5°C net-zero-aligned corporate loan with City Developments Limited (CDL), a three-year GBP 200 million sustainability-linked loan reflecting CDL's commitment to decarbonize by 2030. The bank also developed sector-specific approaches, such as using an Alignment Delta metric for Real Estate to account for the sector's heterogeneity. In 2023, OCBC recorded $56 billion in sustainable finance commitments, surpassing their $50 billion target two years early, with over 100 new sustainable finance transactions totaling $14 billion.\n\nOCBC strengthened its governance structure by establishing the Board Sustainability Committee (BSC) and Sustainability Steering Committee (SSC) in 2023 to provide strategic oversight and ensure effective implementation of sustainability strategy. The bank also expanded its SME Sustainable Finance Framework to Malaysia, Indonesia, and Hong Kong, providing tailored access to sustainable financing. To support SMEs in their decarbonization journey, OCBC partnered with STACS to simplify carbon accounting through the AI-powered ESGpedia platform. Additionally, the bank achieved carbon neutrality for its operational emissions by actively reducing emissions and offsetting residual emissions with carbon credits, while implementing measures such as providing electric vehicle charging facilities at major commercial buildings by 2025.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across sustainability report. Strategy focuses on financed emissions reduction across six key sectors with specific targets. Includes concrete initiatives like the 1.5°C loan product, sector-specific approaches, and governance structures. Implementation details provided with specific client examples and financial metrics. Strategy is comprehensive with both targets and implementation mechanisms.",
      "status": null
    },
