    "strategy": {
      "summary": "SMBC Group's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on a comprehensive transition plan targeting net zero for Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2030 and Scope 3 (portfolio) emissions by 2050. The strategy follows a structured, multi-year approach with clear milestones across all emission scopes, with particular emphasis on supporting customer transitions while transforming the bank's own operations. Key focus areas include phasing out coal financing, setting sector-specific reduction targets for high-emission industries, and significantly scaling sustainable finance to support client decarbonization efforts. The company has systematized its transition plan with specific annual targets and actions, demonstrating a commitment to aligning with the Paris Agreement goals through both operational changes and financial sector leadership.\n\nIn 2023, SMBC implemented several concrete initiatives across emission scopes. For Scope 1 and 2, the company completed switching to renewable power at all buildings in Japan and major group company head offices, while setting new medium-term targets of 40% reduction by FY2025 and 55% reduction by FY2026 compared to FY2021. For Scope 3, SMBC established medium-term reduction targets for power, oil & gas, and coal sectors in 2023, with plans to set targets for steel and automobile sectors, completing the target setting for all nine sectors required by the Net-Zero Banking Alliance (NZBA). The bank is executing a strict phase-out strategy for coal, refusing support for new coal-fired power plants or thermal coal extraction, and working toward zero loan balance as shown in their financial transition graphs. Additionally, SMBC raised its sustainable finance targets from ¥30 trillion to ¥50 trillion for FY2020-FY2029 and launched the Sustana cloud service, which has already been adopted by over 1,000 companies to calculate and reduce greenhouse gas emissions.\n\nTo support implementation, SMBC established robust governance structures including the Sustainability Committee and Sustainability Division, which oversee the bank's decarbonization efforts. The company enhanced its Risk Appetite Framework (RAF) in April 2023 to incorporate climate-related categories and manage emissions by sector in line with the 1.5°C scenario. In May 2023, SMBC released the Transition Finance Playbook, which defines criteria for supporting transition finance in accordance with national/regional policies and international guidelines. The bank also conducts detailed scenario analyses to estimate financial impacts of climate change, using the 1.5°C scenario to identify and manage transition risks across energy, power, automobile, and steel sectors. These mechanisms collectively enable SMBC to balance financial performance with meaningful climate action across its operations and portfolio.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with specific implementation details and timelines. Strategy covers both operational emissions (Scopes 1 & 2) and financed emissions (Scope 3). Comprehensive transition plan with annual milestones from 2021-2050. Specific financial targets and sectoral approaches clearly defined. Strong governance structure established to oversee implementation. Technology solutions like Sustana cloud service developed to support customer decarbonization.",
      "status": null
    },
