    "strategy": {
      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy for 2023 is centered around its Climate Action Plan for all business units through 2030, which serves as the cornerstone of its approach to mitigating climate change effects. The company adopts a holistic strategy that integrates sustainability into business models and decision-making, considering numerous climate-related scenarios including low-carbon pathways. Key focus areas include reducing greenhouse gas emissions through renewable energy adoption, operational efficiency improvements, and implementing circular economy principles across operations. The strategy is guided by a science-based approach using reliable data, with the company identifying key climate-related risks and opportunities to develop coherent strategies and initiatives that address both mitigation and adaptation needs.\n\nSpecific decarbonization initiatives include the operation of two Methane Capture and Bio-CNG Plants that significantly reduced emissions from Palm Oil Mill Effluent (POME), and the replacement of fossil fuels with biogas for electricity generation, transport trucks, and equipment. The company also utilizes byproducts such as palm kernel shells for biomass electricity generation and implements precision farming and smart conservation practices to enhance carbon sequestration. Additional concrete actions include organic fertilizer and herbicide programs, mechanization and automation of processes, preventive maintenance to improve operational efficiency, and sustainable sourcing practices. These initiatives have already contributed to emission reductions in specific operational areas despite an overall 1% increase in total emissions to 62,785 tCO2e in 2023, demonstrating the company's commitment to continuous improvement.\n\nTo support these efforts, the company has established robust governance mechanisms including a Sustainability Advisory Board that guides sustainability strategies and receives quarterly updates on relevant matters. The company implements an Environmental and Social Management System (ESMS) following IFC-PS standards and calculates GHG emissions every three years using the PalmGHG Calculator method approved by RSPO. The company is also working toward 100% RSPO certification across its nucleus palm oil plantations by 2024, which will further support its decarbonization journey through sustainable agricultural practices. The strategy is reinforced by the company's commitment to the 'No Deforestation, No Peat, and No Exploitation (NDPE)' principles, which are embedded in their Group Sustainability Policy and form the foundation for their broader decarbonization approach.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 76-84. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions with specific initiatives for emission reduction. The company provides concrete implementation details rather than just high-level commitments, including specific technologies like Methane Capture and Bio-CNG Plants. The strategy is integrated with broader sustainability principles and governance structures.",
      "status": null
    },
