      "summary": "PT Impack Pratama Industri Tbk's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on three integrated approaches: renewable energy adoption, operational efficiency improvements, and circular economy implementation. The company is actively transitioning to a low-carbon economy through concrete initiatives across its manufacturing operations, with particular emphasis on energy management and emissions reduction. The strategy is structured around specific, measurable actions rather than broad commitments, with clear implementation pathways across different business units.\n\nThe company is implementing several tangible renewable energy initiatives, including the operation of solar panels at Unit 2 Cikarang with a 1,231 kWp capacity, and the installation of solar panels across manufacturing facilities and distribution centers. These efforts contributed to Altira Business Park achieving 'Platinum' certification from the Green Building Council Indonesia (GBCI) in 2023, through specific technologies including Low-Emissivity double glass windows, Variable Refrigerant Flow air conditioning systems, and underground stormwater management. Additionally, Impack is advancing circularity through PT Sirkular Karya Indonesia, which focuses on upcycling recycled plastic waste materials into innovative building materials with high durability.\n\nTo support these initiatives, the company has established a dedicated Risk Management Work Unit (SKMR) to proactively identify and mitigate climate change-related risks. Impack is also implementing a comprehensive energy management system aligned with ISO 14001:2015 standards and has diversified production facilities across provinces and countries with low-risk histories to ensure business continuity during climate disruptions. The company is developing lighter products that use fewer raw materials and is transitioning to low-carbon products and energy sources, while continuously enhancing energy efficiency through state-of-the-art technology applications across all operations.",
