      "summary": "PT Semen Indonesia (Persero) Tbk (SIG) has implemented a focused decarbonization strategy centered on biomass utilization as an alternative fuel source in its cement production process. Over the 2019-2022 period, the company utilized 157,297 tons of agricultural waste including rice husks, corn cobs, and coconut husks, which not only reduced fossil fuel dependency but also created a circular economy for farmers, generating over $2 million in revenue. This biomass initiative represents a concrete operational shift toward lower-carbon production methods within their energy-intensive manufacturing process.\n\nTo support this transition, SIG has implemented technical adaptations to maintain product quality while increasing biomass usage, specifically through adjustments to raw mix design and critical operating parameters (COP). The company is also participating in the Clean Energy Ministerial (CEM), an international forum that unites leading countries and organizations to accelerate clean energy transition. Additionally, SIG has implemented ISO 50001 energy management standards across its operations, providing a structured framework for ongoing energy efficiency improvements.\n\nWhile the company demonstrates practical implementation of biomass utilization and energy management systems, the provided materials focus primarily on operational improvements rather than presenting a comprehensive decarbonization roadmap with specific long-term targets or detailed transition pathways. The strategy appears to prioritize immediate, actionable steps in fuel substitution and process optimization as the foundation of their emissions reduction approach.",
