    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Sinarmas Land Limited's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a comprehensive approach aligned with science-based targets and focused on operational transformation across its portfolio. The company has committed to achieving net zero emissions by 2050 and established a 12-year target to reduce 35% of emissions from energy use in buildings between 2023 and 2034. This strategy is implemented through their ESG Roadmap 2021-2023, which concluded in 2023 with several key milestones including aligning sustainability strategy with global standards like the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, initiating a decarbonization journey through GHG emissions inventory and TCFD disclosure, and creating an efficient internal sustainability reporting system to enhance data collection and validation.\n\nThe company is implementing specific decarbonization initiatives across multiple fronts. For renewable energy adoption, PV systems generated 2,921,756 kWh of electricity in 2023, covering 13% of buildings' energy consumption, while Renewable Energy Certificates (REC) purchases for seven buildings reduced building energy-related GHG emissions by 8.6%. The company is actively electrifying its fleet, introducing 10 electric motorbikes at Kota Deltamas (bringing the total to 20 units) and 12 electric cars for security purposes, with plans to add five more electric motorbikes in 2024. Additionally, they have begun applying REC to mitigate Scope 2 and Scope 3 emissions from buildings and tenant electricity usage, and are studying the feasibility of installing solar panels at the Graha area in KIIC.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a robust governance framework where Strategic Business Units (SBU) and Business Units (BU) hold responsibility for executing ESG initiatives, monitored by SR Champions who verify disclosures and gather insights for enhancement. The company engages an ESG risk rating provider for maturity assessment and has established a comprehensive emission assessment process that now covers all relevant scope 3 emission sources. Through regular climate risk assessments and stakeholder engagement with suppliers and vendors, SML is implementing operational enhancements to reduce emissions while supporting decarbonization efforts across its value chain.",
      "notes": "Strategy details found across multiple pages (10, 20, 42, 45, 46) with specific implementation details and metrics. Strategy focuses on operational emissions with increasing attention to Scope 3. The company has established concrete targets and is implementing specific technologies including solar PV and electric vehicles. Governance structure supports implementation with clear accountability through SR Champions.",
      "status": null
    },
