      "summary": "PT SMI's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on its role as the Energy Transition Mechanism (ETM) Country Platform Manager, appointed by Indonesia's Ministry of Finance in 2022. The company implements a multi-pronged approach focused on accelerating Indonesia's clean energy transition through three core pillars: financing & investment, consulting services, and project development. In 2023, PT SMI executed concrete initiatives including financing 44 new and renewable energy (NRE) projects with a total capacity of 1,438 MW, which have the potential to avoid 6.8 million tons of CO₂e emissions annually. The company signed a Head of Agreement with PLN and a Cooperation Agreement with UNOPS for the Southeast Asia Energy Transition Partnership, launched the SMI Institute to provide research and knowledge sharing, and secured partnerships with the Green Climate Fund (GCF), Islamic Development Bank, and Tony Blair Institute to expand decarbonization efforts. Specific projects included mini-hydro collaborations with MENTARI, solar power assistance programs for public health centers, and a Green Loan agreement with PT PLN to support energy transition. PT SMI also implemented the Organic Waste Management Program using plasma bioconversion technology to optimize waste processing and reduce methane emissions. The company actively participated in international forums including COP28 to share knowledge and best practices while focusing on delivering both environmental benefits and economic value through the ETM, which is projected to generate USD70.9 billion in benefits from 2023 to 2043 while creating new job opportunities in renewable energy sectors.",
