    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Telkom's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a structured Climate Change Strategy framework designed to support Indonesia's Net Zero Emissions (NZE) target by 2060, derived from its 'Right Environmental Approach' ESG pillar. The strategy focuses on two primary operational domains: energy management in data centers and waste reduction initiatives. Key decarbonization actions include implementing energy reduction measures, optimizing energy management in data centers, improving resource efficiency, and expanding renewable energy adoption across operations to directly reduce carbon emissions. This framework operationalizes Telkom's commitment to lowering its environmental footprint beyond the telecommunications sector's typically low-pollution baseline.\n\nThe company is executing specific, measurable waste management initiatives that directly contribute to emission reductions. In the Bresih Program in Tuksongo Village, Central Java, Telkom provides waste management training enabling community members to sort waste independently for processing and banking, collecting an average of 825 kg of waste daily. This effort reduces GHG emissions by approximately 0.24 tons CO₂eq. Complementing this, Telkom's integrated waste management partnership with Tuksongo Village recycled 700 kg of waste into liquid fertilizer, biogas, and magot, achieving the same 0.24 tons CO₂eq emission reduction potential. The company also deployed disposal facilities and waste shredding machines at 14 locations across seven provinces to scale these waste-to-reduction outcomes.\n\nTo support these operational initiatives, Telkom leverages community partnerships and circular economy approaches as core decarbonization mechanisms. The Bresih Program exemplifies this through direct collaboration with local communities to transform waste management practices, while the integrated waste management initiative demonstrates how recycling methods convert waste streams into resources that offset emissions. These community-engaged waste initiatives represent a tangible, localized implementation of Telkom's broader decarbonization framework, translating strategic commitments into measurable emission reductions through practical resource recovery and processing systems.",
      "notes": "Strategy focuses on operational emissions (Scope 1 & 2) through waste management and energy initiatives; community partnerships are key implementation mechanism; specific GHG reduction metrics provided (0.24 tons CO₂eq) but limited details on renewable energy scale or data center specifics; strategy is operational with concrete examples but lacks multi-year roadmap details.",
      "status": null
    },
