      "summary": "Alamtri Resources Indonesia Tbk's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on accelerating the energy transition through concrete operational changes and renewable energy investments. The company has set a target to achieve Net Zero Emissions (NZE) by 2060 or earlier, with specific focus on reducing Scope 1 and Scope 2 GHG emissions through immediate actions. A key component of their strategy involves transitioning to biodiesel blends, having successfully implemented B35 (35% biodiesel) in 2023 which reduced GHG emissions by 34.98% compared to conventional diesel, and preparing for B40 implementation (40% biodiesel) in the near term. The company is also significantly expanding its renewable energy portfolio through strategic solar power installations across operational sites, with existing photovoltaic systems generating 833,728 kWh of electricity in 2024 and avoiding approximately 400 tCO2e of carbon emissions annually. These solar installations include 130 kWp rooftop panels and 468 kWp floating photovoltaic systems at Coal Processing & Barge Loading areas, along with 35 kWp ground-mounted systems at MSW power plant, with additional 165 kWp solar capacity planned for 2025 operations. To support these initiatives, Alamtri has developed a comprehensive GHG emissions reduction strategy that includes exploring carbon sequestration technologies, advancing nature-based solutions, and pursuing other supporting initiatives. The company is also collaborating with the Ministry of Environment and Forestry and the Ministry of Public Works and Housing on the Liang Anggang Nursery Project, which supports environmental rehabilitation efforts and contributes to national climate change mitigation targets, particularly the Forestry and Other Land Use (FOLU) Net Sink 2030 initiative.",
