    "strategy": {
      "summary": "OCBC's 2024 decarbonization strategy centers on a multi-sector approach aligned with the Net-Zero Banking Alliance, focusing on both reducing financed emissions and supporting client transitions. The bank has defined specific targets for six priority sectors comprising over 40% of its corporate and commercial banking loan portfolio: Power, Oil & Gas, Real Estate, Steel, Aviation, and Shipping. Rather than merely setting targets, OCBC is implementing concrete sector-specific initiatives to drive the transition. For Oil & Gas, the bank has committed to not extending project financing to upstream oil and gas projects approved after 2021, while simultaneously supporting carbon capture and storage (CCS) development through financing the Northern Endurance Partnership pipeline and Net Zero Teesside project. In the Real Estate sector, OCBC expanded its SME Energy Assessment (SMEEA) tool to Hong Kong and Malaysia in 2024, providing a free, simple-to-use resource for small property owners to measure and manage energy performance. The bank also executed a $90 million sustainability-linked facility with Kim Seng Heng Engineering & Construction, tied to emissions reduction targets for construction activities.\n\nThe bank is implementing innovative financial solutions across sectors, including the first-in-market Green and Transition Finance Framework for Green Esteel in the Steel sector, which received a Second Party Opinion confirming alignment with international best practices. For aviation, OCBC acted as sole lender for Cathay Pacific's sustainability-linked loan and executed the industry's first sustainability-linked loan (SLL)-based aircraft portfolio financing. Beyond client financing, OCBC is building internal capacity through its Net-Zero Navigator training sessions in Singapore and a comprehensive Net-Zero Capacity Building Framework with three levels: Foundational Knowledge, Sectoral Deep Dives, and Thematic training. These training programs are specifically designed for relationship managers, product partners, and risk managers across Hong Kong, Indonesia, Malaysia, and Singapore, ensuring staff can effectively support client transitions while understanding local market contexts.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across 10 pages with specific 2024 implementation details. Strategy includes concrete sector-specific initiatives with named projects and financial products. Focus is on client transition support through financing and advisory services rather than solely operational emissions reduction. Strategy demonstrates strong integration between governance structure and implementation approaches.",
      "status": null
    },
