      "summary": "PT Bukit Asam Tbk's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a multi-pronged approach that balances continued coal operations with strategic diversification into cleaner energy solutions. The company is implementing concrete initiatives to adapt to the energy transition while maintaining operational relevance. Key focus areas include developing value-added coal derivatives, expanding renewable energy capacity, and optimizing existing operations through digitalization and efficiency improvements.\n\nThe company has launched several specific initiatives to reduce carbon impact. PTBA is conducting a pilot project to convert coal into Artificial Graphite and Anode Sheet for lithium-ion battery production, in collaboration with BRIN. Additionally, they have initiated a Wood Pellet pilot plant in Red Kalimantan, with production scheduled to begin on October 24, 2024. These wood pellets will be used as a coal mixture fuel (co-firing) in coal-fired power plants, reducing overall carbon emissions. The company is also accelerating the development of solar power plants (PLTS), particularly in post-mining areas, to diversify its energy portfolio.\n\nTo support these initiatives, PTBA has integrated its decarbonization efforts into the MIND ID Sustainability Pathway, which provides a structured framework with six pillars including Environment and Climate Change. The company conducts periodic monitoring of strategic policies and implements risk management according to ISO 31000:2018 standards to ensure effective implementation. PTBA is also strengthening operational efficiency through digitalization and optimizing coal transportation systems to reduce emissions during logistics. These concrete actions demonstrate PTBA's commitment to navigating the energy transition while maintaining business sustainability.",
