    "strategy": {
      "summary": "PT TIMAH Tbk's decarbonization strategy centers on implementing a carbon offset roadmap developed since 2023 to achieve Net Zero Emissions (NZE) by 2060. The company's approach specifically focuses on compensating for residual emissions from energy, industrial processes and product use (IPPU), and Forestry and Other Land Use (FOLU) sectors through carbon offset scenarios. This strategic framework aligns with Indonesia's national policies, particularly Minister of Environment and Forestry Regulation (KepmenLHK) 169/2022, which outlines the Operational Plan for Indonesia's FOLU Net Sink 2030 for climate change mitigation and the Indonesia Long-Term Strategy for Low Carbon and Climate Resilience (LTS-LCCR) 2050.\n\nThe company has established concrete emission reduction targets with specific numerical goals. By 2030, PT TIMAH Tbk aims to reduce GHG emissions by up to 102.4 thousand tons CO2e (a 32% reduction from the 2030 baseline) through various scenarios including energy efficiency and alternative fuel adoption. Under the more ambitious NZE3 scenario, where 100% gas is used as an alternative fuel alongside biofuels and biomass, this reduction potential increases to 118.15 thousand tons CO2e (37% reduction). For the longer term, by 2060, emissions are projected to decline to 55.3 thousand tons CO2e under the NZE1 scenario, while the NZE2 scenario envisions using 100% zero-emission electricity from renewable energy sources including nuclear power.\n\nTo support this transition, the company is implementing carbon sequestration measures and conducting analysis of various mitigation action scenarios. The decarbonization roadmap is designed to transform the mining business cycle toward achieving a net-negative emissions target (net sinker). The strategy includes specific initiatives such as utilizing biofuels and biomass as alternative fuels to reduce emissions, with the ultimate goal of enabling the realization of both FOLU Net Sink 2030 and NZE 2060 policy targets within the company's jurisdiction.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with specific emission reduction targets for 2030 and 2060. Strategy focuses on carbon offset scenarios aligned with national policies. Specific numerical targets and alternative fuel initiatives provided. Strategy includes concrete scenarios (NZE1, NZE2, NZE3) with quantifiable reduction potentials.",
      "status": null
    },
