      "summary": "ESSA's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on two concrete initiatives targeting operational emissions reduction. The flagship initiative is the Low-Carbon Ammonia Innovation Project, which aims to capture and store carbon dioxide (CO2) from the ammonia production process at the Pabangai Ammonia Plant. This project has a specific target of capturing approximately 2,547 tons of CO2 per day (0.9 million tons annually), representing approximately 69% of the plant's total CO2 emissions. The project is being implemented in three distinct phases with clear timelines: a completed GHG Measurement Study conducted by JGC Corporation and JOGMEC to ensure carbon footprint alignment with Blue Ammonia standards; a Subsurface Study by LAPI ITB focused on identifying suitable geological formations for CO2 storage (expected completion by February 2025); and a Surface Facility Study, also led by LAPI ITB, involving CO2 injection facility design with target completion by the end of 2024.\n\nAdditionally, ESSA has established a measurable energy efficiency target of achieving a 1% energy conservation reduction over the next five years. To accomplish this, the company implements periodic energy audits, systematic energy conservation programs, adoption of energy-efficient technologies, and integration of Life Cycle Assessment (LCA)-based efficiency calculations. The company recognizes energy management as crucial for reducing operational costs and carbon emissions in the production of LPG, Condensate, and Ammonia. These initiatives demonstrate ESSA's commitment to technological innovation that minimizes environmental impact without compromising productivity, positioning the company as a leader in cleaner energy solutions within Indonesia's ammonia industry.",
