    "strategy": {
      "summary": "ESSA's decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on two primary approaches: implementing carbon capture technology in ammonia production and optimizing energy efficiency across operations. The company has identified energy management as a material topic in its 2024 Sustainability Report, recognizing it as crucial for reducing emissions while maintaining operational competitiveness in LPG, Condensate, and Ammonia production. ESSA's approach integrates regulatory compliance with business resilience, positioning decarbonization as both an environmental necessity and strategic business advantage in the evolving global energy landscape.\n\nThe cornerstone of ESSA's decarbonization efforts is the Low-Carbon Ammonia Innovation Project, which aims to capture and store carbon dioxide from ammonia production. This initiative targets approximately 2,547 tons of CO₂ per day (0.9 million tons annually), representing about 69% of total emissions from the Panggai Ammonia Plant (PAU). The project follows a structured three-phase implementation: the completed GHG Measurement Study by JGC Corporation and JOGMEC; the ongoing Subsurface Study by LAPI ITB (target completion February 2025); and the Surface Facility Study, also led by LAPI ITB, with completion targeted by end of 2024. The project, initiated in 2021, is progressing toward commissioning in Q4 2027 and positions ESSA as a leader in advancing Carbon Capture and Storage technology within Indonesia's ammonia industry.\n\nTo complement its carbon capture initiative, ESSA has committed to a 1% energy conservation reduction over the next five years. The company implements this through periodic energy audits, systematic conservation programs, adoption of energy-efficient technologies, and integration of Life Cycle Assessment (LCA)-based efficiency calculations. This energy efficiency strategy serves as both a risk mitigation approach against energy cost fluctuations and a contributor to environmental sustainability by lowering carbon emissions. ESSA's decarbonization approach demonstrates a practical implementation of sustainability principles, focusing on tangible technological innovation that minimizes environmental impact without compromising productivity.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found with specific decarbonization initiatives. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions through carbon capture in ammonia production and energy efficiency improvements. Implementation details provided for Low-Carbon Ammonia Innovation Project with specific timelines and targets. Energy efficiency program includes measurable target (1% reduction over five years) and concrete implementation methods.",
      "status": null
    },
