    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Kordsa's decarbonization strategy for 2024 is built around science-based targets validated by the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), with a clear pathway toward net-zero greenhouse gas emissions across the entire value chain by 2050. The company has established specific near-term targets to reduce absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by 46.2% by 2030 (from a 2019 base year) and Scope 3 emissions by 25% by 2030 (from a 2021 base year). These targets align with limiting global warming to 1.5°C and form the foundation of their integrated approach that combines operational improvements with strategic innovation. The company has already demonstrated progress, achieving a 21% reduction in Scope 1&2 GHG emissions in 2024 compared to the 2019 base year and a 29.7% reduction in Scope 3 emissions from fuel and energy-related activities compared to the 2021 base year.\n\nTo advance this strategy, Kordsa has implemented concrete initiatives including various emissions reduction projects across all facilities, active research into alternative energy sources for production, and the implementation of circular economy practices. A notable achievement is the successful production of 100% mechanically recycled yarn in Brazil, which optimizes the performance of cord fabrics and yarns in tires while ensuring access to reliable and sustainable raw material sources. The company has also established the Sustainable Advanced Materials Frontier R&D Laboratory in collaboration with TÜBİTAK and opened the Kordsa Advanced Materials Inc. Technical Center in California to design future-ready aerospace and mobility solutions. These facilities support innovation in sustainable materials that directly contribute to emissions reduction.\n\nKordsa's decarbonization efforts are reinforced through robust governance and external validation mechanisms. The company has received an 'A' leadership level rating in the CDP Climate Change Program for 2024, building on their previous 'A-' rating in 2023, and has been listed on the 2024 Global CDP A List for Climate Change. They have also earned the EcoVadis Gold Medal, ranking them in the top 5% of companies in their sector. Additionally, Kordsa has implemented a comprehensive approach to emissions management that includes systematic risk assessment, external assurance for Scope 1, 2, and 3 emission data, and integration of sustainability into their core business model through their 'Sustainability, Innovation, and Digitalization' pillars.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across all provided images. Strategy includes specific targets with base years, implementation details, and validation through recognized frameworks. The company demonstrates concrete progress with measurable reductions already achieved in 2024. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions and value chain (Scope 3) reductions.",
      "status": null
    },
