      "summary": "PT Indonesia Pondasi Raya Tbk's decarbonization strategy centers on reducing operational greenhouse gas emissions through the adoption of biofuel blends in its energy consumption. The company, operating through its Indopora business unit, is implementing Biosolar B20 and B30 as part of its efforts to decrease dependence on fossil fuels and support energy sustainability. This approach represents the primary pathway toward cleaner energy usage within operational activities, with the company positioning fuel blending as a tangible step in reducing GHG emissions generated from operations.\n\nThe specific initiative involves using oil fuels blended with bioenergy derived from organic raw materials to maintain energy availability while contributing to climate change mitigation. By adopting these more eco-friendly fuels, Indopora aims to reduce the negative environmental impact while supporting the transition to clean energy. The company frames this as aligned with its broader commitment to environmentally responsible operations and creating positive impacts on ecosystem sustainability.\n\nWhile the strategy demonstrates a clear direction toward reduced carbon intensity in energy use, it lacks specific targets, implementation timelines, or metrics to measure emission reductions. The company has not disclosed information about renewable energy generation, Scope 3 emissions reduction, or other comprehensive decarbonization approaches that would form a more robust climate strategy. The focus remains primarily on operational (Scope 1) emissions reduction through biofuel blending without detailed implementation plans or broader strategic elements.",
