    "strategy": {
      "summary": "PT TIMAH Tbk's decarbonization strategy centers on implementing a carbon offset scenario to achieve Net Zero Emissions (NZE) by 2060 while aligning with Indonesia's national climate policies. The company has developed a comprehensive decarbonization roadmap since 2023 that specifically targets residual emissions from energy, Industrial Processes and Product Use (IPPU), and Forestry and Other Land Use (FOLU) sectors. This strategy is designed to support Indonesia's FOLU Net Sink 2030 target and NZE 2060 goals as outlined in Minister of Environment and Forestry Regulation (KepmenLHK) 169/2022. The company recognizes that without carbon offset implementation, it would still have significant net emissions (2,704,004.70 tCO2e in 2030 and 1,947,588.61 tCO2e in 2060), making the offset scenario critical to achieving their climate targets.\n\nThe company has identified specific emission reduction potentials through various scenarios. By 2030, PT TIMAH Tbk aims to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by up to 102.4 thousand tons CO2e (32% reduction from baseline) under the ENDC & NZE1, NZE2 scenarios, with potential increasing to 118.15 thousand tons CO2e (37% reduction) under the NZE3 scenario where 100% of gas is used as alternative fuel alongside biofuel and biomass. By 2060, under the NZE1 scenario, emissions are projected to decline to 55.3 thousand tons CO2e, with a complete transition to 100% zero-emission electricity from renewable energy sources. The company is implementing carbon offset initiatives to compensate for residual emissions while simultaneously working toward making its mining business cycle net-negative in the future.\n\nTo support this transition, PT TIMAH Tbk is focusing on specific technological and operational shifts, including the adoption of biofuels and biomass as alternative energy sources, and planning for a complete transition to renewable energy-based electricity by 2060. The company's roadmap is designed to clearly outline how these initiatives will enable the realization of both FOLU Net Sink 2030 and NZE 2060 policies within their jurisdiction. This strategic approach demonstrates the company's commitment to aligning its operations with national climate policies while working toward a net-negative emissions target in the mining sector.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found in sustainability report. Strategy focuses on operational emissions reduction through carbon offset scenario and aligns with Indonesia's national climate policies (FOLU Net Sink 2030 and NZE 2060). Specific reduction targets and scenarios with concrete numbers provided. Implementation details are somewhat limited but specific initiatives like biofuels, biomass, and renewable energy transition are mentioned. The strategy is well-defined with clear timelines (2030 and 2060) and specific emission reduction potentials.",
      "status": null
    },
