      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy is structured around the TCFD framework, with climate risks and opportunities fully integrated into its overall risk management process. The approach centers on evaluating both physical and transition risks as part of the Group's business strategy and risk assessment, with the Board of Directors maintaining oversight responsibility for sustainability matters including climate-related factors. The company recognizes the significant role the real estate industry plays in global carbon emissions and has embedded climate considerations across short, medium, and long-term planning horizons through regular risk reviews and scenario analysis. This strategic approach emphasizes understanding climate impacts on business operations as part of their broader sustainability commitment to reducing environmental impact on the global ecosystem.\n\nThe company currently discloses its Scope 1 and 2 emissions and has established a short-term reduction target, though specific numerical targets are not detailed in the document. A qualitative scenario analysis has been conducted to assess the Group's climate resilience across different time horizons, which informs their risk management approach. The company is also planning to analyze gaps between its current climate-related disclosures and the requirements of the International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB) in FY2025 to enhance its climate reporting framework and align with evolving standards.\n\nSupporting these efforts, the company has established a governance structure where the Board of Directors oversees climate-related matters while the SR Committee (led by the Chief Executive Officer) manages day-to-day execution of policies to address climate risks. Climate-related risks and opportunities are reviewed at least annually as part of the Group's comprehensive risk management process, with specific action plans identified to mitigate identified risks. The company's approach demonstrates a focus on risk integration and reporting frameworks as the foundation for their decarbonization journey.",
