    "strategy": {
      "summary": "United Tractors' decarbonization strategy for 2024 centers on a comprehensive approach that integrates business diversification, renewable energy development, and nature-based solutions. The company is implementing its UT 2030 Sustainability Aspiration, which includes specific targets for greenhouse gas emission reduction and energy management. A key strategic pillar is business portfolio diversification, with the company aiming for non-coal firms to contribute 50% of its total portfolio by 2030. This is being achieved through expanding into gold and nickel segments while developing renewable energy projects including hydro power facilities (PLTA Koro Yaentu at 10 MW, PLTA Kukusan 2 at 5.4 MW, and PLTA Kalipalus at 0.5 MW) and the recent inauguration of an 861 kWp rooftop solar PV system at PT Inti Ganda Perdana's factory in Karawang, West Java.\n\nTo support ecosystem restoration and carbon sequestration, the company has established Nature Based Solutions (NBS) through strategic partnerships. In 2023, they created PT Pertiwi Nusantara Raya (PNR) for forestry management and environmental conservation, followed by the formation of PT Jabar Environmental Solutions (JES) in 2024 with Sumitomo Corporation and Hitachi Zosen Corporation to engage in waste-to-energy power generation. These initiatives are complemented by environmental rehabilitation programs including tree planting at Mount Arjuno, Kota Batu, and East Java, which address forest land functions while contributing to ecosystem restoration and climate change mitigation.\n\nThe company has demonstrated measurable progress in emissions reduction, having successfully reduced emissions by 425,660.07 tons CO2e (11.5% decrease from 2019) and utilizing 22,542.29 GJ of new and renewable energy (31.93% of their total new renewable energy mix). They are implementing climate-related financial disclosures through the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) framework and have integrated climate considerations into their business strategy through the Triple-P Roadmap. The company has also committed to no longer opening new coal mines while working to gradually replace coal as an energy source in alignment with Indonesia's national target of increasing renewable energy capacity to 75 GW by 2030, supporting a just energy transition that maintains economic stability during the decarbonization process.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across several pages of the sustainability report. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions reduction and business model transformation. Specific initiatives with concrete numbers and timelines provided. Strategy integrates business diversification with environmental initiatives. The company has measurable emissions reduction targets and is implementing specific projects to achieve them.",
      "status": null
    },
